CON { stop-state hand test (T0-24, -D T0_STOPMODE only) }

' REBUILT task 3607 (PANEL-CERTIFICATION-EVALUATION.md 2026-09-22, PL-115/PL-116; hold rows added for
' task 3608, DRIVER_REV 8). Eight rows, one wheel. Each row puts the driver in exactly ONE stop or
' hold state and then measures how that state answers a hand on the wheel. The panel names what
' Stephen does BEFORE each row runs (overlay P1), and his button click only sequences the row: every
' verdict below is an instrument reading, never his opinion (overlay P7). The predictions are
' DOCs/plans/STOP-STATE-DESIGN.md SS5 (renumbered here) and DRIVER_REV 8's hold design.
'
' THE OLD "HOLD AT REST" ROW IS RETIRED (arbiter review, same day): since DRIVER_REV 8 the hold at
' rest hands off to the phase short on a 2-tick slip (HS_SLIPPED) BEFORE the driver's own fault
' test (~3 ticks), so its old criterion (turning the hold records a FAULT) would FAIL on correct
' behaviour, and its "fixed cogging resistance" prediction is no longer true -- the hold now grows
' WITH displacement. HOLD-RISE/HOLD-SLIP/HOLD-LIMIT below already prove the hold is powered and
' follows the load; nothing is lost by deleting the superseded mechanism.
'
' ROW IDS ARE SEMANTIC AND FIXED -- they select which art cell and which case-branch a row uses.
' EXECUTION ORDER is a separate sequence (t0sRowOrder, a DAT table): the default order is row-id
' order; -D T0_24_FLT_FIRST (PL-116's discriminator) swaps the two fault rows ahead of the e-stop
' row. T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP is ALWAYS run last in every order, because stop() ends the driver cog.
' The ids are the generator's (task 3619), so t0sScreenTab's row order and these cannot drift apart.
    T0_24_ROW_COUNT     = T0S_ROW_COUNT
    T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE  = T0S_ROW_HOLDRISE                      ' pushed and held displaced: duty should climb to the ceiling
    T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP  = T0S_ROW_HOLDSLIP                      ' a low ceiling: a push should beat it and slip to the short
    T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT = T0S_ROW_HOLDLIMIT                     ' a sustained push at the ceiling: should hand off on the timer
    T0_24_ROW_COAST     = T0S_ROW_COAST                         ' holdAtStop(FALSE) at rest: BR_COAST
    T0_24_ROW_ESTOP     = T0S_ROW_ESTOP                         ' emergencyCutoff() on the coasting wheel at the band: BR_SHORT
    T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST  = T0S_ROW_FLTCOAST                      ' a forced fault under SM_FLOAT: BR_COAST
    T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD   = T0S_ROW_FLTHOLD                       ' a forced fault under SM_BRAKE: BR_SHORT
    T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP   = T0S_ROW_COGSTOP                       ' stop(): the pins released -- the free yardstick, ALWAYS LAST
    T0_24_EV_READ_MAX   = 40                                    ' task 3621: bound on one read of the event log (t0sEvRead())

' THE PANEL AND THE MEASURE COG (task 3619, PL-127; DOCs/plans/T0-24-INTERACTION-DESIGN.md). Every row
' runs INTRO -> SETUP -> ACT -> RESULT. The operator ends every step he takes part in (DONE, or ABORT),
' the program ends only its own (setup, and the two powered fault rows), and a RESULT screen waits for
' NEXT ROW or REDO ROW. Which banner, card, labels and buttons each (row, phase) shows is the generated
' table t0sScreenTab, the same table tools/gen_t0stop_assets.py --storyboard renders for review.
'
' Cog 0 is the panel: it polls PC_MOUSE on every pass, because a click is a LIVE button state
' (p2kbSpin2DbgPcMouse: 0, or -1 while pressed), seen only by a read that lands while it is down.
' Up to SRC_REV 13 the one cog both measured and polled, every 100-150 ms and not at all while the
' wheel turned, and Stephen's clicks on DONE and ABORT went unseen (2026-09-24). The measure cog
' (t0sWorker()) owns the hall poll and every timed act. It prints nothing while it measures: DEBUG
' output is serialised on LOCK[15] (P2-HAZARD-REGISTER DBG-10), so a print could wait out the panel's
' ~30 ms input read and stall the 1 ms hall poll. It buffers its tries and hold samples in hub, and
' cog 0 prints them after the step, outside the measured interval (doctrine D6).
    T0_24_UI_WAIT_MS    = 10                                    ' the panel loop's wait: one PC_MOUSE read every pass, ~30 ms apart
    T0_24_UI_KEY_PASSES = 2                                     ' PC_KEY every second pass (~50-60 ms) -- its own latch holds a key
                                                                 '  ~100 ms, so none falls between reads; a key read twice
                                                                 '  lands inside the next screen's debounce
    T0_24_UI_DEBOUNCE_MS = 300                                  ' after a screen change, input is ignored this long, and a
                                                                 ' button still held from the last screen is no new press
                                                                 ' (t0sReadInput() takes only a 0 -> -1 edge): no double-advance
    T0_24_UI_REDRAW_MS  = 200                                   ' live readings redraw at most 5 times a second
    T0_24_KEY_ENTER     = 13                                    ' duplicates the RIGHT button (the forward action)
    T0_24_KEY_ESC       = 27                                    ' duplicates the LEFT button (ABORT, REDO ROW)
    T0_24_ALLDONE_MS    = 3_000                                 ' the last screen stays this long before the session ends

' PC_MOUSE fills seven consecutive longs, in this order (p2kbSpin2DbgPcMouse, test_bench_dual.spin2
' MOUSE_LONGS): xpos, ypos, wheeldelta, lbutton, mbutton, rbutton, pixel.
    T0_24_MOUSE_LONGS   = 7
    T0_24_MOUSE_XPOS    = 0
    T0_24_MOUSE_YPOS    = 1
    T0_24_MOUSE_LBTN    = 3

' The measure cog's jobs, posted by cog 0 through t0wJob / t0wJobSeq and answered on t0wDoneSeq
    T0_24_JOB_SETUP     = 1                                     ' put the driver in the row's state
    T0_24_JOB_ACT       = 2                                     ' measure the row until DONE / ABORT, or its own end
    T0_24_JOB_TEARDOWN  = 3                                     ' leave the driver ready for the next row or a redo
    T0_24_WORKER_STACK  = 600                                   ' longs: the deepest job is the spin row's episode loop
    T0_24_JOB_POLL_US   = 200                                   ' the idle measure cog's wait between looks at the mailbox

' A spin row's tries, buffered by the measure cog and printed by cog 0 after the step
    T0_24_TRY_MAX       = 16                                    ' tries kept per run of a row; more are counted, not kept
    T0_24_TRY_LONGS     = 11
    T0_24_TRY_HAND      = 0                                     ' hand ticks, up to the release
    T0_24_TRY_SPAN      = 1                                     ' the six-interval span at the release, ms
    T0_24_TRY_AFTER     = 2                                     ' ticks after the release
    T0_24_TRY_AFTER_MS  = 3
    T0_24_TRY_BAND      = 4                                     ' band_ticks
    T0_24_TRY_BAND_MS   = 5
    T0_24_TRY_IN_BAND   = 6
    T0_24_TRY_ENTERED   = 7                                     ' a span reached the band (a coast) rather than stopping inside one
    T0_24_TRY_SHORTED   = 8                                     ' the e-stop row applied emergencyCutoff() at the band
    T0_24_TRY_LATCHED   = 9                                     ' isEmergency() after the try
    T0_24_TRY_MEASURED  = 10                                    ' 1 a reading, 0 not, T0_24_TRY_CUT when DONE / ABORT cut it
    T0_24_TRY_CUT       = 2

' A hold row's 10 ms samples, buffered in a ring by the measure cog and printed by cog 0 after the step
    T0_24_HOLD_RING     = 1_500                                 ' samples kept: the last 15 s of the row; earlier ones are counted as dropped
    T0_24_HOLD_LONGS    = 6                                     ' ms, pos, disp, duty, drv_state, sense_i:
    T0_24_HS_MS         = 0                                     '  one sample's longs, in order
    T0_24_HS_POS        = 1
    T0_24_HS_DISP       = 2
    T0_24_HS_DUTY       = 3
    T0_24_HS_DRV_STATE  = 4
    T0_24_HS_SENSE_I    = 5
    T0_24_SPAN_TO_RATE  = T0_24_TICK_RING * 1_000               ' a six-interval span in ms -> ticks/s

' A hold row's outcome, written by the measure cog into t0wHoldRes[]
    T0_24_HR_LONGS      = 15
    T0_24_HR_DISPLACED  = 0
    T0_24_HR_DISP_MS    = 1
    T0_24_HR_CEIL_MS    = 2
    T0_24_HR_CEIL_I     = 3
    T0_24_HR_SLIP_MS    = 4
    T0_24_HR_LIMIT_MS   = 5
    T0_24_HR_FAULT_MS   = 6
    T0_24_HR_FLT_FIRST  = 7
    T0_24_HR_ABORTED    = 8
    T0_24_HR_PASS       = 9
    T0_24_HR_START_HS   = 10
    T0_24_HR_START_DISP = 11
    T0_24_HR_START_HELD = 12
    T0_24_HR_MAX_DISP   = 13
    T0_24_HR_RISE_MS    = 14                                    ' the rise its displaced rate implies, ms; -1 if never (PL-130)

    T0_24_POLL_MS       = 1                                     ' hall poll period, as T0-12 polls (5 revolutions per second
                                                                 ' before two transitions could fall between polls)
    T0_24_REST_QUIET_MS = 400                                   ' no hall transition for this long = the wheel is at rest
    T0_24_TICK_RING     = 6                                     ' tick timestamps kept: one electrical cycle of hall ticks.
                                                                 ' Every span is read BEFORE the new tick overwrites the
                                                                 ' oldest slot, so it covers SIX intervals, a whole
                                                                 ' commutation cycle, and the hall spacing cannot bias it
                                                                 ' (task 3617: SRC_REV 12's t0sProbe() read after writing,
                                                                 ' and so spanned five)
' PL-115 (rebuilt again after arbiter review): the release is read from the HALL SIGNAL as the
' RATE PEAK, not from a fixed tick-to-tick gap threshold and not from a keypress. See t0sSpinAct()'s
' doc comment for why a fixed gap threshold is wrong -- it lands the release near the END of a
' free coast, not its start.

' THE STOP READING (task 3617, PL-123 item 2): band_ticks, the hall ticks the wheel carries after its rate
' falls to T0_24_BAND_RATE, to rest. The band is fixed and the same on every row, and a coast row's
' release must be above it (in_band), so the reading does not depend on how fast the wheel was spun.
' The band is entered at the first tick after the release whose six-interval span is
' T0_24_BAND_SPAN_MS or more. A wheel that stops within one span of a release above the band never
' shows that span; there the reading is every tick after the release, an upper bound. Only a
' braked wheel does this: a coast carries at least 9 ticks past the band. The limits and their
' derivation are in CON { T0-24 sign-off limits }.
'
' THE E-STOP ROW IS SHORTED BY THE PROGRAM, AT THE BAND (task 3617, arbiter ruling on PL-123). A
' shorted wheel resists a hand far too hard to spin into the band. At pass 2 the hand reached 22.5
' ticks/s (debug_260923-193439.log:2081). So the e-stop row is set up coasting (holdAtStop(FALSE)),
' he spins it hard and lets go, and t0sSpinAct() calls emergencyCutoff() at the band-entry tick, the
' same tick band_ticks counts from. The reading is therefore the SHORT's ticks from 120 ticks/s,
' comparable with every other row. If the e-stop did not short, the wheel coasts on for 9 or more
' ticks and RESTSHORT fails: the negative can still fail. A row where the e-stop was never applied,
' or did not latch, is not a reading of the short. It is not measured. The other brake-state rows
' need no such change: FLTHOLD is driven into the band by the motor itself, and the hold rows are
' pushes judged on the hold's state, not on band_ticks.
    T0_24_BAND_RATE     = 120                                   ' ticks/s: the rate the reading is counted from
    T0_24_BAND_SPAN_MS  = T0_24_TICK_RING * 1_000 / T0_24_BAND_RATE ' 50 ms: six intervals at T0_24_BAND_RATE

' The forced fault (rows FLTCOAST/FLTHOLD, task 3617, PL-123 item 3): drive to speed, then testForceFault()
' under FR_SHIPPED. The driver faults on its next DRIVEN frame, at its own fault test, and takes the stop
' mode's bridge at once: SM_FLOAT coasts, SM_BRAKE shorts. That bridge holds until a stop or a drive is
' commanded (DRIVER_REV 14+). The offset-shift provocation this replaces never faulted in T0-24. At
' Visit 10 pass 2 it plugged the motor into the 10 A abort on both rows (debug_260923-193439.log:2194,
' :2250; PL-119). Same power as the dual harness, so this tier's post-fault readings and its X-2/X-3
' compare.
    T0_24_FLT_POWER     = 50                                    ' driveAtPower(50), the dual harness's FLTAPI_POWER
    T0_24_SPEED_MS      = 4_000                                 ' AT_SPEED bound (the dual harness's STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS)
    T0_24_SETTLE_MS     = 1_000                                 ' at speed before the fault is forced
    T0_24_SAMPLE_MS     = 5                                     ' poll cadence of every bounded wait here
' T0_24_FORCE_WAIT_MS: testForceFault() returns once the front cog has taken the request (one front pass,
'  1 ms). The driver faults on its next driven pass (0.52 ms), and bT0sWaitDriver() reads every
'  T0_24_SAMPLE_MS, so a forced fault shows by the second read, about 7 ms. 15 ms is twice that (the dual
'  harness's FR_PROVOKE_MS rule, where 2 ms reads give 8 ms). No fault by then is a failure of the hook,
'  and the wheel is stopped.
    T0_24_FORCE_WAIT_MS = 15
    T0_24_UNTIL_SPEED   = 0                                     ' the two driver states a powered window ever waits on
    T0_24_UNTIL_FAULT   = 1
    T0_24_REST_WAIT_MS  = 30_000                                ' bound on the post-fault coast to rest
    T0_24_ABORT_AMPS    = 100_000                               ' 10 A in getCurrent()'s 0.1 mA units: the powered window's
                                                                 ' absolute abort, the same ceiling the dual harness aborts on

' Hold rows (task 3608, DRIVER_REV 8): the front cog now follows the load at rest instead of
' holding a fixed duty, and hands off to the phase short on a slip or a sustained push at the
' ceiling. Established-decisions block: HOLD_CEILING_PCT 10, HOLD_RISE_MS 250, HOLD_SLIP_TICKS 2
' (fixed, not settable) are the driver's own provisional defaults; setHoldLimits() lets this
' harness set its own ceiling/rise/limit per row without touching the driver's compiled-in numbers.
' HOLD-RISE and HOLD-LIMIT leave the driver's own default ceiling/rise in force (only HOLD-LIMIT's
' TIME LIMIT is shortened, to make a ~2 s row practical); HOLD-SLIP lowers the ceiling on purpose.
' A hold row has no watch bound (task 3619): it runs until he clicks DONE or ABORT, and the panel says
' when the program has seen what it needs.
    T0_24_HOLD_LOG_MS         = 10                              ' sample cadence (task 3607's hold-row spec)
    T0_24_HOLD_DEFAULT_CEIL_PCT = 10                             ' the driver's own default (established-decisions block)
    T0_24_HOLD_DEFAULT_RISE_MS  = 250
    T0_24_HOLD_DEFAULT_LIMIT_MS = 10_000
    ' PL-130: the hold rises only while the wheel is displaced, so HOLD-RISE judges the rise's own rate, never the
    '  wall time from the first push, which is how firmly he pushed. The rate comes from sample pairs displaced and
    '  under the ceiling at both ends, so no interval's edge enters it: rise_ms = (ceiling - duty_min) x their ms /
    '  their duty gain. DRIVER_REV 17's truncated step made a 250 ms rise take 291 (Visit 10 pass 3); the band
    '  fails that and holds 250.
    T0_24_HOLD_RISE_LO_MS     = 220                              ' DERIVED -- HOLD_RISE_MS (250) less a 10 ms sample either end
    T0_24_HOLD_RISE_HI_MS     = 280                              ' DERIVED -- HOLD_RISE_MS (250) plus it; DRIVER_REV 17's 291 fails
    T0_24_HOLD_SLIP_CEIL_PCT  = 2                                ' HOLD-SLIP: a ceiling low enough a hand push beats it
    T0_24_HOLD_LIMIT_TEST_MS  = 2_000                            ' HOLD-LIMIT: the time limit this row sets and watches for
' Re-arming the hold (task 3617, PL-123 item 1). The front cog arms a new hold only after a pass that sees
' the motor off rest or the stop mode off SM_BRAKE (frontHold()). A stopMotor() at rest is neither, so at
' Visit 10 pass 2 rows 2 and 3 began with row 1's slip still in force (disp_first_ms,0 ... slip_first_ms,0,
' debug_260923-193439.log:1329, :1921). Each hold row therefore selects SM_FLOAT for T0_24_REARM_MS
' first. The front cog runs once per ms, so 20 ms is 20 passes to read HS_OFF. Then SM_BRAKE again arms
' a new hold where the wheel now is. When the stop mode changes at rest, the driver re-seeds the field
' from the halls (restBridge, checkstop, initAngleFmHall). So the re-armed hold does not pull the wheel
' back to row 1's stop angle.
    T0_24_REARM_MS            = 20

CON { T0-24 sign-off limits -- each with its provenance }

' THE READING IS band_ticks: the hall ticks from T0_24_BAND_RATE (120 ticks/s) to rest (task 3617,
' PL-123 item 2). It REPLACES the half-rate time, which depended on the spin. A free wheel slows at a
' nearly constant rate (Coulomb drag), so the time to half its speed grows with the speed. At Visit 10
' pass 2 the half-rate time ranged 100-472 ms across rows (VISIT-10-PASS2-EVALUATION.md SS3.6), and
' FREEREF failed on a healthy wheel. A fixed band removes the spin: the wheel is counted only from 120
' ticks/s down, whatever it was released at. The count scales as 1/deceleration: 120^2 / (2 x decel)
' for a constant-rate coast. A short brakes with a torque that grows with speed, and stops within a
' few ticks.
'
' DERIVED FROM EVERY STOP ON RECORD with a known rate, a tick count and a time to rest. Deceleration is
' r0 / t_rest and r0^2 / (2 x ticks), in ticks/s^2:
'  COAST (BR_COAST):
'   debug_260923-192848.log BM-FRSTAT seq 341   LEFT  X-3  pre_x10 1_064, 312 ms, 14 ticks  ->  341 / 404
'   debug_260923-192848.log BM-FRSTAT seq 880   LEFT  X-3  pre_x10 2_128, 536 ms, 54 ticks  ->  397 / 419
'   debug_260923-192848.log BM-FRSTAT seq 1_434 LEFT  X-3  pre_x10 3_212, 703 ms, 115 ticks ->  457 / 449
'   debug_260923-192848.log BM-FRSTAT seq 3_587 RIGHT X-3  pre_x10 1_064, 183 ms, 12 ticks  ->  581 / 472
'   debug_260923-193439.log:2003  T0-24 row 4 RIGHT at rest, span 54 ms / 5 intervals = 92.6 ticks/s,
'                                  220 ms, 12 ticks                                          ->  421 / 357
'   debug_260923-193439.log:2342  T0-24 row 8 RIGHT pins released, span 21 ms / 5 = 238 ticks/s,
'                                  1_298 ms, 105 ticks (likely undercounted: SRC_REV 12 read input mid-spin) ->  183 / 270
'  The most deceleration on record is 581 ticks/s^2, on the RIGHT wheel, the wheel this tier tests.
'  SHORT (BR_SHORT), ticks from the fault to rest:
'   debug_260923-192848.log BM-FRSTAT seq 559 / 1_098 / 1_693  LEFT  X-2 from 106 / 213 / 321 ticks/s -> 1 / 1 / 3
'   debug_260923-192848.log BM-FRSTAT seq 5_141                RIGHT X-2 from 321 ticks/s          -> 2
'   PL-56 (Visit 2, STOP-STATE-DESIGN.md SS2): emergencyCutoff() stopped a half-speed wheel within 1 tick
'  The most a short carried on record is 3 ticks, from 106 to 321 ticks/s, all above the band.
'  X-2 counts from the fault itself. The fault rows here count from the first 5 ms sample that reads
'  it (bT0sWaitDriver()), about one tick at 220 ticks/s later, so a short reads at most X-2's count.
' PREDICTED band_ticks for a coast: the band is entered when a six-interval span reaches 50 ms. Under a
'  constant deceleration a, a span's mean rate is the rate at its midpoint, 25 ms before the entry
'  tick. So the rate at entry is 120 - 0.025 a, and the ticks to rest are (120 - 0.025 a)^2 / (2 a).
'  At a = 581: 105.5^2 / 1_162 = 9.6, counted as 9. At a = 183: 36. A coast reads 9 to 36 and a short
'  reads 1 to 3. The two limits below sit on either side of a dead band (5-6 ticks), so no reading of
'  one state can pass the other's cell.
' THE BAND IS 120 ticks/s BECAUSE the coast must carry enough ticks to be told from a short. At 100
'  ticks/s the worst coast carries 5.9 ticks (count 5) against a short's 3, with no margin either
'  side. The cost: a spin released below 120 ticks/s (1.3 rev/s) cannot be read. Pass 2's row 4
'  (92.6) would not have been. Such a spin says so on the panel, and he spins again, as often as he
'  likes (task 3619). Row 8 (238) and the driven fault rows clear the band (about 220 ticks/s at power 50,
'  span 22 ms / 5 intervals, debug_260923-193439.log:2195). The e-stop row cannot be spun by hand
'  against the short (pass 2 reached 22.5 ticks/s, :2081). So he spins it FREE, and the program
'  applies emergencyCutoff() at the band entry (T0_24_ROW_ESTOP, t0sSpinAct()).
    SF_COAST_MIN_TICKS  = 7                                     ' DERIVED -- at or above this the wheel coasted: 2 under the
                                                                 ' least coast predicted (9), 4 over the most a short carried (3)
    SF_BRAKE_MAX_TICKS  = 4                                     ' DERIVED -- at or below this the wheel was braked: 1 over the
                                                                 ' most a short carried (3), 5 under the least coast (9)
    SF_MODE_GAP_TICKS   = SF_COAST_MIN_TICKS - SF_BRAKE_MAX_TICKS ' DERIVED -- 3: two rows on opposite sides of the dead band
                                                                 ' differ by at least this. Predicted: at least 9 - 3 = 6
    SF_BAND_TICKS_HI    = 1_000                                 ' no upper criterion: the least deceleration on record (183)
                                                                 ' predicts 36 ticks; 1_000 only fills the record's hi field
    SF_HAND_MIN_TICKS   = 10                                    ' DERIVED -- the row is judged only when the wheel actually
                                                                 ' moved: 10 hall ticks is 40 degrees of wheel, and a
                                                                 ' six-interval span needs seven ticks before a release rate exists

DAT { owning task numbers, printed in each cell's records }

sTaskPromises   BYTE    "3577", 0                               ' the API-promise cells: ACCEL, KMMI, VOLTGET
sTaskCleanup    BYTE    "3574", 0                               ' the bench-cleanup cell: DEADGAP
sTaskStopMode   BYTE    "3578", 0                               ' the stop-state hand-test cells (T0-24)
sTaskHoldRows   BYTE    "3608", 0                               ' the hold-mechanism cells (T0-24 rows 1-3)

sCellHoldRise   BYTE    "R17-T0-HOLDRISE", 0                    ' row 1: a displaced hold rises toward its ceiling
sCellHoldSlip   BYTE    "R17-T0-HOLDSLIP", 0                    ' row 2: a beaten ceiling slips to the phase short
sCellHoldLimit  BYTE    "R17-T0-HOLDLIMIT", 0                   ' row 3: a sustained push at the ceiling times out to the short
sCellRestCoast  BYTE    "R17-T0-RESTCOAST", 0                   ' row 4: holdAtStop(FALSE) at rest really coasts
sCellRestShort  BYTE    "R17-T0-RESTSHORT", 0                   ' row 5: the e-stop brakes -- and so did the old float
sCellStopGap    BYTE    "R17-T0-STOPGAP", 0                     ' rows 4 and 5 are different states, by a margin
sCellFltCoast   BYTE    "R17-T0-FLTCOAST", 0                    ' row: a forced fault under SM_FLOAT coasts
sCellFltShort   BYTE    "R17-T0-FLTSHORT", 0                    ' row: a forced fault under SM_BRAKE brakes
sCellFltGap     BYTE    "R17-T0-FLTGAP", 0                      ' the two fault rows are different states, by a margin
sCellFreeRef    BYTE    "R17-T0-FREEREF", 0                     ' last row: the released pins, this run's free yardstick

sCritHoldRise   BYTE    "RISE_MS_IN_BAND", 0
sCritHoldSlip   BYTE    "SLIPS_WITHIN_2_TICKS", 0
sCritHoldLimit  BYTE    "LIMITS_AFTER_SUSTAINED_PUSH", 0
' task 3617 (PL-123 item 2): the stop cells judge band_ticks, not the half-rate time, so their tokens say so
sCritRestCoast  BYTE    "COAST_BAND_TICKS", 0
sCritRestShort  BYTE    "SHORT_BAND_TICKS", 0
sCritStopGap    BYTE    "COAST_LESS_SHORT_TICKS", 0
sCritFltCoast   BYTE    "FLT_COAST_BAND_AND_FAULTED", 0
sCritFltShort   BYTE    "FLT_SHORT_BAND_AND_FAULTED", 0
sCritFltGap     BYTE    "FLTCOAST_LESS_FLTHOLD_TICKS", 0
sCritFreeRef    BYTE    "FREE_BAND_TICKS", 0

' task 3621 (R20.1): the driver's reporting -- T0-25's cells (-D T0_STOPREASON) and T0-24's event cell (-D T0_STOPMODE)
sTaskReporting  BYTE    "3621", 0
sCellEvHold     BYTE    "R20-T0-EV-HOLD", 0                     ' T0-24 rows 1-3: the hold's hand-offs reported as events
sCritEvHold     BYTE    "EV_MATCHES_HOLD_STATE", 0
sCellSrCmd      BYTE    "R20-T0-SR-COMMANDED", 0                ' T0-25: a stopMotor() reads SR_COMMANDED, and nothing before it
sCellSrLimit    BYTE    "R20-T0-SR-ATLIMIT", 0                  ' ...a time limit reads SR_AT_LIMIT, an earlier stopMotor() not
sCellSrEstop    BYTE    "R20-T0-SR-ESTOP", 0                    ' ...emergencyCutoff() reads SR_EMERGENCY, one at rest changes nothing
sCellSrLink     BYTE    "R20-T0-SR-LINKLOST", 0                 ' ...the command timeout reads SR_LINK_LOST, a refreshed drive not
sCellEvStop     BYTE    "R20-T0-EV-STOP", 0                     ' ...the seven stops as seven EV_STOP, in order
sCellEvLost     BYTE    "R20-T0-EV-LOST", 0                     ' ...a reader 20 behind is told EV_LOST 4 first, then keeps 16
sCellEvTotal    BYTE    "R20-T0-EV-TOTAL", 0                    ' ...getEventTotal() counts the lost ones too
sCellEv2Cog     BYTE    "R20-T0-EV-2COG", 0                     ' ...two reading cogs each read every stop
sCritSrCmd      BYTE    "NONE_OPEN_CMD_STOP", 0
sCritSrLimit    BYTE    "LIMIT_NOT_EARLY_STOP", 0
sCritSrEstop    BYTE    "ESTOP_NOT_AT_REST", 0
sCritSrLink     BYTE    "LOST_NOT_REFRESHED", 0
sCritEvStop     BYTE    "SEVEN_STOPS_IN_ORDER", 0
sCritEvLost     BYTE    "LOST_FIRST_THEN_16", 0
sCritEvTotal    BYTE    "TOTAL_COUNTS_LOST", 0
sCritEv2Cog     BYTE    "EACH_COG_READS_ALL", 0

DAT { T0-12 hand-copy of the driver's hall-position-delta table (PL-39) }

' HAND-MAINTAINED COPY of isp_bldc_motor.spin2:1885-1892 (deltas65), indexed (old<<3 | new) same as
' the driver's own pos_ accumulation (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:2490-2497, "altgb hall_, #deltas /
' getbyte / signx tmpY, #7 / add pos_, tmpY"). This file starts no driver cog, so it decodes the
' sign of the hand turn itself rather than reading the driver's pos. If the library's deltas65
' table ever changes, this copy drifts silently -- there is no shared symbol between a Spin2 DAT
' array here and the PASM DAT the driver copies into its cog image. Read with `SIGNX 7`, matching
' the driver's own `signx tmpY, #7`, since a Spin2 BYTE array read is unsigned 0..255 (Spin2's `~`
' is post-clear, not a sign extend -- p2kbSpin2Operators).

t0hHallDeltas65    BYTE    0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
                    BYTE    0, 0, 0,-1, 0, 1, 0, 0
                    BYTE    0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0,-1, 0
                    BYTE    0, 1,-1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
                    BYTE    0, 0, 0, 0, 0,-1, 1, 0
                    BYTE    0,-1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0
                    BYTE    0, 0, 1, 0,-1, 0, 0, 0
                    BYTE    0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0

CON { sign-off limits (task 3504) -- compiled-in CON limits per cell, each with its provenance;
      full derivations in DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md SS A.4/A.5 }

    SF_ZXS_LO     = 0            ' definitional -- a max - min spread cannot be negative
    SF_ZXS_HI     = 50           ' DERIVED -- SS A.5-e: 2x the predicted post-fix spread (~2.5 mV), in MV_X10

    SF_STOP_LO    = 0
    SF_STOP_HI    = 0            ' DERIVED -- stationary halls never transition (SS A.4 row 3)

    SF_REPEAT_LO  = 0
    SF_REPEAT_HI  = 0            ' DERIVED -- every one of 32 reads on a real board must read REV_B

    SF_TICKS_LO   = 173
    SF_TICKS_HI   = 174          ' DERIVED -- SS A.5-b: 1000 mm x 90 / 518.6 mm = 173.5, truncated or rounded

    SF_COG_LO     = 0
    SF_COG_HI     = 7            ' DERIVED -- start() returns a cog id 0..7 on success (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:86)

    SF_RESTART_LO = 0            ' DERIVED -- PL-24 fix: a second start() must orphan no cog; each start() now costs SF_START_COGS

    SF_EXHAUST_LO = -1           ' DERIVED -- start()'s own -1-on-failure contract (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:86, :121); coginit()'s
                                 ' own observed exhaustion form is $8000_xxxx (:110-112), not -1 -- corrected per PL-44 finding 7

OBJ { objects under test }

#ifdef BENCH_CFG
    user    : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench"                 ' bench compile-time hardware config (-D BENCH_CFG)
#else
    user    : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig"                       ' active compile-time hardware config
#endif
    motor   : "isp_bldc_motor"                                  ' primary instance, T0-1/3/5/6/8/10/11/13/14/15
    motorA  : "isp_bldc_motor"                                  ' second instance, T0-7 overlap probe, T0-14b scratch, T0-16/T0-21/T0-22
    motorB  : "isp_bldc_motor"                                  ' second instance, T0-7 overlap probe only
    motorP  : "isp_bldc_motor"                                  ' T0-17 (PL-48) only: an instance nothing else has touched
    steer   : "isp_steering_2wheel"                             ' T0-18 (never started first) and T0-19 (cog count, R17-T0-VOLTGET)
    benchLog : "isp_bench_log"                                  ' the cog-event quiet window (PL-41, PL-85)

VAR { cog-exhaustion spacer stacks (runExhaustionPhase(): T0-8, T0-15b, T0-22) }

    LONG    spacerStacks[MAX_SPACER_COGS * SPACER_STACK_LONGS]
    LONG    heldSpacerId[MAX_SPACER_COGS]                       ' occupySpacers() / releaseSpacers(): the spacers held across a start

VAR { run state }

' R16-T0-NOABORT: T0-6's two returned codes, judged together with T0-7's in one cell
    LONG    bUnitsCodesOk

' R10-T0-STOPREADY (T0-15d) judges the state T0-15c's own stop() left behind, so it is valid
' only when T0-15c ran to that stop() with both start()s returning a real cog id (0..7). A
' start() that returns -1 also calls stop() (the PL-36 failure branch), which leaves DCS_Unknown
' with no driver ever run -- a PASS read from nothing. T0-15c clears this first and sets it last.
    LONG    bRestartStopValid

' R17-T0-VOLTGET (judged in T0-19, beside the steering object's own reads) compares against the motor object's
' getDriveVoltage(), read by T0-3 while its motor runs. T0-3 clears the flag first and sets it once the read is taken.
    LONG    motorVolt
    LONG    motorMilliVolts
    LONG    bMotorVoltRead

#ifdef T0_STOPMODE
VAR { T0-24 per-row readings (-D T0_STOPMODE only) }

' One row's readings, kept per row because three cells compare two rows with each other. Only
' this build declares them, so the unattended t0 binary carries none of it.
    LONG    t0sHandTicks[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                       ' hall ticks while his hand was on the wheel
    LONG    t0sAfterTicks[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                      ' hall ticks after he let go
    LONG    t0sAfterMs[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                         ' how long those took
    LONG    t0sBandTicks[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                       ' ticks from T0_24_BAND_RATE to rest: the criterion (task 3617)
    LONG    t0sBandMs[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                          ' ms those took (printed, not judged)
    LONG    bT0sInBand[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                         ' TRUE when the release was above T0_24_BAND_RATE
    LONG    bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                    ' TRUE when the row's state was reached AND its release was in band
    LONG    bT0sStillFaulted[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                   ' rows FLTCOAST/FLTHOLD: still FAULTED when the row ended
    LONG    t0sReleaseSpan[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                     ' the six-interval span at the release (a spin) or at speed (a fault row), ms

' The band entry of the coast being measured, shared by t0sSpinAct() and t0sCoastDecay() through
' t0sBandReset(), t0sBandTick() and t0sBandResult(), so every row's reading is one computation.
' Only the measure cog touches them.
    LONG    bT0sBandEntered                                     ' TRUE once a span after the release reached T0_24_BAND_SPAN_MS
    LONG    t0sBandEntryTick                                    ' the tick count at that tick
    LONG    t0sBandEntryMs                                      ' getms() at that tick

' Hold rows (task 3608): one outcome per row, judged directly from the driver's own state
' transitions -- never from how hard or how long he pushed.
    LONG    bT0sHoldRiseMeasured                                ' TRUE when he actually displaced a fresh hold this row
    LONG    bT0sHoldRisePass                                    ' duty rose from duty_min toward the ceiling inside the bound
    LONG    bT0sHoldSlipMeasured
    LONG    bT0sHoldSlipPass                                    ' HS_SLIPPED inside HOLD_SLIP_TICKS, ahead of any fault
    LONG    bT0sHoldLimitMeasured
    LONG    bT0sHoldLimitPass                                   ' HS_LIMITED reached after the sustained push

' R20-T0-EV-HOLD (task 3621): per hold row, its last run's event-log reading after ACT (cog 0 only) beside the
' hold states the measure cog saw in that ACT (t0wHoldRes), so the cell compares two sources of one fact.
    LONG    bT0sEvRan[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                          ' cog 0 read the log after this row's ACT
    LONG    t0sEvSlips[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                         ' EV_HOLD_SLIP events that ACT
    LONG    t0sEvSlipMin[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                       ' ...the least |value| among them, hall ticks
    LONG    t0sEvLimits[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                        ' EV_HOLD_LIMIT events that ACT
    LONG    bT0sEvClean[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                        ' the read ended on EV_NONE with nothing lost
    LONG    bT0sEvSlipSeen[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                     ' the measure cog saw HS_SLIPPED that ACT
    LONG    bT0sEvLimitSeen[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                    ' ...and HS_LIMITED
    LONG    bT0sEvMeasured[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                     ' ...and the row's own cell was a measurement

' The panel's input (cog 0 only): PC_MOUSE's seven longs, one array so they are adjacent by
' construction (DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS7), and the state that turns readings into presses.
    LONG    t0sMouse[T0_24_MOUSE_LONGS]
    LONG    t0sKey                                              ' PC_KEY's reading
    LONG    t0sPrevLbtn                                         ' last pass's left button: a press is its 0 -> -1 edge
    LONG    t0sIgnoreUntilMs                                    ' getms() before which a press belongs to the last screen
    LONG    t0sUiPass                                           ' panel-loop passes, paces PC_KEY

' The measure cog's mailbox. Cog 0 writes the request longs, then t0wJobSeq last; the measure cog
' writes every result long, then t0wDoneSeq last. Each long has one writer.
    LONG    t0wStack[T0_24_WORKER_STACK]
    LONG    t0wJob                                              ' cog 0: T0_24_JOB_*
    LONG    t0wRow                                              ' cog 0: T0_24_ROW_*
    LONG    t0wJobSeq                                           ' cog 0: bumped to post a job
    LONG    t0wTakenSeq                                         ' measure cog: set equal to t0wJobSeq once the job's first phrase is set
    LONG    t0wDoneSeq                                          ' measure cog: set equal to t0wJobSeq when the job is done
    LONG    t0wStopReq                                          ' cog 0: DONE was clicked -- end the measurement
    LONG    t0wAbortReq                                         ' cog 0: ABORT was clicked -- stop the wheel, end the row unmeasured
    LONG    t0wStatus                                           ' measure cog: the live T0S_ST_* phrase
    LONG    t0wRead1                                            ' measure cog: the live readings, -1 when there is none
    LONG    t0wRead2
    LONG    bT0wSetUp                                           ' measure cog: SETUP reached the row's state
    LONG    t0wWhy                                              ' measure cog: the row's RESULT phrase, T0S_ST_*
    LONG    t0wRes1                                             ' measure cog: the RESULT readings, -1 when there is none
    LONG    t0wRes2
    LONG    t0wProtCode                                         ' measure cog: getProtectiveStop() after ACT
' SETUP's re-armed hold (bT0sRearmHold()), printed by cog 0 as the rearm record
    LONG    t0wOffHs
    LONG    t0wHoldHs
    LONG    t0wHoldDisp
    LONG    bT0wFaultSig
    LONG    bT0wHeld
' A powered row's provocation (t0sPowerAct()), printed by cog 0 as the provoke and at_rest records
    LONG    t0wFrErr
    LONG    t0wForceErr
    LONG    bT0wAtSpeed
    LONG    bT0wFaulted
    LONG    bT0wEntered
    LONG    t0wAbortAmps                                        ' the reading that tripped the 10 A abort, 0 when none did
    LONG    t0wDrvState
' A spin row's tries, and a hold row's samples and outcome
    LONG    t0wTries[T0_24_TRY_MAX * T0_24_TRY_LONGS]
    LONG    t0wTryCount                                         ' tries this run, including any beyond T0_24_TRY_MAX
    LONG    t0wHold[T0_24_HOLD_RING * T0_24_HOLD_LONGS]
    LONG    t0wHoldCount                                        ' samples this run, including any the ring dropped
    LONG    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_LONGS]
#endif

#ifdef T0_STOPREASON
VAR { T0-25 helper reader cog (-D T0_STOPREASON only) }

' R20-T0-EV-2COG needs a SECOND cog reading the event log while cog 0 reads it too, because what it certifies -- one
' cursor per reading cog -- cannot show from one cog's reads. The helper only reads and counts; it prints nothing.
' Cog 0 writes bT0rGo; the helper writes every other long, bT0rReady and bT0rDone last. Each long has one writer.
    LONG    t0rStack[T0_25_HELPER_STACK]
    LONG    bT0rReady                                           ' helper: it has read the log to EV_NONE (caught up)
    LONG    bT0rGo                                              ' cog 0: its stops are made; read them now
    LONG    t0rHelperStops                                      ' helper: EV_STOP events it read after bT0rGo
    LONG    t0rHelperReads                                      ' helper: events of any kind it read after bT0rGo
    LONG    bT0rHelperClean                                     ' helper: that read ended on EV_NONE with nothing lost
    LONG    bT0rDone                                            ' helper: the counts above are final
#endif

#ifdef T0_STOPMODE
DAT { T0-24 row execution order (task 3607, PL-116 discriminator) }

' Semantic row ids (T0_24_ROW_*) are fixed; this table is the ONLY thing -D T0_24_FLT_FIRST
' changes. T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP is always last: stop() ends the driver cog, so nothing can run after
' it. Read with t0sRowOrder[seqPos], seqPos 0-based -- a DAT LONG array indexes directly, same as
' t0hHallDeltas65 above.
#ifdef T0_24_FLT_FIRST
t0sRowOrder     LONG    T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE, T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP, T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT, T0_24_ROW_COAST, T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST, T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD, T0_24_ROW_ESTOP, T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP
#else
t0sRowOrder     LONG    T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE, T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP, T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT, T0_24_ROW_COAST, T0_24_ROW_ESTOP, T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST, T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD, T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP
#endif

DAT { T0-24 screen table -- GENERATED by tools/gen_t0stop_assets.py, do not hand-edit }

' One entry per (row, phase), row-major in T0_24_ROW_* order then PH_* order. Each entry is
' T0S_SCREEN_BYTES bytes (T0S_SCR_*): banner, card, reading label 1, reading label 2, left button,
' right button, and the phrase the screen opens with (blank where cog 0 supplies its own).
' The generator's --storyboard renders these same entries, so the reviewed screens are these.
t0sScreenTab
    BYTE     0,  0,  0,  0,  0,  1,  0   ' HOLDRISE PH_INTRO
    BYTE     1,  0,  0,  0,  5,  0,  2   ' HOLDRISE PH_SETUP
    BYTE     2,  1,  1,  2,  5,  2,  7   ' HOLDRISE PH_ACT
    BYTE     4,  2,  3,  2,  6,  3,  0   ' HOLDRISE PH_RESULT
    BYTE     0,  3,  0,  0,  0,  1,  0   ' HOLDSLIP PH_INTRO
    BYTE     1,  3,  0,  0,  5,  0,  3   ' HOLDSLIP PH_SETUP
    BYTE     2,  4,  1,  2,  5,  2,  7   ' HOLDSLIP PH_ACT
    BYTE     4,  5,  4,  2,  6,  3,  0   ' HOLDSLIP PH_RESULT
    BYTE     0,  6,  0,  0,  0,  1,  0   ' HOLDLIMIT PH_INTRO
    BYTE     1,  6,  0,  0,  5,  0,  2   ' HOLDLIMIT PH_SETUP
    BYTE     2,  7,  1,  2,  5,  2,  7   ' HOLDLIMIT PH_ACT
    BYTE     4,  8,  5,  2,  6,  3,  0   ' HOLDLIMIT PH_RESULT
    BYTE     0,  9,  0,  0,  0,  1,  0   ' COAST PH_INTRO
    BYTE     1,  9,  0,  0,  5,  0,  4   ' COAST PH_SETUP
    BYTE     2, 10,  6,  7,  5,  2, 17   ' COAST PH_ACT
    BYTE     4, 11,  8,  9,  6,  3,  0   ' COAST PH_RESULT
    BYTE     0, 12,  0,  0,  0,  1,  0   ' ESTOP PH_INTRO
    BYTE     1, 12,  0,  0,  5,  0,  4   ' ESTOP PH_SETUP
    BYTE     2, 13,  6,  7,  5,  2, 17   ' ESTOP PH_ACT
    BYTE     4, 14,  8,  9,  6,  3,  0   ' ESTOP PH_RESULT
    BYTE     0, 15,  0,  0,  0,  1,  0   ' FLTCOAST PH_INTRO
    BYTE     1, 15,  0,  0,  5,  0,  6   ' FLTCOAST PH_SETUP
    BYTE     3, 16,  6,  7,  5,  0, 26   ' FLTCOAST PH_ACT
    BYTE     4, 17,  8,  9,  6,  3,  0   ' FLTCOAST PH_RESULT
    BYTE     0, 18,  0,  0,  0,  1,  0   ' FLTHOLD PH_INTRO
    BYTE     1, 18,  0,  0,  5,  0,  6   ' FLTHOLD PH_SETUP
    BYTE     3, 19,  6,  7,  5,  0, 26   ' FLTHOLD PH_ACT
    BYTE     4, 20,  8,  9,  6,  3,  0   ' FLTHOLD PH_RESULT
    BYTE     0, 21,  0,  0,  0,  1,  0   ' COGSTOP PH_INTRO
    BYTE     1, 21,  0,  0,  0,  0,  5   ' COGSTOP PH_SETUP
    BYTE     2, 22,  6,  7,  5,  2, 17   ' COGSTOP PH_ACT
    BYTE     4, 23,  8,  9,  6,  4,  0   ' COGSTOP PH_RESULT

' The panel tests (PL-135): T0S_TEST_COUNT entries of T0S_TEST_BYTES bytes -- the row and phase
' (T0S_TEST_ROW, T0S_TEST_PHASE), then a screen entry laid out as above (from T0S_TEST_SCREEN).
' A row's first run shows this screen in place of its (row, phase) entry in t0sScreenTab.
t0sTestTab
    BYTE     0,  0,  7, 26, 10,  0,  0,  0,  0   ' HOLDRISE PH_INTRO panel test
    BYTE     3,  3,  8, 27,  8,  9,  6,  0,  0   ' COAST PH_RESULT panel test
    BYTE     5,  2,  3, 28,  6,  7,  5,  0, 26   ' FLTCOAST PH_ACT panel test
    BYTE     5,  3,  8, 29,  8,  9,  6,  0,  0   ' FLTCOAST PH_RESULT panel test
#endif

PUB main() | trapCode
'' Run every Tier 0 test in sequence and tag its result on the debug stream. Exactly ONE
'' top-level trap covers the whole run (task 3539, PL-44/PL-47): main() calls \runTier0Tests()
'' and prints trapCode on EVERY run, not only when something aborted (P3), so a genuine abort
'' this file did not anticipate is visible instead of silently ending the session. Individual
'' tests are no longer separately \-trapped -- that was a trap nested inside this one's frame,
'' PL-44's H7 suspect -- and normal library calls inside them are made untrapped and judged by
'' their returned value. The very last thing printed, alone on its own line with nothing else in
'' that debug() call, is the literal text DEBUG_END_SESSION -- tools/bench-run.sh runs
'' pnut-term-ts with --exit-on-end-session, and that phrase is its end-of-session marker.
'' Emitting it here, only after DONE, lets that batch mode close the terminal itself once the
'' suite has genuinely finished, instead of waiting on an operator keypress or a fixed timeout.
'' No other debug() output anywhere in this harness may contain this phrase, or the session
'' would end early.
''

' @local trapCode - the top-level trap's value: 0 on a normal return from runTier0Tests()
'                    (it returns nothing meaningful), or the abort value if something aborted

#ifdef T0_STOPMODE
    ' T0-24 is the one build of this harness that drives the motor: the FLTCOAST/FLTHOLD rows provoke a fault at
    '  T0_24_FLT_POWER. The banner says so, because "no motion" in a log this build wrote would be
    '  a false description of what the operator was standing next to.
    debug("* test_bench_t0 -- T0-24 stop-state hand test: ATTENDED, THE WHEEL SPINS ON TWO ROWS -- src_rev ", udec_(SRC_REV))
#elseifdef T0_STOPREASON
    ' T0-25 drives the RIGHT wheel on every leg, so its banner says so, as T0-24's does
    debug("* test_bench_t0 -- T0-25 stop reasons and event log: UNATTENDED, THE RIGHT WHEEL IS DRIVEN -- src_rev ", udec_(SRC_REV))
#else
    debug("* test_bench_t0 -- Tier 0: no motion -- src_rev ", udec_(SRC_REV))
#endif
    debug("* active config: motor_type_enum=", udec_(user.MOTOR_TYPE), " base=", udec_(T0_MOTOR_BASE), " voltage_enum=", udec_(user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE), " wheel_dia_x10=", udec_(round(user.WHEEL_DIA_IN_INCH *. 10.0)))
    debug("* bench expects MOTOR_TYPE=MOTR_6_5_INCH (0) and wheel_dia_x10=65; with wheel_dia_x10=0 the T0-3/T0-6 distance conversions report unavailable rather than a tick count")

    trapCode := \runTier0Tests()
    debug("T0-TRAP,code,", sdec_(trapCode))                  ' P3: printed every run, not only on abort

    debug("* test_bench_t0 -- DONE")
    debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")

PRI runTier0Tests()
' The single top-level trap's body (called only as \runTier0Tests() from main()). No call in
' here is itself \-trapped except T0-6's and T0-7's own deliberate abort probes -- see their
' comments -- so this is the only trap frame any of them can nest inside.
'

#ifdef T0_HAND
    ' T0_HAND build (bench-run.sh t0-hand): T0-12 only. It is an operator-attended reference
    ' measurement with no sign-off cell, so this build runs none of the unattended tests and
    ' declares no cells -- its log can never be mistaken for an unattended Tier 0 run.
    testT0_12()
#elseifdef T0_STOPMODE
    ' T0_STOPMODE build (bench-run.sh t0-stopmode): T0-24 only, for the same reason -- it waits on
    ' a person at every row, and on two rows it drives the motor. Its cells are its own.
    testT0_24()
#elseifdef T0_STOPREASON
    ' T0_STOPREASON build (bench-run.sh t0-stopreason, task 3621): T0-25 only. Unattended, but it drives the RIGHT
    ' wheel, which plain t0 promises never to do (DRIVER-REPORTING-DESIGN.md SS6, the t0-stopmode precedent).
    testT0_25()
#else
    ' Sign-off declarations (design rule 3, SS 0): one per cell this binary will judge, emitted
    ' before anything starts a cog. Row 8 (R8-T0-ZXS) covers all four channel variants (ZXS_I/
    ' U/V/W) under a single declared cell, per design SS A.2's "feature row is the set of cells
    ' sharing row" -- the manifest joins on the cell id, not the per-channel crit token.
    emitCellDecl(@"R8-T0-ZXS", @"3529")
    emitCellDecl(@"R3-T0-STOPPED", @"3501")
    emitCellDecl(@"R2-T0-REPEAT", @"3500")
    emitCellDecl(@"R2-T0-DIRTY", @"3500")
    emitCellDecl(@"R2-T0-EMPTY", @"3500")
    emitCellDecl(@"R4-T0-1M-TICKS", @"3502")
    emitCellDecl(@"R1-T0-START", @"3499")
    emitCellDecl(@"R1-T0-RESTART", @"3499")
    emitCellDecl(@"R10-T0-STOPREADY", @"3533")
    emitCellDecl(@"R1-T0-EXHAUST", @"3499")
    emitCellDecl(@"R16-T0-LIMKEEP", @"3554")
    emitCellDecl(@"R16-T0-NOABORT", @"3554")
    emitCellDecl(@"R16-T0-BADGROUP", @"3554")
    emitCellDecl(@"R16-T0-PINSKEEP", @"3554")
    emitCellDecl(@"R16-T0-STRNOTSTART", @"3555")
    emitCellDecl(@"R16-T0-STEERCOGS", @"3513")
    emitCellDecl(@"R16-T0-RESTZERO", @"3556")
    emitCellDecl(@"R16-T0-NOBOARD", @"3556")
    emitCellDecl(@"R16-T0-FRONTFAIL", @"3513")
    emitCellDecl(@"R17-T0-NOBOARDSTART", @"3570")
    emitCellDecl(@"R17-T0-DEADGAP", @sTaskCleanup)
    emitCellDecl(@"R17-T0-ACCEL", @sTaskPromises)
    emitCellDecl(@"R17-T0-KMMI", @sTaskPromises)
    emitCellDecl(@"R17-T0-VOLTGET", @sTaskPromises)

    testT0_1()
    testT0_3()
    testT0_5()
    testT0_6()
    testT0_7()

    ' T0-18 before anything starts the steering object: it judges a never-started instance
    testT0_18()

    ' T0-11 and T0-13 run BEFORE T0-10 (design SS H.1 order rule): both are real start()/stop()
    ' cycles on `motor`, and running them before T0-10's own start()/stop() (and well before
    ' T0-8's destructive cog exhaustion) keeps every one of their five/one start()s clean.
    testT0_11()
    testT0_13()

    ' T0-14 (board-detection sweeps) also belongs on the non-destructive side of T0-8, and after
    ' T0-7 so it can release T0-7's motorA/motorB pin claims itself (each sub-test does so).
    testT0_14a()
    testT0_14b()
    testT0_14c()

    ' T0-15a/c/d (start/restart/stopready) are non-destructive cog accounting; T0-15b
    ' (exhaustion) is deliberately last, after T0-8's slot (see T0-8's own comment).
    testT0_15a()
    testT0_15c()
    testT0_15d()

    ' T0-16..T0-23 (task 3560): the 6.0.0 start, pin, steering, current-sense and no-board cells. Each
    ' releases every claim and cog it takes. T0-22 (front-cog failure) runs in the exhaustion phase below.
    testT0_16()
    testT0_17()
    testT0_19()
    testT0_20()
    testT0_21()
    testT0_23()

    ' T0-10 runs BEFORE the exhaustion phase deliberately. Both drive the same motor object,
    ' and the phase is destructive: it occupies every spare cog so that start() must fail,
    ' which leaves the object half-initialised. Run in the other order, T0-10's own start()
    ' then returns 0 and its ADC reading is never taken -- observed in the 2026-09-10 bench
    ' run. Destructive tests go last.
    testT0_10()

    ' The cog-exhaustion cells T0-8, R1-T0-EXHAUST (T0-15b, design SS H.1: never leaves fewer free
    ' cogs than it found) and R16-T0-FRONTFAIL (T0-22) run last, sharing ONE occupancy (PL-85).
    runExhaustionPhase()
#endif

#ifndef T0_OWN_TIER
' Unattended test bodies -- compiled out of every build that runs one test of its own (T0_OWN_TIER, top of
' file). The three helpers those tests share, bWaitReady(), emitCellDecl() and emitCellBool(), sit between
' the gated ranges.
PRI testT0_1() | deadGap, minGap, bPass
' A1 / R17-T0-DEADGAP (task 3574): the whole of init() runs through testSetup() and the commutation dead gap it
' derives is at least DEADTIME_MIN_NS at this clock. Both Parallax 64010 manuals specify a 250 ns minimum on
' either board revision (A1, PL-9); the library now uses 260 ns everywhere. UNFIXED: Rev B got 52 ns -- 14
' ticks at 270 MHz against the 68 this requires -- so the cell FAILs. testSetup() is called UNTRAPPED (task
' 3539): a genuine abort from a bad voltage/motor pairing is caught by main()'s single top-level trap. The
' values T0-1 used to print beside it (the other drive constants, the sense resistor, the board string) fed no
' cell and no open finding, so they are retired (task 3574).
'
' @local deadGap - dead_gap from testGetDriveConstants(), in system ticks
' @local minGap - the fewest ticks that are DEADTIME_MIN_NS at CLKFREQ, rounded up
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    motor.testSetup(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    deadGap, _, _, _, _, _ := motor.testGetDriveConstants()
    ' ticks per us x ns / 1000, rounded up. CLKFREQ / HZ_PER_MHZ truncates on a clock that is not a whole
    ' number of MHz; every clock this file is built at is (270 MHz here, 200/270/300 on the clock loads).
    minGap := ((CLKFREQ / HZ_PER_MHZ) * DEADTIME_MIN_NS + NS_PER_US - 1) / NS_PER_US
    bPass := (deadGap >= minGap)
    debug("T0-1,dead_gap,", udec_(deadGap), ",min_ticks,", udec_(minGap), ",clkfreq,", udec_(CLKFREQ))
    emitCellBool(@"R17-T0-DEADGAP", @sTaskCleanup, @"RIGHT", @"DEADTIME_250NS_MIN", TRUE, bPass, DEADGAP_READS_JUDGED)

PRI testT0_3() | startResult, bReady, eM, eCm, eMm, ticksM, ticksCm, ticksMm, bAgree, bTicksInBand, bPass, eRot, keptRot, eDist, keptDist, eTime, keptTime, bKeep, bKmMiOk
' F: stopAfterDistance() computes its tick target in three equivalent ways --
' 1 DDU_M, 100 DDU_CM, 1000 DDU_MM -- and stores it in the private VAR
' motorStopHallTicks, read back here via the testGetStopHallTicks() getter.
' All three should agree; DDU_M coming out a factor of ten short of the other
' two CONFIRMS finding F. Since the error contract (task 3554, F-5) a stop
' limit is accepted only by a started motor -- an unstarted one returns
' ERR_NOT_STARTED and arms nothing -- so the motor is started at zero command
' first. The limit is armed at rest and never crossed, so nothing turns.
'
' task 3504 / R4-T0-1M-TICKS: a BOOL cell (task 3537). measured is TRUE only when
' every call returned NO_ERROR, the DDU_M reading (ticksM) is in SF_TICKS_LO..
' SF_TICKS_HI (SS A.5-b) AND the three units agree.
'
' task 3554 / R16-T0-LIMKEEP (F-4): with the 1000 mm limit armed, three rejected
' calls -- stopAfterRotation(1, 99), stopAfterDistance(1, 99), stopAfterTime(0,
' DTU_SEC) -- must each return their code (ERR_BAD_UNITS, ERR_BAD_UNITS,
' ERR_BAD_COUNT) and leave the armed limit as it was. UNFIXED: stopAfterRotation()
' zeroed the armed limit before validating, and an illegal unit aborted.
'
' task 3577 / R17-T0-KMMI (K), on the same running motor after LIMKEEP: see bUnitsKmMiOk().
' The motor's getDriveVoltage() is read here too, for T0-19's R17-T0-VOLTGET.
' All three cells are NOMEAS when the start did not reach ready.
'
' @local startResult - start()'s return
' @local bReady - TRUE when the driver reported ready within READY_WAIT_MS
' @local eM - stopAfterDistance(1, DDU_M)'s status
' @local eCm - stopAfterDistance(100, DDU_CM)'s status
' @local eMm - stopAfterDistance(1000, DDU_MM)'s status
' @local ticksM - motorStopHallTicks after stopAfterDistance(1, DDU_M)
' @local ticksCm - motorStopHallTicks after stopAfterDistance(100, DDU_CM)
' @local ticksMm - motorStopHallTicks after stopAfterDistance(1000, DDU_MM)
' @local bAgree - TRUE when all three tick readings match (PL-23: printed as TRUE/FALSE)
' @local bTicksInBand - TRUE when ticksM falls in SF_TICKS_LO..SF_TICKS_HI
' @local bPass - R4-T0-1M-TICKS's measured value and verdict
' @local eRot - stopAfterRotation(1, 99)'s status
' @local keptRot - the armed limit after it
' @local eDist - stopAfterDistance(1, 99)'s status
' @local keptDist - the armed limit after it
' @local eTime - stopAfterTime(0, DTU_SEC)'s status
' @local keptTime - the armed limit after it
' @local bKeep - R16-T0-LIMKEEP's measured value and verdict
' @local bKmMiOk - R17-T0-KMMI's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-3,begin")
    bMotorVoltRead := FALSE
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    bReady := bWaitReady(startResult)
    debug("T0-3,start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",ready,", zstr_(bReady ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

    if bReady
        eM := motor.stopAfterDistance(1, motor.DDU_M)
        ticksM := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
        debug("T0-3,ddu_m,1,status,", sdec_(eM), ",ticks,", udec_(ticksM))

        eCm := motor.stopAfterDistance(100, motor.DDU_CM)
        ticksCm := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
        debug("T0-3,ddu_cm,100,status,", sdec_(eCm), ",ticks,", udec_(ticksCm))

        eMm := motor.stopAfterDistance(1000, motor.DDU_MM)
        ticksMm := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
        debug("T0-3,ddu_mm,1000,status,", sdec_(eMm), ",ticks,", udec_(ticksMm))

        bAgree := (ticksM == ticksCm) and (ticksCm == ticksMm)
        debug("T0-3,end,agree,", zstr_(bAgree ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

        bTicksInBand := (ticksM >= SF_TICKS_LO) and (ticksM <= SF_TICKS_HI)
        bPass := bAgree and bTicksInBand and (eM == motor.NO_ERROR) and (eCm == motor.NO_ERROR) and (eMm == motor.NO_ERROR)
        emitCellBool(@"R4-T0-1M-TICKS", @"3502", @"NONE", @"DDU_M_TICKS", TRUE, bPass, 1)

        eRot := motor.stopAfterRotation(1, 99)
        keptRot := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
        eDist := motor.stopAfterDistance(1, 99)
        keptDist := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
        eTime := motor.stopAfterTime(0, motor.DTU_SEC)
        keptTime := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
        bKeep := (eRot == motor.ERR_BAD_UNITS) and (eDist == motor.ERR_BAD_UNITS) and (eTime == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT)
        bKeep := bKeep and (ticksMm <> 0) and (keptRot == ticksMm) and (keptDist == ticksMm) and (keptTime == ticksMm)
        debug("T0-3,limkeep,armed,", udec_(ticksMm), ",rot_status,", sdec_(eRot), ",kept,", udec_(keptRot), ",dist_status,", sdec_(eDist), ",kept,", udec_(keptDist), ",time_status,", sdec_(eTime), ",kept,", udec_(keptTime))
        emitCellBool(@"R16-T0-LIMKEEP", @"3554", @"RIGHT", @"REJECT_KEEPS_LIMIT", TRUE, bKeep, 3)

        bKmMiOk := bUnitsKmMiOk()
        emitCellBool(@"R17-T0-KMMI", @sTaskPromises, @"RIGHT", @"KM_MI_EXACT_CMD", TRUE, bKmMiOk, KMMI_CLAIMS_JUDGED)
        motorVolt, motorMilliVolts := motor.getDriveVoltage()
        bMotorVoltRead := TRUE
    else
        emitCellBool(@"R4-T0-1M-TICKS", @"3502", @"NONE", @"DDU_M_TICKS", FALSE, FALSE, 1)
        emitCellBool(@"R16-T0-LIMKEEP", @"3554", @"RIGHT", @"REJECT_KEEPS_LIMIT", FALSE, FALSE, 3)
        emitCellBool(@"R17-T0-KMMI", @sTaskPromises, @"RIGHT", @"KM_MI_EXACT_CMD", FALSE, FALSE, KMMI_CLAIMS_JUDGED)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()
    motor.getError()                                        ' drain this cog's first recorded code, so a later cell reads only its own
#endif

PRI bWaitReady(startResult) : bReady | readyMs
' Wait, bounded by READY_WAIT_MS, for `motor` to report ready after a start() that returned a cog id.
'
' @param startResult - the start()'s return; a failed start (< 0) is never ready
' @returns bReady - TRUE when start() returned a cog id and the driver reported ready in the bound
' @local readyMs - ready-wait accumulator

    bReady := FALSE
    if startResult >= 0
        readyMs := 0
        repeat while (motor.isReady() == FALSE) and (readyMs < READY_WAIT_MS)
            waitms(READY_POLL_MS)
            readyMs += READY_POLL_MS
        bReady := motor.isReady()

#ifndef T0_OWN_TIER
PRI testT0_5() | minDef, maxDef, incDef, decrDef, eBelow, eNegative, eAbove, bRefuseOk, eAnchor, stepAnchor, bAnchorOk, eTop, stepTop, bTopOk, eRestore, bPass
' G / R17-T0-ACCEL (task 3577): setAcceleration() takes a rate in mm/s^2 at the rim, refuses one outside
' [ACCEL_MIN_MM_S2 .. ACCEL_MAX_MM_S2] with ERR_BAD_COUNT and changes nothing, and turns an accepted one into a
' constant ramp -- ramp_min == ramp_max == the step for that rate, ramp_inc 0, ramp_down untouched. The step for
' ACCEL_ANCHOR_MM_S2 must land within 1% of the default ramp_min (see the constant's derivation), and a larger
' rate must give a larger step. Nothing starts: the test calls testSetup() itself for the wheel geometry.
' UNFIXED: {rate} went straight into ramp_inc with no check, so every refused rate changed the ramp and an
' accepted one left ramp_min and ramp_max at their defaults -- the cell FAILs on both halves.
' NOMEAS when the active config has no wheel diameter (ERR_NO_WHEEL_DIA): there is no rim to convert at.
'
' @local minDef - the default ramp_min, read back before any call
' @local maxDef - the default ramp_max
' @local incDef - the default ramp_inc
' @local decrDef - the default ramp_down
' @local eBelow - setAcceleration(ACCEL_MIN_MM_S2 - 1)'s return (expected ERR_BAD_COUNT)
' @local eNegative - setAcceleration(ACCEL_BELOW_RANGE)'s return (expected ERR_BAD_COUNT)
' @local eAbove - setAcceleration(ACCEL_MAX_MM_S2 + 1)'s return (expected ERR_BAD_COUNT)
' @local bRefuseOk - every refusal returned its code and left the ramp as it was
' @local eAnchor - setAcceleration(ACCEL_ANCHOR_MM_S2)'s return
' @local stepAnchor - the step it produced
' @local bAnchorOk - the anchor call produced a constant ramp within 1% of the default ramp_min
' @local eTop - setAcceleration(ACCEL_MAX_MM_S2)'s return
' @local stepTop - the step it produced
' @local bTopOk - the top rate produced a constant ramp with a larger step than the anchor's
' @local eRestore - setRampingValues()'s return restoring the defaults
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-5,begin")
    motor.testSetup(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    motor.getError()                                        ' start from a clear slot
    minDef, maxDef, incDef, decrDef := motor.getRampingValues()

    eBelow := motor.setAcceleration(motor.ACCEL_MIN_MM_S2 - 1)
    bRefuseOk := (eBelow == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT) and bRampEquals(minDef, maxDef, incDef, decrDef)
    eNegative := motor.setAcceleration(ACCEL_BELOW_RANGE)
    bRefuseOk := bRefuseOk and (eNegative == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT) and bRampEquals(minDef, maxDef, incDef, decrDef)
    eAbove := motor.setAcceleration(motor.ACCEL_MAX_MM_S2 + 1)
    bRefuseOk := bRefuseOk and (eAbove == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT) and bRampEquals(minDef, maxDef, incDef, decrDef)
    motor.getError()                                        ' drain the refusals' recorded code
    debug("T0-5,refuse,below,", sdec_(eBelow), ",negative,", sdec_(eNegative), ",above,", sdec_(eAbove), ",unchanged,", zstr_(bRefuseOk ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

    eAnchor := motor.setAcceleration(ACCEL_ANCHOR_MM_S2)
    stepAnchor, bAnchorOk := constRampStep(@"anchor", ACCEL_ANCHOR_MM_S2, eAnchor, decrDef)
    bAnchorOk := bAnchorOk and (abs(stepAnchor - minDef) <= minDef / ACCEL_ANCHOR_TOL_DIV)
    eTop := motor.setAcceleration(motor.ACCEL_MAX_MM_S2)
    stepTop, bTopOk := constRampStep(@"top", motor.ACCEL_MAX_MM_S2, eTop, decrDef)
    bTopOk := bTopOk and (stepTop > stepAnchor)

    eRestore := motor.setRampingValues(minDef, maxDef, incDef, decrDef)      ' later tests start this motor
    bPass := bRefuseOk and bAnchorOk and bTopOk and (eRestore == motor.NO_ERROR)
    emitCellBool(@"R17-T0-ACCEL", @sTaskPromises, @"NONE", @"MM_S2_CONST_RAMP", eAnchor <> motor.ERR_NO_WHEEL_DIA, bPass, ACCEL_CALLS_JUDGED)

PRI constRampStep(pLabel, rateMmS2, eAccel, decrWant) : rampStep, bConst
' Read back the ramp an accepted setAcceleration() left, judge that it is a constant ramp, and print it.
' One debug() record serves every rate T0-5 accepts.
'
' @param pLabel - pointer to the rate's name, printed as the line's tag ("anchor" or "top")
' @param rateMmS2 - the rate that was set, mm/s squared
' @param eAccel - setAcceleration()'s return for it
' @param decrWant - the ramp_down it must have left untouched
' @returns rampStep - the step it produced: ramp_min read back
' @returns bConst - TRUE when the call returned NO_ERROR and left ramp_min == ramp_max, ramp_inc 0, ramp_down untouched

    rampStep, _, _, _ := motor.getRampingValues()
    bConst := (eAccel == motor.NO_ERROR) and bRampEquals(rampStep, rampStep, 0, decrWant)
    debug("T0-5,", zstr_(pLabel), ",mm_s2,", sdec_(rateMmS2), ",status,", sdec_(eAccel), ",step,", sdec_(rampStep), ",constant,", zstr_(bConst ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))
#endif

PRI emitCellDecl(pCell, pTask)
' One SIGNOFF-DECL, from hub strings (see emitCellBool() for why).
'
' @param pCell - pointer to the cell id
' @param pTask - pointer to the owning todo-mcp task number, as text

    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,", zstr_(pCell), ",task,", zstr_(pTask))

PRI emitCellBool(pCell, pTask, pMotor, pCrit, bMeasured, bPass, instCount)
' One BOOL SIGNOFF for a cell. The cell, motor and criterion names are hub strings rather than
' literals inside the debug() call, so every cell shares these two DEBUG records and their data -- this
' binary's DEBUG data is the budget PL-74's silent build ran close to (study F12), and each literal SIGNOFF
' line spends about 150 bytes of it.
'
' @param pCell - pointer to the cell id
' @param pTask - pointer to the owning todo-mcp task number, as text
' @param pMotor - pointer to the motor token (NONE, RIGHT, BOTH)
' @param pCrit - pointer to the criterion token
' @param bMeasured - TRUE when the condition arose and bPass is a measurement
' @param bPass - the criterion held
' @param instCount - the claims the verdict covers, printed as n when measured

    if bMeasured
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,", zstr_(pCell), ",task,", zstr_(pTask), ",motor,", zstr_(pMotor), ",crit,", zstr_(pCrit), ",measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,", udec_(instCount), ",verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,", zstr_(pCell), ",task,", zstr_(pTask), ",motor,", zstr_(pMotor), ",crit,", zstr_(pCrit), ",measured,NA,lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")

PRI emitCellNum(pCell, pTask, pMotor, pCrit, bMeasured, measuredVal, loVal, hiVal, pUnits, nCount, pVerdict)
' One numeric SIGNOFF for a cell, from hub strings, for the same reason as emitCellBool(): the text of
' a literal debug() record counts against the DEBUG data this binary must stay under (DBG-2), while
' hub strings do not. It prints byte for byte what the literal SIGNOFF lines it replaced printed.
'
' @param pCell - pointer to the cell id
' @param pTask - pointer to the owning todo-mcp task number, as text
' @param pMotor - pointer to the motor token (NONE, RIGHT, BOTH)
' @param pCrit - pointer to the criterion token
' @param bMeasured - TRUE when the condition arose and measuredVal is a measurement
' @param measuredVal - the reading (printed only when measured)
' @param loVal - the criterion's low limit
' @param hiVal - its high limit
' @param pUnits - pointer to the units token
' @param nCount - the n printed, in both forms, exactly as the caller gives it
' @param pVerdict - pointer to PASS or FAIL (printed only when measured)

    if bMeasured
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,", zstr_(pCell), ",task,", zstr_(pTask), ",motor,", zstr_(pMotor), ",crit,", zstr_(pCrit), ",measured,", sdec_(measuredVal), ",lo,", sdec_(loVal), ",hi,", sdec_(hiVal), ",units,", zstr_(pUnits), ",n,", udec_(nCount), ",verdict,", zstr_(pVerdict))
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,", zstr_(pCell), ",task,", zstr_(pTask), ",motor,", zstr_(pMotor), ",crit,", zstr_(pCrit), ",measured,NA,lo,", sdec_(loVal), ",hi,", sdec_(hiVal), ",units,", zstr_(pUnits), ",n,", udec_(nCount), ",verdict,NOMEAS")

#ifndef T0_OWN_TIER
PRI bRampEquals(minWant, maxWant, incWant, decrWant) : bSame | minRamp, maxRamp, incRamp, decrRamp
' Report whether `motor`'s four ramping values read back exactly as given.
'
' @param minWant - expected ramp_min
' @param maxWant - expected ramp_max
' @param incWant - expected ramp_inc
' @param decrWant - expected ramp_down
' @returns bSame - TRUE when all four read back equal
'
' @local minRamp - ramp_min read back
' @local maxRamp - ramp_max read back
' @local incRamp - ramp_inc read back
' @local decrRamp - ramp_down read back

    minRamp, maxRamp, incRamp, decrRamp := motor.getRampingValues()
    bSame := (minRamp == minWant) and (maxRamp == maxWant) and (incRamp == incWant) and (decrRamp == decrWant)

PRI testT0_6() | resultKm, resultMi, rotResult, eRotCode, eStopDist, eStopCode
' I/T, K: getDistance(DDU_KM)/(DDU_MI) are valid units and return a value.
' getRotationCount(99) (99 is not a DRU_* unit) and stopAfterDistance(0,
' DDU_IN) (a zero distance) used to abort; under the error contract (task 3554)
' the getter returns its neutral 0 and records ERR_BAD_UNITS, and the command
' returns and records ERR_BAD_COUNT. The two codes feed R16-T0-NOABORT, judged
' in T0-7. UNFIXED: both calls aborted, which ended the run at main()'s trap
' and left the cell with no verdict.
'
' @local resultKm - getDistance(DDU_KM)'s return
' @local resultMi - getDistance(DDU_MI)'s return
' @local rotResult - getRotationCount(99)'s return (expected 0)
' @local eRotCode - getError() after it (expected ERR_BAD_UNITS)
' @local eStopDist - stopAfterDistance(0, DDU_IN)'s return (expected ERR_BAD_COUNT)
' @local eStopCode - getError() after it (expected ERR_BAD_COUNT)

    motor.getError()                                        ' start from a clear slot
    resultKm := motor.getDistance(motor.DDU_KM)
    debug("T0-6,call,getDistance_KM,result,", sdec_(resultKm))

    resultMi := motor.getDistance(motor.DDU_MI)
    debug("T0-6,call,getDistance_MI,result,", sdec_(resultMi))

    motor.getError()                                        ' the distance calls' own codes are not judged here
    rotResult := motor.getRotationCount(99)
    eRotCode := motor.getError()
    debug("T0-6,call,getRotationCount_99,result,", sdec_(rotResult), ",error,", sdec_(eRotCode))

    eStopDist := motor.stopAfterDistance(0, motor.DDU_IN)
    eStopCode := motor.getError()
    debug("T0-6,call,stopAfterDistance_0in,status,", sdec_(eStopDist), ",error,", sdec_(eStopCode))

    bUnitsCodesOk := (rotResult == 0) and (eRotCode == motor.ERR_BAD_UNITS) and (eStopDist == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT) and (eStopCode == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT)

PRI testT0_7() | eSetupA, eOverlap, eOverlapCode, eNonOverlap, bPass
' AE: two separate isp_bldc_motor instances, testSetup() on deliberately
' overlapping pin groups -- PINS_P0_P15 and PINS_P8_P23 overlap on P8-P15, the
' audit's own example. motorA claims P0-P15; motorB's overlapping testSetup()
' is refused: since the error contract (task 3554) it RETURNS
' ERR_PIN_GROUP_IN_USE and records it, where it used to abort. No real board is
' wired to either base, so this only ever toggles unused pins briefly while
' probing for a board that is not there.
'
' AE's other half, the one that matters to shipped code: two motors on
' NON-overlapping ranges must still both initialise (motorB on P32_P47).
'
' R16-T0-NOABORT (task 3554): TRUE when T0-6's two codes were right AND
' motorA's claim returned NO_ERROR AND the overlap returned and recorded
' ERR_PIN_GROUP_IN_USE AND the non-overlapping claim returned NO_ERROR. That this
' line prints at all is the "nothing aborted" half.
'
' T0-14a/T0-14b release motorA/motorB's claims made here (P0_P15, P32_P47)
' before they run, so this test's claims never leak into theirs.
'
' @local eSetupA - motorA.testSetup(P0_P15)'s status
' @local eOverlap - motorB.testSetup(P8_P23)'s status (expected ERR_PIN_GROUP_IN_USE)
' @local eOverlapCode - motorB.getError() after it
' @local eNonOverlap - motorB.testSetup(P32_P47)'s status
' @local bPass - R16-T0-NOABORT's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-7,begin,left_base,P0_P15,right_base,P8_P23")
    motorA.getError()
    motorB.getError()
    eSetupA := motorA.testSetup(motorA.PINS_P0_P15, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    eOverlap := motorB.testSetup(motorB.PINS_P8_P23, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorB.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    eOverlapCode := motorB.getError()
    debug("T0-7,end,claim_status,", sdec_(eSetupA), ",overlap_status,", sdec_(eOverlap), ",overlap_error,", sdec_(eOverlapCode))

    debug("T0-7,nonoverlap,begin,held_base,P0_P15,new_base,P32_P47")
    eNonOverlap := motorB.testSetup(motorB.PINS_P32_P47, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorB.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    debug("T0-7,nonoverlap,end,status,", sdec_(eNonOverlap))
    motorA.getError()
    motorB.getError()

    bPass := bUnitsCodesOk and (eSetupA == motorA.NO_ERROR) and (eOverlap == motorB.ERR_PIN_GROUP_IN_USE) and (eOverlapCode == motorB.ERR_PIN_GROUP_IN_USE) and (eNonOverlap == motorB.NO_ERROR)
    emitCellBool(@"R16-T0-NOABORT", @"3554", @"NONE", @"CODE_NOT_ABORT", TRUE, bPass, 4)

PRI spread5(pArr) : spreadVal | idx, mx, mn
' Helper for R8-T0-ZXS (T0-11): max - min of 5 LONGs at {pArr}.
'
' @param pArr - address of a 5-element LONG array
' @returns spreadVal - max(pArr[0..4]) - min(pArr[0..4])
' @local idx - loop index
' @local mx - running maximum
' @local mn - running minimum

    mx := LONG[pArr][0]
    mn := LONG[pArr][0]
    repeat idx from 1 to 4
        if LONG[pArr][idx] > mx
            mx := LONG[pArr][idx]
        if LONG[pArr][idx] < mn
            mn := LONG[pArr][idx]
    spreadVal := mx - mn

PRI emitZxsSignoff(pCritStr, measuredSpread, validCount)
' Helper for R8-T0-ZXS (T0-11): emit one channel's SIGNOFF record. NOMEAS with n = validCount
' when fewer than 5 valid lifetimes were captured (design SS A.5-e); the 5-of-5 path prints
' measuredSpread against SF_ZXS_LO..SF_ZXS_HI. A genuine abort during T0-11 is caught by main()'s
' single top-level trap (task 3539), which ends the whole run before this is even reached.
'
' Worst-case bytes for this line ("R8-T0-ZXS"/"ZXS_I".."ZXS_W", motor RIGHT,
' measured up to -2_147_483_648, n 5, verdict FAIL): counted by hand at 130
' bytes, well under the 255-byte per-debug() limit (test_bench_detect.spin2
' header) and under design SS B.2's general 193-byte bound.
'
' @param pCritStr - pointer to "ZXS_I"/"ZXS_U"/"ZXS_V"/"ZXS_W"
' @param measuredSpread - spread5()'s result for this channel (ignored, NA, when validCount < 5)
' @param validCount - number of valid lifetimes captured (0..5)

    if validCount == 5
        emitCellNum(@"R8-T0-ZXS", @"3529", @"RIGHT", pCritStr, TRUE, measuredSpread, SF_ZXS_LO, SF_ZXS_HI, @"MV_X10", 5, ((measuredSpread >= SF_ZXS_LO) and (measuredSpread <= SF_ZXS_HI)) ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL")
    else
        emitCellNum(@"R8-T0-ZXS", @"3529", @"RIGHT", pCritStr, FALSE, 0, SF_ZXS_LO, SF_ZXS_HI, @"MV_X10", validCount, 0)

PRI testT0_11() | cycleIdx, validCount, startResult, rawMotorCog, readyMs, sampleIdx, sumI, sumU, sumV, sumW, meanI[5], meanU[5], meanV[5], meanW[5], nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, nSenseU, nSenseV, nSenseW, eDrvrState, bDidFault, bValid, spreadI, spreadU, spreadV, spreadW
' R8-T0-ZXS (task 3529), design SS H.1: 5 cycles of start() -> wait ready
' (<= 2000 ms, T0 has no watchdog) -> 200 samples x 5 ms of testGetTelemetry()
' i/u/v/w at zero command (start() leaves the command at zero, drive floated)
' -> stop() -> 500 ms rest. Per channel: max - min of the 5 lifetime means
' (in mV x10) is the measured value; fewer than 5 valid lifetimes is NOMEAS.
'
' PL-21: telemetry is read only while `motor`'s own driver cog is actually
' running (start() succeeded AND isReady() went TRUE within the 2000 ms
' budget) -- otherwise this cycle contributes no lifetime at all, exactly
' the frozen-telemetry hazard PL-21 documents.
'
' Accumulator bound: sense_*_mV is a millivolt reading against the driver's
' 3300 mV ADC scale (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:2617, numerator = 3300 mV << 11),
' so |sense_x_mV| <= 5000 with generous margin. Over 200 samples,
' |sumX| <= 200 * 5000 = 1_000_000, and |sumX * 10| <= 10_000_000 -- both
' comfortably inside the 32-bit signed range (+-2_147_483_647).
'
' start() is called UNTRAPPED (task 3539): it returns a cog id 0..7 on success or -1 on
' failure, neither of which is an abort. POSITIVE CONTROL (P4): bValid also requires
' testGetMotorCog() to independently read back startResult + 1 -- the same cross-check T0-15a
' uses -- so a stuck value cannot satisfy this cell by accident; a real abort is caught by
' main()'s single top-level trap instead.
'
' @local cycleIdx - 0..4, which of the 5 start()/stop() cycles
' @local validCount - number of cycles that produced a valid lifetime (0..5)
' @local startResult - start()'s return for this cycle
' @local rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot right after start(), the positive control
' @local readyMs - ready-wait accumulator, bounded at 2000 ms
' @local sampleIdx - 0..199, which telemetry sample within a lifetime
' @local sumI - per-lifetime accumulator of sense_i_mV samples (see bound above)
' @local sumU - per-lifetime accumulator of sense_u_mV samples
' @local sumV - per-lifetime accumulator of sense_v_mV samples
' @local sumW - per-lifetime accumulator of sense_w_mV samples
' @local meanI - the up-to-5 lifetime means of sense_i_mV, in mV x10
' @local meanU - the up-to-5 lifetime means of sense_u_mV, in mV x10
' @local meanV - the up-to-5 lifetime means of sense_v_mV, in mV x10
' @local meanW - the up-to-5 lifetime means of sense_w_mV, in mV x10
' @local nDuty - testGetTelemetry()'s duty sample (unused here)
' @local nErr - testGetTelemetry()'s error sample (unused here)
' @local nSenseI - testGetTelemetry()'s sense_i_mV sample
' @local nSenseU - testGetTelemetry()'s sense_u_mV sample
' @local nSenseV - testGetTelemetry()'s sense_v_mV sample
' @local nSenseW - testGetTelemetry()'s sense_w_mV sample
' @local eDrvrState - testGetTelemetry()'s DCS_* sample (unused here)
' @local bDidFault - testGetTelemetry()'s fault sample (unused here)
' @local bValid - TRUE when this cycle's start() succeeded, went ready in time, and cross-checked
' @local spreadI - spread5()'s result for the I channel (NA when validCount < 5)
' @local spreadU - spread5()'s result for the U channel (NA when validCount < 5)
' @local spreadV - spread5()'s result for the V channel (NA when validCount < 5)
' @local spreadW - spread5()'s result for the W channel (NA when validCount < 5)

    debug("T0-11,begin")
    validCount := 0
    repeat cycleIdx from 0 to 4
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        benchLog.cogEventEnd()
        rawMotorCog := motor.testGetMotorCog()
        readyMs := 0
        repeat while (motor.isReady() == FALSE) and (readyMs < 2000)
            waitms(10)
            readyMs += 10
        bValid := (startResult >= 0) and motor.isReady() and (rawMotorCog == startResult + 1)
        if bValid
            sumI := 0
            sumU := 0
            sumV := 0
            sumW := 0
            repeat sampleIdx from 0 to 199
                nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, nSenseU, nSenseV, nSenseW, eDrvrState, bDidFault := motor.testGetTelemetry()
                sumI += nSenseI
                sumU += nSenseU
                sumV += nSenseV
                sumW += nSenseW
                waitms(5)
            meanI[validCount] := (sumI * 10) / 200
            meanU[validCount] := (sumU * 10) / 200
            meanV[validCount] := (sumV * 10) / 200
            meanW[validCount] := (sumW * 10) / 200
            debug("T0-11,lifetime,", udec_(validCount), ",mean_i_x10,", sdec_(meanI[validCount]), ",mean_u_x10,", sdec_(meanU[validCount]), ",mean_v_x10,", sdec_(meanV[validCount]), ",mean_w_x10,", sdec_(meanW[validCount]))
            validCount += 1
        else
            debug("T0-11,cycle,", udec_(cycleIdx), ",skipped,not_ready,start_result,", sdec_(startResult), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog))
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        motor.stop()
        waitms(500)

    if validCount == 5
        spreadI := spread5(@meanI)
        spreadU := spread5(@meanU)
        spreadV := spread5(@meanV)
        spreadW := spread5(@meanW)
    debug("T0-11,end,valid_lifetimes,", udec_(validCount))
    emitZxsSignoff(@"ZXS_I", spreadI, validCount)
    emitZxsSignoff(@"ZXS_U", spreadU, validCount)
    emitZxsSignoff(@"ZXS_V", spreadV, validCount)
    emitZxsSignoff(@"ZXS_W", spreadW, validCount)

PRI testT0_13() | startResult, rawMotorCog, readyMs, missedCount, illegalCount, sumCounts, bReady, bPass
' R3-T0-STOPPED (task 3501), design SS H.1: start at zero command, wait ready
' (<= 2000 ms), hold 1000 ms, read both hall integrity counts. measured =
' missed + illegal; a stationary motor's hall code never transitions, so the
' criterion is exactly 0.
' start() is called UNTRAPPED (task 3539): it returns a cog id 0..7 on success or -1 on
' failure, neither of which is an abort; a genuine abort is caught by main()'s single
' top-level trap. POSITIVE CONTROL (P4): the ready branch also requires testGetMotorCog() to
' independently read back startResult + 1, so a stuck value cannot satisfy this cell.
'
' @local startResult - start()'s return
' @local rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot right after start(), the positive control
' @local readyMs - ready-wait accumulator, bounded at 2000 ms
' @local missedCount - getHallIntegrityCounts()'s nMissedTransitions
' @local illegalCount - getHallIntegrityCounts()'s nIllegalCodes
' @local sumCounts - missedCount + illegalCount, this cell's measured value
' @local bReady - TRUE when the driver reached ready within budget
' @local bPass - this cell's verdict

    debug("T0-13,begin")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    rawMotorCog := motor.testGetMotorCog()
    readyMs := 0
    repeat while (motor.isReady() == FALSE) and (readyMs < 2000)
        waitms(10)
        readyMs += 10
    bReady := motor.isReady()
    if (startResult >= 0) and bReady and (rawMotorCog == startResult + 1)
        waitms(1000)
        missedCount, illegalCount := motor.getHallIntegrityCounts()
        sumCounts := missedCount + illegalCount
        bPass := (sumCounts == SF_STOP_LO)
        debug("T0-13,end,missed,", udec_(missedCount), ",illegal,", udec_(illegalCount))
        emitCellNum(@"R3-T0-STOPPED", @"3501", @"NONE", @"STOPPED_COUNTS", TRUE, sumCounts, SF_STOP_LO, SF_STOP_HI, @"COUNT", 1, bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL")
    else
        debug("T0-13,end,not_ready,start_result,", sdec_(startResult), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog))
        emitCellNum(@"R3-T0-STOPPED", @"3501", @"NONE", @"STOPPED_COUNTS", FALSE, 0, SF_STOP_LO, SF_STOP_HI, @"COUNT", 0, 0)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_14a() | baseIdx, pinBase, iter, eBoardRev, notRevBCount, pMotorTok
' R2-T0-REPEAT (task 3500): 32 x testSetup() + getBoardType() on each
' populated base, P16 and P32. motorA/motorB are stopped first so T0-7's pin
' claims are released before this test claims the same bases. testSetup() is
' called UNTRAPPED (task 3539); a genuine abort is caught by main()'s single
' top-level trap.
'
' @local baseIdx - 0 (T0_MOTOR_BASE) or 1 (T0_SECOND_BASE)
' @local pinBase - the base under test this iteration
' @local iter - 0..31, which of the 32 reads
' @local eBoardRev - getBoardType()'s return for this read
' @local notRevBCount - this base's measured value: reads that were not REV_B
' @local pMotorTok - "RIGHT" for P16, "LEFT" for P32 (the bench boards), the record's motor field

    debug("T0-14,begin,repeat")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    motorB.stop()

    repeat baseIdx from 0 to 1
        if baseIdx == 0
            pinBase := T0_MOTOR_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"RIGHT"
        else
            pinBase := T0_SECOND_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"LEFT"
        notRevBCount := 0
        repeat iter from 0 to 31
            motor.testSetup(pinBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
            eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
            if eBoardRev <> motor.REV_B
                notRevBCount += 1
        debug("T0-14a,base,", udec_(pinBase), ",not_revb_count,", udec_(notRevBCount))
        emitCellNum(@"R2-T0-REPEAT", @"3500", pMotorTok, @"READS_NOT_REVB", TRUE, notRevBCount, SF_REPEAT_LO, SF_REPEAT_HI, @"COUNT", 32, (notRevBCount == 0) ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_14b() | baseIdx, pinBase, otherBase, deadGap, pwmLimit, dutyMin, dutyMax, adcFrame, frameCnt, pinAdcX, eBoardRev, startResult, readyMs, bDirtyIsRevB, pMotorTok
' R2-T0-DIRTY (task 3500), design SS H.1: on each populated base, an
' initialised but NOT running group. The harness itself drives base+4 into
' the driver's own steady-state ADC sampling mode -- adc_modes+2 =
' p_adc_1x | p_count_highs, WRPIN'd onto adc_pins at isp_bldc_motor.spin2:2913
' (mode constants at :2633..2635); the matching count period is adc_fram,
' WXPIN'd at :2909, and this test reads adc_fram back through the existing
' testGetDriveConstants() getter rather than recomputing it -- then leaves
' the pin with DIR low (pinfloat(), which per spin2-authoring-guide.md:1270
' clears DIR only and leaves the WRPIN mode set), exactly the state an idle
' driver cog would
' leave it in without the "defensive clear" getBoardType() performs (its own
' pinclear() at :900 when motorCog == 0). measured TRUE when the read that
' follows is REV_B; this is the cell that FAILs if that defensive clear ever
' regresses.
'
' Also: start() -> ready -> stop() on the same group, then start the OTHER
' group on motorA in between (to confirm it stays clean of this group's
' state), then testSetup()+getBoardType() again on the original group.
' Printed as T0-14b CSV lines; not a separate sign-off instance (design
' SS H.1 states one SIGNOFF per base for this cell).
'
' testSetup() and start() below are all called UNTRAPPED (task 3539); a genuine abort is caught
' by main()'s single top-level trap instead.
'
' @local baseIdx - 0 (T0_MOTOR_BASE) or 1 (T0_SECOND_BASE)
' @local pinBase - the base under test this iteration
' @local otherBase - the other populated base, started on motorA in between
' @local deadGap - dead_gap, from testGetDriveConstants() (unused here)
' @local pwmLimit - pwm_limit, from testGetDriveConstants() (unused here)
' @local dutyMin - duty_min, from testGetDriveConstants() (unused here)
' @local dutyMax - duty_max, from testGetDriveConstants() (unused here)
' @local adcFrame - adc_fram, the ADC sample period matching the PWM frame width (programmed into the ADC pin)
' @local frameCnt - frame_cnt, from testGetDriveConstants() (unused here)
' @local pinAdcX - pinBase + 4, the detection/ADC-common pin
' @local eBoardRev - getBoardType()'s return, read twice per base
' @local startResult - start()'s return for the confirm cycle
' @local readyMs - ready-wait accumulator, bounded at 2000 ms, reused for both confirm starts
' @local bDirtyIsRevB - this base's measured value: the dirty-pin read was REV_B
' @local pMotorTok - "RIGHT" for P16, "LEFT" for P32 (the bench boards), the record's motor field

    debug("T0-14,begin,dirty")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    motorB.stop()

    repeat baseIdx from 0 to 1
        if baseIdx == 0
            pinBase := T0_MOTOR_BASE
            otherBase := T0_SECOND_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"RIGHT"
        else
            pinBase := T0_SECOND_BASE
            otherBase := T0_MOTOR_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"LEFT"

        motor.testSetup(pinBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        deadGap, pwmLimit, dutyMin, dutyMax, adcFrame, frameCnt := motor.testGetDriveConstants()
        pinAdcX := pinBase + 4

        wrpin(pinAdcX, P_ADC_1X | P_COUNT_HIGHS)
        wxpin(pinAdcX, adcFrame)
        pinfloat(pinAdcX)                              ' DIR low; PINFLOAT() clears DIR only, the WRPIN mode survives (spin2-authoring-guide.md:1270)

        eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
        bDirtyIsRevB := (eBoardRev == motor.REV_B)
        debug("T0-14b,base,", udec_(pinBase), ",dirty_read,", udec_(eBoardRev))

        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        startResult := motor.start(pinBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        benchLog.cogEventEnd()
        readyMs := 0
        repeat while (motor.isReady() == FALSE) and (readyMs < 2000)
            waitms(10)
            readyMs += 10
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        motor.stop()

        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        motorA.start(otherBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        benchLog.cogEventEnd()
        readyMs := 0
        repeat while (motorA.isReady() == FALSE) and (readyMs < 2000)
            waitms(10)
            readyMs += 10
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        motorA.stop()

        motor.testSetup(pinBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
        debug("T0-14b,base,", udec_(pinBase), ",poststart_read,", udec_(eBoardRev))

        emitCellBool(@"R2-T0-DIRTY", @"3500", pMotorTok, @"POSTSTOP_REVB", TRUE, bDirtyIsRevB, 1)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_14c() | eBoardRev, bEmpty
' R2-T0-EMPTY (task 3500): testSetup(PINS_P0_P15) + getBoardType(). measured
' TRUE when it reads REV_Unknown. NEVER probe PINS_P40_P55: its sense pin P44
' is the LEFT board's pin_pwm_w_l (32 + 12), and T0 runs with the rail on --
' getBoardType() drives it high for 1 ms (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:889-890,
' hazard also recorded at test_bench_detect.spin2:161-165). testSetup() is
' called UNTRAPPED (task 3539); a genuine abort is caught by main()'s single
' top-level trap.
'
' @local eBoardRev - getBoardType()'s return
' @local bEmpty - this cell's measured value: the read was REV_Unknown

    debug("T0-14,begin,empty")
    motor.testSetup(motor.PINS_P0_P15, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
    bEmpty := (eBoardRev == motor.REV_Unknown)
    debug("T0-14c,base,P0_P15,read,", udec_(eBoardRev))
    emitCellBool(@"R2-T0-EMPTY", @"3500", @"NONE", @"EMPTY_NODET", TRUE, bEmpty, 1)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_15a() | startResult, rawMotorCog, bPass
' R1-T0-START (task 3499): start() on P16, called UNTRAPPED (task 3539) --
' it returns a cog id 0..7 on success or -1 on failure, neither of which is
' an abort; a genuine abort is caught by main()'s single top-level trap. The
' return must be in 0..7 and equal testGetMotorCog() - 1. A BOOL cell (task
' 3537): measured is TRUE only when both hold; the two raw numbers are on the
' T0-15a line. testGetMotorCog() is ALSO this cell's positive control (P4):
' it is read independently of start()'s own return, so a stuck value cannot
' satisfy the cell by accident.
'
' @local startResult - start()'s return
' @local rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot, taken right after start()
' @local bPass - this cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-15,begin,start")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    rawMotorCog := motor.testGetMotorCog()
    bPass := (startResult >= SF_COG_LO) and (startResult <= SF_COG_HI) and (startResult == rawMotorCog - 1)
    debug("T0-15a,start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog))
    emitCellBool(@"R1-T0-START", @"3499", @"NONE", @"RET_EQ_COG_M1", TRUE, bPass, 1)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_15c() | baseline, startResult1, free1, startResult2, rawMotorCog2, free2, free3, diffFree, bPass
' R1-T0-RESTART (task 3499): count free cogs (baseline) -> start() -> free1 ->
' start() again with NO stop() -> free2 -> stop() -> free3. A BOOL cell (task
' 3537): measured is TRUE only when |free2 - free1| + |free3 - baseline| == 0
' AND free1 == baseline - SF_START_COGS (PL-24: a second start() must not orphan
' the first start's cogs; task 3513: a start() is the driver plus its front cog,
' so this is also the single-motor fixed-cog-count cell -- UNFIXED, start()
' alone took 1 cog and this term FAILs); the four free-cog counts are on the
' T0-15c line. T0-15d reads
' state immediately after this test's own stop(), so it must be called right
' after this one from runTier0Tests().
' Both start()s are called UNTRAPPED (task 3539); a genuine abort is caught
' by main()'s single top-level trap. POSITIVE CONTROL (P4): the second
' start()'s testGetMotorCog() readback must independently agree with its own
' return, so a stuck value on either start() cannot satisfy this cell.
'
' @local baseline - free cogs before either start()
' @local startResult1 - first start()'s return
' @local free1 - free cogs after the first start()
' @local startResult2 - second start()'s return, no intervening stop()
' @local rawMotorCog2 - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot after the second start(), the positive control
' @local free2 - free cogs after the second start()
' @local free3 - free cogs after this test's stop()
' @local diffFree - abs(free2-free1) + abs(free3-baseline), one of this cell's two conditions
' @local bPass - this cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-15,begin,restart")
    bRestartStopValid := FALSE
    baseline := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult1 := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    free1 := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult2 := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    rawMotorCog2 := motor.testGetMotorCog()
    free2 := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()
    bRestartStopValid := (startResult1 >= 0) and (startResult2 >= 0) and (rawMotorCog2 == startResult2 + 1)
    free3 := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    diffFree := abs(free2 - free1) + abs(free3 - baseline)
    bPass := (diffFree == SF_RESTART_LO) and (free1 == baseline - SF_START_COGS)
    debug("T0-15c,baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",free1,", udec_(free1), ",start1,", sdec_(startResult1), ",free2,", udec_(free2), ",start2,", sdec_(startResult2), ",raw_motor_cog2,", sdec_(rawMotorCog2), ",free3,", udec_(free3))
    emitCellBool(@"R1-T0-RESTART", @"3499", @"NONE", @"NO_ORPHAN", TRUE, bPass, 1)

PRI testT0_15d() | bReady, bStopped, eState, bPass
' R10-T0-STOPREADY (task 3533): right after T0-15c's own stop() (this method
' must run immediately after testT0_15c() from runTier0Tests(), with no other
' call touching `motor` in between). measured TRUE when isReady() is FALSE
' AND isStopped() is FALSE (PL-28 item 2 / task 3533: stop() now leaves
' drv_state at DCS_Unknown, not stale). getDriverState() is logged beside the
' verdict; DCS_Unknown is expected.
' This cell judges the state T0-15c's own stop() left, so it is NOMEAS,n,0
' when either of T0-15c's start()s returned -1 or failed its positive
' control, or T0-15c never reached its stop() -- bRestartStopValid FALSE.
'
' @local bReady - motor.isReady()'s value right now
' @local bStopped - motor.isStopped()'s value right now
' @local eState - motor.getDriverState()'s value right now (expect DCS_Unknown)
' @local bPass - this cell's verdict

    bReady := motor.isReady()
    bStopped := motor.isStopped()
    eState := motor.getDriverState()
    bPass := (bReady == FALSE) and (bStopped == FALSE)
    debug("T0-15d,driver_state,", udec_(eState), ",ready,", zstr_(bReady ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",stopped,", zstr_(bStopped ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",t0_15c_valid,", zstr_(bRestartStopValid ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))
    emitCellBool(@"R10-T0-STOPREADY", @"3533", @"NONE", @"STOP_NOT_READY", bRestartStopValid, bPass, 1)

PRI runExhaustionPhase() | baseline, cogsOccupied, heldCount, startT15, rawCogT15, startT22, codeT22, rawCogT22, freeAfter
' The three cog-exhaustion cells share ONE occupancy (PL-85: each used to start and stop seven spacers of
' its own, and every damaged record sat beside such a burst). One occupy burst, then T0-8 and T0-15b with
' every spare cog held; one spacer released so exactly one cog is free for T0-22's start; one release
' burst; then one free-cog count that both T0-15b and T0-22 judge (free_after == baseline, as before).
' Destructive: a start() that fails can leave the object half-initialised, so this runs last.

' Local Variables:
' @local baseline - free cogs before the occupancy
' @local cogsOccupied - spacers the occupancy started (every spare cog)
' @local heldCount - spacers held (every spare cog, then one fewer for T0-22)
' @local startT15 - T0-15b's start() return under total exhaustion
' @local rawCogT15 - testGetMotorCog() after T0-15b's start()
' @local startT22 - T0-22's start() return with one cog free
' @local codeT22 - getError() after T0-22's start()
' @local rawCogT22 - testGetMotorCog() after T0-22's start()
' @local freeAfter - free cogs after every spacer is released

    debug("T0-EXH,begin,one_occupancy,cells,T0-8,T0-15b,T0-22")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()
    motorA.stop()
    motor.getError()
    baseline := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    cogsOccupied := occupySpacers(MAX_SPACER_COGS)
    heldCount := cogsOccupied

    testT0_8(heldCount)
    startT15, rawCogT15 := testT0_15bStart()

    heldCount := releaseOneSpacer(heldCount)
    startT22, codeT22, rawCogT22 := testT0_22Start()

    releaseSpacers(heldCount)
    freeAfter := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    debug("T0-EXH,end,baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",held_for_t22,", udec_(heldCount), ",free_after,", udec_(freeAfter))

    testT0_15bJudge(cogsOccupied, baseline, startT15, rawCogT15, freeAfter)
    testT0_22Judge(baseline, heldCount, startT22, codeT22, rawCogT22, freeAfter)

PRI testT0_8(heldCount) | startResult
' C, AD: with every spare cog occupied (runExhaustionPhase()), call the real start() (not testSetup())
' and print its raw return. coginit() returns the documented $8000_xxxx form on failure, not a bare -1;
' start() itself returns -1 on failure specifically, which is what R1-T0-EXHAUST (T0-15b) checks. This
' test exists to print the raw value, not to judge it; R1-T0-EXHAUST is the harsher probe that also
' confirms no cog leaked.
'
' @param heldCount - spacers holding every spare cog

' Local Variables:
' @local startResult - start()'s raw return value under cog exhaustion, called UNTRAPPED
'                       (task 3539): cog exhaustion is a normal -1 return, not an abort, so
'                       nothing here needs a trap; a genuine abort is caught by main()'s single
'                       top-level trap instead

    debug("T0-8,begin")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    debug("T0-8,end,cogs_occupied,", udec_(heldCount), ",start_return,", sdec_(startResult))

    ' stop() unconditionally. A start() that returned -1 may STILL have gotten
    ' partway -- the 2026-09-10 run shows a driver cog reaching INIT on a call
    ' that reported failure -- so the object can be left half-initialised, and
    ' anything that starts it afterwards then fails too. Leave it clean.
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI spacerLoop()
' Idle forever -- exists only to occupy a cog so start() has none left (runExhaustionPhase()). It never
' prints and holds no lock, so it may be stopped at any moment.
'

    repeat
        waitms(1000)

PRI occupySpacers(maxCount) : heldCount | spareCogId
' Start up to maxCount spacer cogs and hold them in heldSpacerId[] until releaseSpacers(). The whole
' burst is one cog event: nothing prints until it ends.
'
' @param maxCount - the most spacers to start
' @returns heldCount - spacers now running

' Local Variables:
' @local spareCogId - cogspin()'s return for the current attempt

    heldCount := 0
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    repeat while heldCount < (maxCount <# MAX_SPACER_COGS)
        spareCogId := cogspin(NEWCOG, spacerLoop(), @spacerStacks[heldCount * SPACER_STACK_LONGS])
        if spareCogId < 0
            quit
        heldSpacerId[heldCount] := spareCogId
        heldCount += 1
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()

PRI releaseOneSpacer(heldCount) : stillHeld
' Stop the last spacer occupySpacers() started, freeing exactly one cog.
'
' @param heldCount - spacers held now
' @returns stillHeld - spacers held after this (heldCount - 1, or 0 when none was held)

    stillHeld := heldCount
    if stillHeld > 0
        stillHeld -= 1
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        cogstop(heldSpacerId[stillHeld])

PRI releaseSpacers(heldCount) | spacerIdx
' Stop the first heldCount spacers occupySpacers() started, as one cog event.
'
' @param heldCount - spacers to stop

' Local Variables:
' @local spacerIdx - index into heldSpacerId[]

    if heldCount > 0                                        ' repeat 0 to -1 would count down, not skip
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        repeat spacerIdx from 0 to heldCount - 1
            cogstop(heldSpacerId[spacerIdx])

PRI testT0_16() | baseline, startResult, eCode, rawMotorCog, freeAfter, bPass
' R16-T0-BADGROUP (task 3554, F-3): start() with a value that is not a PINS_* group. The error contract
' validates every argument before anything is acquired, so the call must return -1, record
' ERR_BAD_PIN_GROUP, launch no cog (testGetMotorCog() 0) and leave the free-cog count unchanged.
' UNFIXED: an illegal group launched a driver cog on pins derived from -1 (F-3).
'
' @local baseline - free cogs before the call
' @local startResult - start()'s return (expected -1)
' @local eCode - getError() after it (expected ERR_BAD_PIN_GROUP)
' @local rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog() after it (expected 0)
' @local freeAfter - free cogs after the call
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-16,begin,bad_group")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    motorA.getError()
    baseline := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motorA.start(BAD_PIN_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    eCode := motorA.getError()
    rawMotorCog := motorA.testGetMotorCog()
    freeAfter := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    bPass := (startResult == -1) and (eCode == motorA.ERR_BAD_PIN_GROUP) and (rawMotorCog == 0) and (freeAfter == baseline)
    debug("T0-16,end,start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",error,", sdec_(eCode), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog), ",baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",free_after,", udec_(freeAfter))
    emitCellBool(@"R16-T0-BADGROUP", @"3554", @"NONE", @"REJECT_NO_COG", TRUE, bPass, 1)

PRI testT0_17() | markPins, legalBase, dirBefore, startResult, dirAfter, bPass
' R16-T0-PINSKEEP (task 3554, PL-48): the release demo's order -- validBasePinForChoice() then start() on a
' fresh instance -- must not touch P8..P15, where demo_single_motor runs HDMI. The marker is this cog's own
' DIR bits for P8..P15, set through a 15 k pull-down (WRPIN P_LOW_15K, then PINLOW), so the marker drives
' nothing harder than a pull resistor. PINCLEAR clears DIR (p2kbSpin2Pinclear), and the unfixed chain ran
' pinclear(0 addpins 7) and pinclear(8 addpins 7) on THIS cog inside start()'s stop-first, so a cleared
' bit is the defect. motorP is an instance nothing else in this file has touched.
' UNFIXED: validBasePinForChoice() took the claim, start() then stop()ped first with pinbase still 0, and
' DIR bits 8..15 read 0 afterwards.
'
' @local markPins - the P8..P15 pin field
' @local legalBase - validBasePinForChoice()'s return
' @local dirBefore - DIR bits 8..15 after the marker is set (expected all set)
' @local startResult - motorP.start()'s return
' @local dirAfter - DIR bits 8..15 after start() and stop()
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-17,begin,pins_keep")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()
    markPins := PL48_MARK_BASE addpins PL48_MARK_SPAN
    wrpin(markPins, P_LOW_15K)
    pinlow(markPins)
    dirBefore := (DIRA >> PL48_MARK_SHIFT) & PL48_MARK_MASK
    legalBase := motorP.validBasePinForChoice(T0_MOTOR_BASE)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motorP.start(legalBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorP.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    motorP.stop()
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    dirAfter := (DIRA >> PL48_MARK_SHIFT) & PL48_MARK_MASK
    pinclear(markPins)
    bPass := (dirBefore == PL48_MARK_MASK) and (dirAfter == PL48_MARK_MASK) and (startResult >= SF_COG_LO) and (startResult <= SF_COG_HI)
    debug("T0-17,end,legal_base,", sdec_(legalBase), ",start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",dir_before,", uhex_(dirBefore), ",dir_after,", uhex_(dirAfter))
    emitCellBool(@"R16-T0-PINSKEEP", @"3554", @"RIGHT", @"P8_P15_UNTOUCHED", TRUE, bPass, 1)

PRI testT0_18() | eDist, eTime, eOwn, eLeft, eRight, bPass
' R16-T0-STRNOTSTART (task 3555, F-5c): stop limits on a steering object that was never started. start()
' would erase them, so each is refused: stopAfterDistance() and stopAfterTime() must return
' ERR_NOT_STARTED, and getError()'s first (steering) result must name it. Nothing moves: no cog exists.
' UNFIXED: both calls returned nothing and silently armed a limit start() then erased (F-5c).
'
' @local eDist - stopAfterDistance(1, DDU_M)'s return
' @local eTime - stopAfterTime(1, DTU_SEC)'s return
' @local eOwn - getError()'s steering result
' @local eLeft - getError()'s left-wheel result (not judged; printed)
' @local eRight - getError()'s right-wheel result (not judged; printed)
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-18,begin,steer_not_started")
    steer.getError()
    eDist := steer.stopAfterDistance(1, steer.DDU_M)
    eTime := steer.stopAfterTime(1, steer.DTU_SEC)
    eOwn, eLeft, eRight := steer.getError()
    bPass := (eDist == motor.ERR_NOT_STARTED) and (eTime == motor.ERR_NOT_STARTED) and (eOwn == motor.ERR_NOT_STARTED)
    debug("T0-18,end,dist_status,", sdec_(eDist), ",time_status,", sdec_(eTime), ",error,", sdec_(eOwn), ",left_error,", sdec_(eLeft), ",right_error,", sdec_(eRight))
    emitCellBool(@"R16-T0-STRNOTSTART", @"3555", @"BOTH", @"LIMIT_REFUSED", TRUE, bPass, 2)

PRI testT0_19() | baseline, startResult, freeRunning, freeStopped, bPass, voltBefore, milliVoltsBefore, voltRunning, milliVoltsRunning, bVoltOk
' R16-T0-STEERCOGS (task 3513): the two-wheel form costs 3 cogs -- two owned drivers and one steering front
' cog -- and stop() returns all of them. The start commands zero speed on both wheels, so nothing turns.
' NOT A DISCRIMINATOR, and stated as such: the unfixed two-wheel shape was also 3 cogs (two drivers plus
' the sense task). The single-motor form, which did change (1 -> 2), is judged by R1-T0-RESTART.
'
' AK / R17-T0-VOLTGET (task 3577): getDriveVoltage() returns the PWR_* value start() was given
' (user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE) and its nominal mV (SF_PACK_MV). The motor object's answer is T0-3's read of its running
' motor; the steering object's must agree while running, and be PWR_Unknown and 0 before its first start().
' Those reads start and stop nothing, and the final getError() drains the not-started code the first records.
' The unfixed library had no such getter, so this cell is COVERAGE of a new member rather than a before/after
' discriminator: it FAILs on a wrong mapping, on a steering forward that disagrees with the wheel, or on a
' not-started answer that claims a voltage. NOMEAS when T0-3's motor never reached ready.
'
' @local baseline - free cogs before start()
' @local startResult - steer.start()'s return (the front cog id, 0..7)
' @local freeRunning - free cogs while started
' @local freeStopped - free cogs after stop()
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict
' @local voltBefore - steer.getDriveVoltage() before start(): the PWR_* value (expected PWR_Unknown)
' @local milliVoltsBefore - its mV (expected 0)
' @local voltRunning - steer.getDriveVoltage() while running: the PWR_* value
' @local milliVoltsRunning - its mV
' @local bVoltOk - R17-T0-VOLTGET's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-19,begin,steer_cogs")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()
    motorA.stop()
    motorB.stop()
    motorP.stop()
    baseline := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    voltBefore, milliVoltsBefore := steer.getDriveVoltage()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := steer.start(T0_SECOND_BASE, T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    freeRunning := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    voltRunning, milliVoltsRunning := steer.getDriveVoltage()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    steer.stop()
    freeStopped := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    steer.getError()
    bPass := (startResult >= SF_COG_LO) and (startResult <= SF_COG_HI) and (freeRunning == baseline - SF_STEER_COGS) and (freeStopped == baseline)
    debug("T0-19,end,start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",free_running,", udec_(freeRunning), ",free_stopped,", udec_(freeStopped))
    emitCellBool(@"R16-T0-STEERCOGS", @"3513", @"BOTH", @"THREE_COGS_RETURNED", TRUE, bPass, 1)

    bVoltOk := (motorVolt == user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE) and (motorMilliVolts == SF_PACK_MV) and (startResult >= SF_COG_LO)
    bVoltOk := bVoltOk and (voltBefore == motor.PWR_Unknown) and (milliVoltsBefore == 0)
    bVoltOk := bVoltOk and (voltRunning == motorVolt) and (milliVoltsRunning == motorMilliVolts)
    debug("T0-19,volt,motor,", sdec_(motorVolt), ",mv,", sdec_(motorMilliVolts), ",steer_before,", sdec_(voltBefore), ",mv,", sdec_(milliVoltsBefore), ",steer_running,", sdec_(voltRunning), ",mv,", sdec_(milliVoltsRunning))
    emitCellBool(@"R17-T0-VOLTGET", @sTaskPromises, @"BOTH", @"CONFIGURED_VOLTAGE", bMotorVoltRead, bVoltOk, VOLT_READS_JUDGED)

PRI testT0_20() | baseIdx, pinBase, pMotorTok, startResult, sampleIdx, ampsSum, amps, meanAmps, pVerdict
' R16-T0-RESTZERO (task 3556, PL-45): getCurrent() at rest reads near 0 on each board. start() samples the
' floated rest zero (~1 s) and getCurrent() nets it out; this averages REST_SAMPLES readings at zero command
' and judges the mean against SF_REST_LO..SF_REST_HI (0.1 mA units). UNFIXED: the LEFT board read about 535
' (0.05 A, Visit 1). The RIGHT board's unfixed offset (~27) already sits inside the band, so only the LEFT
' instance discriminates; that is stated here and in the run sheet.
'
' @local baseIdx - 0 RIGHT (T0_MOTOR_BASE), 1 LEFT (T0_SECOND_BASE)
' @local pinBase - the base under test
' @local pMotorTok - the record's motor field
' @local startResult - start()'s return
' @local sampleIdx - sample loop counter
' @local ampsSum - sum of the readings
' @local amps - one getCurrent() reading, 0.1 mA units
' @local meanAmps - the instance's measured value
' @local pVerdict - PASS, FAIL or NOMEAS

    repeat baseIdx from 0 to 1
        if baseIdx == 0
            pinBase := T0_MOTOR_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"RIGHT"
        else
            pinBase := T0_SECOND_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"LEFT"
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        startResult := motor.start(pinBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        benchLog.cogEventEnd()
        if bWaitReady(startResult)
            ampsSum := 0
            repeat sampleIdx from 1 to REST_SAMPLES
                waitms(REST_SAMPLE_MS)
                amps, _ := motor.getCurrent()
                ampsSum += amps
            meanAmps := ampsSum / REST_SAMPLES
            pVerdict := ((meanAmps >= SF_REST_LO) and (meanAmps <= SF_REST_HI)) ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"
            debug("T0-20,base,", udec_(pinBase), ",mean_amps_x10k,", sdec_(meanAmps))
            emitCellNum(@"R16-T0-RESTZERO", @"3556", pMotorTok, @"REST_AMPS_X10K", TRUE, meanAmps, SF_REST_LO, SF_REST_HI, @"AMPS_X10K", REST_SAMPLES, pVerdict)
        else
            debug("T0-20,base,", udec_(pinBase), ",not_ready,start_return,", sdec_(startResult))
            emitCellNum(@"R16-T0-RESTZERO", @"3556", pMotorTok, @"REST_AMPS_X10K", FALSE, 0, SF_REST_LO, SF_REST_HI, @"AMPS_X10K", 0, 0)
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        motor.stop()
    motor.getError()

PRI testT0_21() | eSetup, amps, watts, eCode, bPass
' R16-T0-NOBOARD (task 3556, PL-25): getCurrent() on a group with no board (P0_P15, the empty group R2-T0-EMPTY
' already probes) returns its documented neutral 0 A / 0 mW and records ERR_BOARD_NOT_DETECTED.
' UNFIXED: nothing was recorded, and a nonzero sense reading divided by -1 read negative. The recorded code
' is the discriminating half: with no driver running the hub sense long is 0 either way.
'
' @local eSetup - motorA.testSetup(P0_P15)'s status
' @local amps - getCurrent()'s current
' @local watts - getCurrent()'s power
' @local eCode - getError() after it (expected ERR_BOARD_NOT_DETECTED)
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-21,begin,no_board")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    eSetup := motorA.testSetup(motorA.PINS_P0_P15, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    motorA.getError()
    amps, watts := motorA.getCurrent()
    eCode := motorA.getError()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    bPass := (eSetup == motorA.NO_ERROR) and (amps == 0) and (watts == 0) and (eCode == motorA.ERR_BOARD_NOT_DETECTED)
    debug("T0-21,end,setup_status,", sdec_(eSetup), ",amps,", sdec_(amps), ",watts,", sdec_(watts), ",error,", sdec_(eCode))
    emitCellBool(@"R16-T0-NOBOARD", @"3556", @"NONE", @"ZERO_AND_CODE", TRUE, bPass, 1)

PRI testT0_22Start() : startResult, eCode, rawMotorCog
' R16-T0-FRONTFAIL (task 3513), the start: runExhaustionPhase() holds all but one cog, so the driver takes
' the last one and the front cog cannot launch. testT0_22Judge() judges it once the spacers are released.
'
' @returns startResult - start()'s return (expected -1)
' @returns eCode - getError() after it (expected ERR_NO_FREE_COG)
' @returns rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog() after it (expected 0)

    debug("T0-22,begin,front_fail")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    eCode := motor.getError()
    rawMotorCog := motor.testGetMotorCog()

PRI testT0_22Judge(baseline, heldCount, startResult, eCode, rawMotorCog, freeAfter) | eClaim, bMeasured, bPass
' R16-T0-FRONTFAIL (task 3513): a start() with exactly one free cog. The driver takes it, the front cog
' cannot launch, and the start must undo itself: return -1, record ERR_NO_FREE_COG, leave no driver
' (testGetMotorCog() 0), give every cog back, and release the pin claim so another instance can take the
' group (motorA.testSetup() on the same group returns NO_ERROR -- PL-36's release, on the new failure
' path). NOMEAS when the spacers could not leave exactly one cog free. Nothing turns: the driver that
' briefly runs commands zero.
' UNFIXED: one cog was enough for start(), which returned a cog id, so the cell FAILs on the return.
'
' @param baseline - free cogs before the spacers
' @param heldCount - spacers held across the start
' @param startResult - start()'s return (expected -1)
' @param eCode - getError() after it (expected ERR_NO_FREE_COG)
' @param rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog() after it (expected 0)
' @param freeAfter - free cogs after the spacers are released

' Local Variables:
' @local eClaim - motorA.testSetup() on the same group (expected NO_ERROR)
' @local bMeasured - the spacers left exactly one cog free
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    eClaim := motorA.testSetup(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    motorA.getError()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()
    bMeasured := (heldCount == baseline - 1)
    bPass := (startResult == -1) and (eCode == motor.ERR_NO_FREE_COG) and (rawMotorCog == 0) and (freeAfter == baseline) and (eClaim == motorA.NO_ERROR)
    debug("T0-22,end,baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",held,", udec_(heldCount), ",start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",error,", sdec_(eCode), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog), ",free_after,", udec_(freeAfter), ",claim_status,", sdec_(eClaim))
    emitCellBool(@"R16-T0-FRONTFAIL", @"3513", @"RIGHT", @"UNDO_NO_LEAK", bMeasured, bPass, 1)

PRI testT0_23() | baseline, startResult, eCode, rawMotorCog, freeAfter, eClaim, bPass
' R17-T0-NOBOARDSTART (task 3570, PL-73): start() on a group with no board (P0_P15, the empty group R2-T0-EMPTY
' already probes), auto-detecting, must be refused: return -1, record ERR_BOARD_NOT_DETECTED, leave no driver
' (testGetMotorCog() 0), take no cog, and release the pin claim (motorA.testSetup() on the same group returns
' NO_ERROR). A board is driven only when detected or forced, because without its revision there is no current
' limit. Nothing is ever driven: the refusal comes before any cog is launched.
' UNFIXED: the start succeeded -- a driver ran on the empty group with no current limit -- so the cell FAILs on
' the return, the recorded code and the cog count.
'
' @local baseline - free cogs before the start
' @local startResult - motorA.start()'s return (expected -1)
' @local eCode - getError() after it (expected ERR_BOARD_NOT_DETECTED)
' @local rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog() after it (expected 0)
' @local freeAfter - free cogs after it (expected baseline)
' @local eClaim - motorA.testSetup() on the same group afterwards (expected NO_ERROR: the claim was released)
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-23,begin,no_board_start")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    motorA.getError()
    baseline := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motorA.start(motorA.PINS_P0_P15, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    eCode := motorA.getError()
    rawMotorCog := motorA.testGetMotorCog()
    freeAfter := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    eClaim := motorA.testSetup(motorA.PINS_P0_P15, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    motorA.getError()
    bPass := (startResult == -1) and (eCode == motorA.ERR_BOARD_NOT_DETECTED) and (rawMotorCog == 0) and (freeAfter == baseline) and (eClaim == motorA.NO_ERROR)
    debug("T0-23,end,start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",error,", sdec_(eCode), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog), ",baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",free_after,", udec_(freeAfter), ",claim_status,", sdec_(eClaim))
    emitCellBool(@"R17-T0-NOBOARDSTART", @"3570", @"NONE", @"REFUSED_NO_LEAK", TRUE, bPass, 1)

PRI bUnitsKmMiOk() : bKmMiOk | eKm, ticksKm, eM, ticksM, eMi, ticksMi, eFt, ticksFt, eCmdKm, armedKm, eCmdMi, armedMi, eHuge, eCmdHuge, keptHuge
' K / R17-T0-KMMI (task 3577), on T0-3's running motor at zero command: kilometres and miles are distance units a
' caller can COMMAND. ticksForDistance() gives 1 km exactly the ticks of M_PER_KM metres and 1 mi exactly those of
' FT_PER_MI feet; stopAfterDistance() accepts both units and arms exactly those ticks; and a distance too large for
' a long is refused with ERR_BAD_COUNT, leaving the armed limit in place. Nothing turns: the limit is armed at rest.
' UNFIXED: the conversion had no KM or MI, so every such call returned ERR_BAD_UNITS and this FAILs at once.
'
' @returns bKmMiOk - TRUE when every conversion, command and refusal held
'
' @local eKm - ticksForDistance(1, DDU_KM)'s status
' @local ticksKm - its ticks
' @local eM - ticksForDistance(M_PER_KM, DDU_M)'s status
' @local ticksM - its ticks
' @local eMi - ticksForDistance(1, DDU_MI)'s status
' @local ticksMi - its ticks
' @local eFt - ticksForDistance(FT_PER_MI, DDU_FT)'s status
' @local ticksFt - its ticks
' @local eCmdKm - stopAfterDistance(1, DDU_KM)'s status
' @local armedKm - the armed limit after it
' @local eCmdMi - stopAfterDistance(1, DDU_MI)'s status
' @local armedMi - the armed limit after it
' @local eHuge - ticksForDistance(POSX, DDU_KM)'s status (expected ERR_BAD_COUNT)
' @local eCmdHuge - stopAfterDistance(POSX, DDU_MI)'s status (expected ERR_BAD_COUNT)
' @local keptHuge - the armed limit after it (expected armedMi)

    eKm, ticksKm := motor.ticksForDistance(1, motor.DDU_KM)
    eM, ticksM := motor.ticksForDistance(M_PER_KM, motor.DDU_M)
    eCmdKm := motor.stopAfterDistance(1, motor.DDU_KM)
    armedKm := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
    eMi, ticksMi := motor.ticksForDistance(1, motor.DDU_MI)
    eFt, ticksFt := motor.ticksForDistance(FT_PER_MI, motor.DDU_FT)
    eCmdMi := motor.stopAfterDistance(1, motor.DDU_MI)
    armedMi := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
    eHuge, _ := motor.ticksForDistance(POSX, motor.DDU_KM)
    eCmdHuge := motor.stopAfterDistance(POSX, motor.DDU_MI)
    keptHuge := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
    motor.getError()                                        ' drain the refusal's recorded code
    bKmMiOk := bUnitOk(@"km", eKm, ticksKm, eM, ticksM, eCmdKm, armedKm)
    bKmMiOk := bUnitOk(@"mi", eMi, ticksMi, eFt, ticksFt, eCmdMi, armedMi) and bKmMiOk
    bKmMiOk := bKmMiOk and (eHuge == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT) and (eCmdHuge == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT) and (keptHuge == armedMi)
    debug("T0-3,huge,status,", sdec_(eHuge), ",cmd_status,", sdec_(eCmdHuge), ",kept,", sdec_(keptHuge))

PRI bUnitOk(pUnit, eUnit, ticksUnit, eRef, ticksRef, eCmd, armedTicks) : bOk
' Judge and print one large unit: its conversion equals its exact equivalent in a smaller unit, and commanding it
' arms exactly those ticks. One debug() record serves both units.
'
' @param pUnit - pointer to the unit's name, printed as the line's tag ("km" or "mi")
' @param eUnit - ticksForDistance(1, unit)'s status
' @param ticksUnit - its ticks
' @param eRef - ticksForDistance() of the same distance in the smaller unit: its status
' @param ticksRef - its ticks
' @param eCmd - stopAfterDistance(1, unit)'s status
' @param armedTicks - the armed limit after it
' @returns bOk - TRUE when every call returned NO_ERROR and all three tick counts agree

    bOk := (eUnit == motor.NO_ERROR) and (eRef == motor.NO_ERROR) and (eCmd == motor.NO_ERROR)
    bOk := bOk and (ticksUnit == ticksRef) and (armedTicks == ticksUnit)
    debug("T0-3,", zstr_(pUnit), ",status,", sdec_(eUnit), ",ticks,", sdec_(ticksUnit), ",ref_status,", sdec_(eRef), ",ref_ticks,", sdec_(ticksRef), ",cmd_status,", sdec_(eCmd), ",armed,", sdec_(armedTicks))

PRI testT0_10() | pinAdcX, xNodeCounts
' C-6b: pin_adc_x_i (base+3) falls inside adc_pins, so the driver already
' samples it as a calibrated, frame-locked ADC every cycle -- it is simply
' never read. Start the REAL driver (rail must be on for this one test) so the
' fourth channel is live, then read it with RQPIN so this harness never steals
' the driver's own acknowledge on a pin the driver cog rdpin's every cycle.
' Commanded speed stays at zero (start() calls setTargetAccel(0) before the
' cog launches), so nothing turns.
'
' start() is called UNTRAPPED (task 3539): a genuine abort is caught by main()'s single top-level trap.
'
' @local pinAdcX - pinbase + 3, the X-node ADC pin
' @local xNodeCounts - RQPIN()'s lower 31 bits (bit 31 is the pin's C flag)

    debug("T0-10,begin,rail_must_be_on,TRUE")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    ' The reading is not gated on start()'s return (AD+: a start whose return read 0 once ran a real cog).
    ' AD+ is fixed and R1-T0-START certifies the return, so the start_return print is retired (task 3574).
    waitms(50)                                              ' let the driver cog reach its running, calibrated state
    pinAdcX := T0_MOTOR_BASE + 3
    xNodeCounts := RQPIN(pinAdcX) & $7FFF_FFFF
    debug("T0-10,end,pin,", udec_(pinAdcX), ",x_node_counts,", udec_(xNodeCounts))
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_15bStart() : startResult, rawMotorCog
' R1-T0-EXHAUST (task 3499), the start: runExhaustionPhase() holds every free cog, so the real start()
' must fail. start() is called UNTRAPPED (task 3539): under total cog exhaustion it returns -1
' gracefully, which is NOT an abort; a genuine abort is caught by main()'s single top-level trap.
'
' @returns startResult - start()'s return under total cog exhaustion
' @returns rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot after the failed start()

    debug("T0-15,begin,exhaust")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    rawMotorCog := motor.testGetMotorCog()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_15bJudge(cogsOccupied, baseline, startResult, rawMotorCog, freeAfter) | bPass
' R1-T0-EXHAUST (task 3499), design SS H.1: runs LAST (runExhaustionPhase()). Count free cogs
' (baseline), occupy every free cog, call the real start(), release the spacers, count free cogs again.
' A BOOL cell (task 3537): measured is TRUE only when start() returns -1 AND testGetMotorCog() == 0 AND
' free cogs after release == baseline, so the suite is never left short a cog; the raw numbers are on
' the T0-15b line.
'
' @param cogsOccupied - spacers that held every free cog across the start
' @param baseline - free cogs before the occupancy
' @param startResult - start()'s return under total cog exhaustion
' @param rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot after the failed start()
' @param freeAfter - free cogs after every spacer is released

' Local Variables:
' @local bPass - this cell's measured value and verdict

    bPass := (startResult == SF_EXHAUST_LO) and (rawMotorCog == 0) and (freeAfter == baseline)
    debug("T0-15b,cogs_occupied,", udec_(cogsOccupied), ",start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog), ",baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",free_after,", udec_(freeAfter))
    emitCellBool(@"R1-T0-EXHAUST", @"3499", @"NONE", @"RET_NEG_NOLEAK", TRUE, bPass, 1)
#endif

#ifdef T0_STOPREASON
PRI testT0_25() | startResult, bReady, eStartErr
' T0-25, stop reasons and the soft-event log (task 3621, R20.1; DRIVER-REPORTING-DESIGN.md SS1, SS2, SS6) -- compiled
' only under -D T0_STOPREASON (its own bench-run.sh tier, t0-stopreason), because every leg drives the RIGHT wheel
' (T0_MOTOR_BASE) and plain t0 promises no motion. UNATTENDED: nothing waits on a person.
'
' THE CELLS, each with the negative that lets it FAIL (SS6):
'   R20-T0-SR-COMMANDED - stopMotor() reads SR_COMMANDED, still 500 ms later; NEGATIVE: every leg's read as its drive
'                          opens is SR_NONE -- six of the seven follow a stop that left a reason, so a reason a new
'                          drive does not clear fails here
'   R20-T0-SR-ATLIMIT   - a time limit reads SR_AT_LIMIT; NEGATIVE: stopMotor() under the same armed limit reads
'                          SR_COMMANDED, and still does after the limit's deadline passes at rest
'   R20-T0-SR-ESTOP     - emergencyCutoff() at speed reads SR_EMERGENCY; NEGATIVE: one at rest after a stop leaves
'                          SR_COMMANDED (first cause wins, and no drive is open)
'   R20-T0-SR-LINKLOST  - the command timeout reads SR_LINK_LOST; NEGATIVE: re-sent drives keep it open (SR_NONE), and
'                          the stopMotor() after them reads SR_COMMANDED
'   R20-T0-EV-STOP      - reading the log after the legs gives exactly seven EV_STOP, 41 42 41 47 41 46 41, in rising
'                          ms; a missing, extra or reordered one fails, and so does any loss
'   R20-T0-EV-LOST      - T0_25_CYCLES drive/stop cycles with nothing read, then a read: EV_LOST first, its value the
'                          events queued past EV_QUEUE_DEPTH (4 when the cycles' 20 stops are all that was queued), then
'                          EV_QUEUE_DEPTH retained, then EV_NONE; EV_NONE before EV_LOST, a wrong count or fewer kept fails
'   R20-T0-EV-TOTAL     - getEventTotal(EV_STOP) is 27 (7 + 20); one that counts only what was read (23) fails
'   R20-T0-EV-2COG      - a helper cog and cog 0 each read the same T0_25_COG_CYCLES stops; a shared cursor gives
'                          one of them fewer, which fails
' A start that does not come up ready leaves every cell NOMEAS, and the start's getError() is printed.
'
' @local startResult - start()'s return
' @local bReady - TRUE when the driver came up ready
' @local eStartErr - getError() after a start that did not come up

    emitCellDecl(@sCellSrCmd, @sTaskReporting)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellSrLimit, @sTaskReporting)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellSrEstop, @sTaskReporting)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellSrLink, @sTaskReporting)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellEvStop, @sTaskReporting)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellEvLost, @sTaskReporting)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellEvTotal, @sTaskReporting)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellEv2Cog, @sTaskReporting)
    debug("T0-25,begin,wheel,RIGHT_P16,power,", udec_(T0_25_POWER), ",legs,", udec_(T0R_LEGS), ",cycles,", udec_(T0_25_CYCLES))

    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    bReady := bWaitReady(startResult)
    eStartErr := motor.getError()                               ' NO_ERROR after a good start; the -1's cause otherwise
    debug("T0-25,start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",ready,", zstr_(bReady ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",error,", sdec_(eStartErr))
    if bReady
        motor.holdAtStop(FALSE)                                 ' coast at rest: the hold's hand-offs are T0-24's, not these legs'
        t0rStopLegs()
        t0rEvLost()
        t0rTwoCog()
    else
        emitCellBool(@sCellSrCmd, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritSrCmd, FALSE, FALSE, 0)
        emitCellBool(@sCellSrLimit, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritSrLimit, FALSE, FALSE, 0)
        emitCellBool(@sCellSrEstop, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritSrEstop, FALSE, FALSE, 0)
        emitCellBool(@sCellSrLink, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritSrLink, FALSE, FALSE, 0)
        emitCellBool(@sCellEvStop, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritEvStop, FALSE, FALSE, 0)
        emitCellBool(@sCellEvLost, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritEvLost, FALSE, FALSE, 0)
        emitCellBool(@sCellEvTotal, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritEvTotal, FALSE, FALSE, 0)
        emitCellBool(@sCellEv2Cog, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritEv2Cog, FALSE, FALSE, 0)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()
    motor.getError()                                            ' drain this cog's slot
    debug("T0-25,end")

PRI t0rStopLegs() | legIdx, legErr[T0R_LEGS], legOpen[T0R_LEGS], legStop[T0R_LEGS], legAfter[T0R_LEGS], bOpensNone, stopBuf[T0_25_EV_STOPS], nStops, nRead, nLost, bEnded, bRising, bOrder
' The four stop-reason cells and R20-T0-EV-STOP: the seven legs in order (t0rLeg(), each printed as T0-25,leg), then
' one read of the log, which must hold exactly their seven EV_STOP in order.
'
' @local legIdx - T0R_LEG_*
' @local legErr - each leg's first non-zero call return, NO_ERROR when every call took
' @local legOpen - each leg's getStopReason() as its drive opened
' @local legStop - ...after its stop
' @local legAfter - ...after its later act
' @local bOpensNone - every leg's open read was SR_NONE and every leg's calls took
' @local stopBuf - the EV_STOP values read, in order
' @local nStops - EV_STOP events read
' @local nRead - events of any kind read
' @local nLost - events the read was told it lost
' @local bEnded - the read ended on EV_NONE
' @local bRising - each EV_STOP's ms was later than the one before
' @local bOrder - exactly T0_25_EV_STOPS EV_STOP, each the one its leg recorded

    bOpensNone := TRUE
    repeat legIdx from 0 to T0R_LEGS - 1
        legErr[legIdx], legOpen[legIdx], legStop[legIdx], legAfter[legIdx] := t0rLeg(legIdx)
        bOpensNone &= (legOpen[legIdx] == motor.SR_NONE) and (legErr[legIdx] == motor.NO_ERROR)
    emitCellBool(@sCellSrCmd, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritSrCmd, TRUE, bOpensNone and (legStop[T0R_LEG_CMD] == motor.SR_COMMANDED) and (legAfter[T0R_LEG_CMD] == motor.SR_COMMANDED), T0R_LEGS + 2)
    emitCellBool(@sCellSrLimit, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritSrLimit, TRUE, (legErr[T0R_LEG_LIMIT] == motor.NO_ERROR) and (legStop[T0R_LEG_LIMIT] == motor.SR_AT_LIMIT) and (legErr[T0R_LEG_LIMIT_NEG] == motor.NO_ERROR) and (legStop[T0R_LEG_LIMIT_NEG] == motor.SR_COMMANDED) and (legAfter[T0R_LEG_LIMIT_NEG] == motor.SR_COMMANDED), 3)
    emitCellBool(@sCellSrEstop, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritSrEstop, TRUE, (legErr[T0R_LEG_ESTOP] == motor.NO_ERROR) and (legStop[T0R_LEG_ESTOP] == motor.SR_EMERGENCY) and (legErr[T0R_LEG_ESTOP_NEG] == motor.NO_ERROR) and (legStop[T0R_LEG_ESTOP_NEG] == motor.SR_COMMANDED) and (legAfter[T0R_LEG_ESTOP_NEG] == motor.SR_COMMANDED), 3)
    emitCellBool(@sCellSrLink, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritSrLink, TRUE, (legErr[T0R_LEG_LINK] == motor.NO_ERROR) and (legStop[T0R_LEG_LINK] == motor.SR_LINK_LOST) and (legErr[T0R_LEG_LINK_NEG] == motor.NO_ERROR) and (legOpen[T0R_LEG_LINK_NEG] == motor.SR_NONE) and (legStop[T0R_LEG_LINK_NEG] == motor.SR_COMMANDED), 3)

    nStops, nRead, nLost, bEnded, bRising, _ := t0rDrain(@"STOP", @stopBuf, T0_25_EV_STOPS)
    bOrder := (nStops == T0_25_EV_STOPS)
    if bOrder
        repeat legIdx from 0 to T0_25_EV_STOPS - 1
            bOrder &= (stopBuf[legIdx] == t0rWantStop(legIdx))
    emitCellBool(@sCellEvStop, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritEvStop, TRUE, bOrder and bRising and bEnded and (nLost == 0), T0_25_EV_STOPS)

PRI t0rLeg(legIdx) : eErr, srOpen, srStop, srAfter | startMs, bRest
' One stop-reason leg (this CON's T0R_LEG_* notes say what each does and reads), printed as T0-25,leg. Every leg ends
' with the driver at rest (bounded) and this cog's error slot drained, so the next leg starts from rest and clean.
'
' @param legIdx - T0R_LEG_*
' @returns eErr - the first non-zero return of the leg's calls, NO_ERROR when every one took
' @returns srOpen - getStopReason() as the drive opened (LINK_NEG: after its re-sent drives)
' @returns srStop - getStopReason() after the stop
' @returns srAfter - getStopReason() after the leg's later act (the wait, the clear, the e-stop at rest)
'
' @local startMs - getms() when LINK_NEG's re-sent drives began
' @local bRest - the driver read DCS_STOPPED at the leg's end

    eErr := motor.NO_ERROR
    case legIdx
        T0R_LEG_LIMIT, T0R_LEG_LIMIT_NEG:
            eErr := motor.stopAfterTime(T0_25_LIMIT_MS, motor.DTU_MILLISEC)     ' armed before the drive it limits
        T0R_LEG_LINK:
            eErr := motor.setCommandTimeout(T0_25_TIMEOUT_MS)                   ' left on through LINK_NEG
    eErr := t0rFirstErr(eErr, motor.driveAtPower(T0_25_POWER))
    srOpen := motor.getStopReason()
    case legIdx
        T0R_LEG_CMD:
            waitms(T0_25_RUN_MS)
            motor.stopMotor()
            srStop := motor.getStopReason()
            waitms(T0_25_STICKY_MS)
            srAfter := motor.getStopReason()
        T0R_LEG_LIMIT:
            waitms(T0_25_LIMIT_MS)                                              ' the limit's stop is written by then: it begins early by the ramp
            bT0rRest()
            srStop := motor.getStopReason()
            srAfter := srStop
        T0R_LEG_LIMIT_NEG:
            waitms(T0_25_EARLY_MS)
            motor.stopMotor()
            srStop := motor.getStopReason()
            waitms(T0_25_LIMIT_MS)                                              ' past the armed deadline: it fires at rest, no drive open
            srAfter := motor.getStopReason()
        T0R_LEG_ESTOP:
            waitms(T0_25_RUN_MS)
            motor.emergencyCutoff()
            srStop := motor.getStopReason()
            eErr := t0rFirstErr(eErr, motor.clearEmergency())
            srAfter := motor.getStopReason()
        T0R_LEG_ESTOP_NEG:
            waitms(T0_25_RUN_MS)
            motor.stopMotor()
            srStop := motor.getStopReason()
            bT0rRest()
            motor.emergencyCutoff()                                             ' at rest, after the stop: no drive is open
            srAfter := motor.getStopReason()
            eErr := t0rFirstErr(eErr, motor.clearEmergency())
        T0R_LEG_LINK:
            waitms(T0_25_SILENT_MS)                                             ' no command: the timeout stops it
            srStop := motor.getStopReason()
            srAfter := srStop
        T0R_LEG_LINK_NEG:
            startMs := getms()
            repeat while (getms() - startMs) < T0_25_SILENT_MS
                waitms(T0_25_REFRESH_MS)
                eErr := t0rFirstErr(eErr, motor.driveAtPower(T0_25_POWER))
            srOpen := motor.getStopReason()                                     ' still open: no timeout fired on a live link
            motor.stopMotor()
            srStop := motor.getStopReason()
            srAfter := srStop
            eErr := t0rFirstErr(eErr, motor.setCommandTimeout(motor.CMD_TIMEOUT_OFF))
    bRest := bT0rRest()
    motor.getError()                                                            ' LINK's ERR_COMMAND_TIMEOUT, or nothing
    debug("T0-25,leg,", zstr_(t0rLegName(legIdx)), ",err,", sdec_(eErr), ",sr_open,", udec_(srOpen), ",sr_stop,", udec_(srStop), ",sr_after,", udec_(srAfter), ",rest,", zstr_(bRest ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

PRI t0rEvLost() | bBase, eKind, totBefore, stopsBefore, eErr, cycleIdx, totAfter, stopsAfter, queued, nStops, nRead, nLost, bEnded, firstKind, nKept, nTotal
' R20-T0-EV-LOST and R20-T0-EV-TOTAL. First the log is read to EV_NONE with every kind's total taken just before the
' read that returns EV_NONE -- so no event can fall between the baseline and the cursor: one queued after the totals
' is either returned by that read (and the baseline is taken again) or counted in queued below. Then T0_25_CYCLES
' drive/stop cycles with nothing read, and one read: EV_LOST first, valued at the events queued past
' EV_QUEUE_DEPTH, then EV_QUEUE_DEPTH kept, then EV_NONE. The cycles' own EV_STOP total must be T0_25_CYCLES.
' Pre-registered (SS6): the cycles' 20 stops are all that is queued, so EV_LOST 4, then 16 EV_STOP.
'
' @local bBase - the log was read to EV_NONE, so the baseline is exact
' @local eKind - a read's kind
' @local totBefore - every counted kind's total at the baseline
' @local stopsBefore - EV_STOP's total at the baseline
' @local eErr - the cycles' first non-zero drive return
' @local cycleIdx - 1..T0_25_CYCLES
' @local totAfter - every counted kind's total after the cycles
' @local stopsAfter - EV_STOP's total after them
' @local queued - events queued across the cycles, of any kind
' @local nStops - EV_STOP events the read returned
' @local nRead - events of any kind it returned, EV_LOST among them
' @local nLost - the value EV_LOST reported
' @local bEnded - the read ended on EV_NONE
' @local firstKind - the kind the read returned first
' @local nKept - events returned after the EV_LOST
' @local nTotal - getEventTotal(EV_STOP) at the end

    bBase := FALSE
    repeat T0_25_DRAIN_MAX
        totBefore := t0rTotalAll()
        stopsBefore := motor.getEventTotal(motor.EV_STOP)
        eKind, _, _ := motor.getEvent()
        if eKind == motor.EV_NONE
            bBase := TRUE
            quit
    eErr := motor.NO_ERROR
    repeat cycleIdx from 1 to T0_25_CYCLES
        eErr := t0rFirstErr(eErr, motor.driveAtPower(T0_25_POWER))
        waitms(T0_25_CYCLE_MS)
        motor.stopMotor()
        waitms(T0_25_CYCLE_MS)
    bT0rRest()
    totAfter := t0rTotalAll()
    stopsAfter := motor.getEventTotal(motor.EV_STOP)
    queued := totAfter - totBefore
    nStops, nRead, nLost, bEnded, _, firstKind := t0rDrain(@"LOST", 0, 0)
    nKept := (nRead - 1) #> 0
    debug("T0-25,lost,base,", zstr_(bBase ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",queued,", sdec_(queued), ",cycle_stops,", sdec_(stopsAfter - stopsBefore), ",first_kind,", udec_(firstKind), ",lost,", sdec_(nLost), ",kept,", sdec_(nKept), ",kept_stops,", udec_(nStops), ",ended,", zstr_(bEnded ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",err,", sdec_(eErr))
    emitCellBool(@sCellEvLost, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritEvLost, bBase, (eErr == motor.NO_ERROR) and (stopsAfter - stopsBefore == T0_25_CYCLES) and (queued > motor.EV_QUEUE_DEPTH) and (firstKind == motor.EV_LOST) and (nLost == queued - motor.EV_QUEUE_DEPTH) and (nKept == motor.EV_QUEUE_DEPTH) and bEnded, 3)
    nTotal := motor.getEventTotal(motor.EV_STOP)
    debug("T0-25,total,ev_stop,", sdec_(nTotal), ",want,", udec_(T0_25_EV_STOPS + T0_25_CYCLES))
    emitCellBool(@sCellEvTotal, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritEvTotal, TRUE, nTotal == T0_25_EV_STOPS + T0_25_CYCLES, 1)

PRI t0rTwoCog() | helperCog, startMs, bHelperReady, eErr, cycleIdx, nStops, nRead, nLost, bEnded, bHelperDone
' R20-T0-EV-2COG: a helper cog (t0rHelper()) reads the log to EV_NONE and says so; cog 0 does the same, then makes
' T0_25_COG_CYCLES drive/stop cycles and releases the helper; both then read, at the same time, each through its own
' cursor, and each must read exactly T0_25_COG_CYCLES EV_STOP with nothing lost. NOMEAS when the helper never started
' or never reported. The helper is stopped by this cog, in a quiet window, whatever happened.
'
' @local helperCog - cogspin()'s return; < 0 when no cog was free
' @local startMs - getms() when a handshake wait began
' @local bHelperReady - the helper caught up before the cycles
' @local eErr - the cycles' first non-zero drive return
' @local cycleIdx - 1..T0_25_COG_CYCLES
' @local nStops - EV_STOP events cog 0 read after the cycles
' @local nRead - events of any kind cog 0 read then
' @local nLost - events cog 0 was told it lost
' @local bEnded - cog 0's read ended on EV_NONE
' @local bHelperDone - the helper reported its counts

    bT0rReady := FALSE
    bT0rGo := FALSE
    bT0rDone := FALSE
    t0rDrain(@"CATCHUP", 0, 0)                                  ' cog 0 at the head too, before the cycles
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    helperCog := cogspin(NEWCOG, t0rHelper(), @t0rStack)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    startMs := getms()
    repeat while (helperCog >= 0) and (bT0rReady == FALSE) and ((getms() - startMs) < T0_25_HANDSHAKE_MS)
        waitms(READY_POLL_MS)
    bHelperReady := bT0rReady
    eErr := motor.NO_ERROR
    nStops := 0
    nRead := 0
    nLost := 0
    bEnded := FALSE
    if bHelperReady
        repeat cycleIdx from 1 to T0_25_COG_CYCLES
            eErr := t0rFirstErr(eErr, motor.driveAtPower(T0_25_POWER))
            waitms(T0_25_CYCLE_MS)
            motor.stopMotor()
            waitms(T0_25_CYCLE_MS)
        bT0rRest()
        bT0rGo := TRUE                                          ' the helper reads now, while cog 0 reads too
        nStops, nRead, nLost, bEnded, _, _ := t0rDrain(@"TWOCOG", 0, 0)
        startMs := getms()
        repeat while (bT0rDone == FALSE) and ((getms() - startMs) < T0_25_HANDSHAKE_MS)
            waitms(READY_POLL_MS)
    bHelperDone := bT0rDone
    if helperCog >= 0
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        cogstop(helperCog)
    debug("T0-25,twocog,helper_cog,", sdec_(helperCog), ",ready,", zstr_(bHelperReady ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",done,", zstr_(bHelperDone ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",main_stops,", udec_(nStops), ",helper_stops,", udec_(t0rHelperStops), ",main_reads,", udec_(nRead), ",helper_reads,", udec_(t0rHelperReads), ",err,", sdec_(eErr))
    emitCellBool(@sCellEv2Cog, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritEv2Cog, bHelperReady and bHelperDone, (eErr == motor.NO_ERROR) and (nStops == T0_25_COG_CYCLES) and (t0rHelperStops == T0_25_COG_CYCLES) and bEnded and (nLost == 0) and bT0rHelperClean, 2)

PRI t0rHelper() | eKind, nValue, bLost
' The helper reader cog of R20-T0-EV-2COG (its own cog; prints nothing). It reads the log to EV_NONE -- its cursor
' starts at 0, so it is told EV_LOST and then reads what is kept -- and says it is ready; once cog 0 says go, it reads
' again to EV_NONE, counting EV_STOP, and reports. Then it parks until cog 0 stops it.
'
' @local eKind - a read's kind
' @local nValue - its value
' @local bLost - the counted read was told it lost events

    repeat T0_25_DRAIN_MAX
        eKind, _, _ := motor.getEvent()
        if eKind == motor.EV_NONE
            quit
    bT0rReady := TRUE
    repeat until bT0rGo
        waitms(1)
    t0rHelperStops := 0
    t0rHelperReads := 0
    bT0rHelperClean := FALSE
    bLost := FALSE
    repeat T0_25_DRAIN_MAX
        eKind, _, nValue := motor.getEvent()
        if eKind == motor.EV_NONE
            bT0rHelperClean := (bLost == FALSE)
            quit
        t0rHelperReads += 1
        if eKind == motor.EV_LOST
            bLost := TRUE
        elseif eKind == motor.EV_STOP
            t0rHelperStops += 1
    bT0rDone := TRUE
    repeat
        waitms(T0_25_CYCLE_MS)

PRI t0rDrain(pPhase, pStops, maxStops) : nStops, nRead, nLost, bEnded, bRising, firstKind | eKind, nMs, nValue, lastStopMs
' Read this cog's log to EV_NONE (at most T0_25_DRAIN_MAX reads), printing every event as T0-25,ev. One debug()
' record serves every read in T0-25 (DBG-2).
'
' @param pPhase - pointer to the phase's name, printed on each event
' @param pStops - where to store the EV_STOP values in order, 0 for nowhere
' @param maxStops - how many values pStops holds
' @returns nStops - EV_STOP events read
' @returns nRead - events of any kind read, EV_LOST among them
' @returns nLost - EV_LOST's values summed
' @returns bEnded - the read ended on EV_NONE inside the bound
' @returns bRising - each EV_STOP's ms was later than the previous one's
' @returns firstKind - the first kind read, EV_NONE when there was none
'
' @local eKind - a read's kind
' @local nMs - its getms() stamp
' @local nValue - its value
' @local lastStopMs - the previous EV_STOP's ms

    nStops := 0
    nRead := 0
    nLost := 0
    bEnded := FALSE
    bRising := TRUE
    firstKind := motor.EV_NONE
    lastStopMs := 0
    repeat T0_25_DRAIN_MAX
        eKind, nMs, nValue := motor.getEvent()
        if nRead == 0
            firstKind := eKind
        if eKind == motor.EV_NONE
            bEnded := TRUE
            quit
        nRead += 1
        debug("T0-25,ev,", zstr_(pPhase), ",n,", udec_(nRead), ",kind,", udec_(eKind), ",ms,", udec_(nMs), ",value,", sdec_(nValue))
        if eKind == motor.EV_LOST
            nLost += nValue
        elseif eKind == motor.EV_STOP
            if (nStops > 0) and ((nMs - lastStopMs) <= 0)
                bRising := FALSE
            lastStopMs := nMs
            if nStops < maxStops
                long[pStops][nStops] := nValue
            nStops += 1

PRI bT0rRest() : bRest | startMs
' Wait, bounded by T0_25_REST_MS, for the driver to read DCS_STOPPED.
'
' @returns bRest - TRUE when it did
'
' @local startMs - getms() when the wait began

    startMs := getms()
    repeat until (motor.getDriverState() == motor.DCS_STOPPED) or ((getms() - startMs) >= T0_25_REST_MS)
        waitms(READY_POLL_MS)
    bRest := (motor.getDriverState() == motor.DCS_STOPPED)

PRI t0rTotalAll() : nSum | eKind
' Every counted kind's getEventTotal(), summed: the events queued since start(), read or not, lost or not.
'
' @returns nSum - the sum over EV_STOP .. EV_FOLDBACK
'
' @local eKind - EV_STOP .. EV_FOLDBACK

    nSum := 0
    repeat eKind from motor.EV_STOP to motor.EV_FOLDBACK
        nSum += motor.getEventTotal(eKind)

PRI t0rFirstErr(eFirst, eNext) : eErr
' The first non-zero of two call returns.
'
' @param eFirst - the earlier return
' @param eNext - the later one
' @returns eErr - eFirst when it is not NO_ERROR, else eNext

    eErr := eFirst
    if eErr == motor.NO_ERROR
        eErr := eNext

PRI t0rWantStop(stopIdx) : eReason
' The SR_* the stopIdx'th EV_STOP must carry: the legs' stops in T0R_LEG_* order -- ESTOP_NEG's e-stop at rest records
' none, so its one stop is the stopMotor() before it.
'
' @param stopIdx - 0..T0_25_EV_STOPS-1
' @returns eReason - SR_COMMANDED, SR_AT_LIMIT, SR_EMERGENCY or SR_LINK_LOST

    eReason := lookupz(stopIdx : motor.SR_COMMANDED, motor.SR_AT_LIMIT, motor.SR_COMMANDED, motor.SR_EMERGENCY, motor.SR_COMMANDED, motor.SR_LINK_LOST, motor.SR_COMMANDED)

PRI t0rLegName(legIdx) : pName
' The name a leg is printed under.
'
' @param legIdx - T0R_LEG_*
' @returns pName - pointer to the name

    pName := lookupz(legIdx : @"COMMANDED", @"ATLIMIT", @"ATLIMIT_NEG", @"ESTOP", @"ESTOP_NEG", @"LINKLOST", @"LINKLOST_NEG")
#endif

#ifdef T0_HAND
PRI testT0_12() | keyCode, bArmed, hallPin, hallCode, priorCode, transitions, illegalCount, pollIdx, pos
' T0-12, hand-rotation anchor -- SEPARABLE, compiled only under -D T0_HAND
' (its own bench-run.sh tier, t0-hand), so the unattended T0 run never waits
' on a person. The operator presses S, turns the right wheel by hand exactly
' T0_12_REVOLUTIONS revolutions in the direction T0_12_TOLD_CCW names, then
' presses SPACE; no other key starts or stops the count. It anchors 90 hall transitions per revolution and
' 5.763 mm/tick (isp_bldc_motor.spin2 hall tics per rotation, and
' DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md SS A.5-b), and, per PL-39, ties the
' instructed direction to the sign of the tick change and the hall sequence
' observed. No sign-off cell -- confirmed against
' DOCs/analyses/bench/SIGNOFF-MANIFEST.tsv, which carries no T0-12 row; this
' is an operator-attended reference measurement, not a graded cell.
'
' No driver cog runs here, so the driver-maintained tick count
' (getRawHallTicks() reads the driver's pos) cannot move. This harness counts
' the transitions itself: it reads the three hall inputs (base+5..base+7)
' with pinread() every T0_12_POLL_MS. They are plain inputs -- nothing ever
' raises their DIR (task 3524) -- not smart pins, so pinread() is safe and no
' RDPIN is involved. Any change of the 3-bit code counts as one transition,
' and entering an illegal code (%000 or %111, symmetric under any bit order)
' is also counted separately. At a 1 ms poll a hand turn would need more than
' 5 revolutions per second (450 transitions per second, one every ~2.2 ms)
' before two transitions could fall between polls. `pos` accumulates the
' signed delta from t0hHallDeltas65 on every transition (PL-39); the table's
' own construction contributes 0 for any transition touching an illegal code,
' so no separate guard is needed.
'
' The pc_key() keypress-read pattern (own backtick, last in its debug()
' statement, ~100 ms poll matching PC_KEY's own latch window) already follows
' DOCs/REF-NO-COMMIT/dbg-display-theory/DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS7.
' The panel draws via the same doc's SS2-SS6 LAYER/CROP/UPDATE technique
' (t0hSetupPanel(), t0hDrawPanel()) from the committed assets
' tools/gen_t0hand_assets.py writes; rendering is shown only on the rig.
'
' @local keyCode - pc_key()'s last-read key code, 0 when none is latched
' @local bArmed - TRUE once a 0 reading has been seen (so a held key cannot register twice)
' @local hallPin - base+5, the lowest of the three hall inputs
' @local hallCode - the 3-bit hall code just read
' @local priorCode - the previous poll's 3-bit hall code
' @local transitions - hall code changes counted since the start keypress
' @local illegalCount - entries into %000 or %111 since the start keypress
' @local pollIdx - polls since the start keypress, paces the key checks, progress lines and redraws
' @local pos - signed tick position accumulated from t0hHallDeltas65 (PL-39)

    t0hSetupPanel()
    t0hDrawPanel(T0H_STATE_WAITING, 0, 0)
    debug("T0-12,begin,told_direction,", zstr_(T0_12_TOLD_CCW ? @"CCW_FROM_HUB" : @"CW_FROM_HUB"), ",revolutions,", udec_(T0_12_REVOLUTIONS), ",wheel,RIGHT_P16,prompt,press_S_then_turn_the_wheel_by_hand_then_press_SPACE")

    hallPin := T0_MOTOR_BASE + T0_12_HALL_OFFSET

    bArmed := FALSE
    repeat
        debug(`bench `pc_key(@keyCode))
        if keyCode == 0
            bArmed := TRUE
        if bArmed and ((keyCode == T0_12_KEY_START) or (keyCode == T0_12_KEY_START_LC))
            quit
        waitms(T0_12_KEY_WAIT_MS)

    priorCode := pinread(hallPin addpins T0_12_HALL_SPAN)
    transitions := 0
    illegalCount := 0
    pollIdx := 0
    pos := 0
    t0hDrawPanel(T0H_STATE_COUNTING, transitions, illegalCount)
    debug("T0-12,started,hall_pin,", udec_(hallPin), ",hall_code,", udec_(priorCode), ",told_direction,", zstr_(T0_12_TOLD_CCW ? @"CCW_FROM_HUB" : @"CW_FROM_HUB"), ",prompt,press_SPACE_to_stop_count")

    bArmed := FALSE
    repeat
        hallCode := pinread(hallPin addpins T0_12_HALL_SPAN)
        if hallCode <> priorCode
            transitions += 1
            if (hallCode == %000) or (hallCode == %111)
                illegalCount += 1
            pos += t0hHallDeltas65[(priorCode << 3) | hallCode] SIGNX 7    ' BYTE reads 0..255; SIGNX 7 gives -1/0/+1
            priorCode := hallCode
        pollIdx += 1
        if (pollIdx +// T0_12_KEY_POLLS) == 0
            debug(`bench `pc_key(@keyCode))
            if keyCode == 0
                bArmed := TRUE
            if bArmed and (keyCode == T0_12_KEY_STOP)
                quit
        if (pollIdx +// T0_12_PRINT_POLLS) == 0
            debug("T0-12,running,transitions,", udec_(transitions), ",illegal,", udec_(illegalCount), ",pos,", sdec_(pos))
            t0hDrawPanel(T0H_STATE_COUNTING, transitions, illegalCount)
        waitms(T0_12_POLL_MS)

    t0hDrawPanel(T0H_STATE_DONE, transitions, illegalCount)
    debug("T0-12,end,transitions,", udec_(transitions), ",illegal,", udec_(illegalCount), ",pos,", sdec_(pos), ",final_hall_code,", udec_(priorCode), ",told_direction,", zstr_(T0_12_TOLD_CCW ? @"CCW_FROM_HUB" : @"CW_FROM_HUB"), ",note,expect_90_per_revolution_(5.763_mm_per_tick)")

PRI t0hSetupPanel()
' Create the T0-12 panel window and load its layers -- crop-and-overlay technique,
' DOCs/REF-NO-COMMIT/dbg-display-theory/DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS2 and SS6 step 4,
' as drawn on this bench by test_bench_char.spin2's since-removed panel
' (DOCs/analyses/bench/2026-09-12/debug_260912-153807.log:19, LAYER/CROP 1/UPDATE sequence).
' Layer numbers and geometry are the T0H_* CON constants tools/gen_t0hand_assets.py also prints;
' the two must stay in sync (same discipline as tools/gen_bench_char_assets.py).
'
' The assets t0h_bg.bmp, t0h_state.bmp and t0h_digits.bmp are generated by
' `python3 tools/gen_t0hand_assets.py` and committed beside this file.

    debug(`PLOT bench TITLE 'T0-12 hand-rotation anchor' SIZE 420 240 POS 60 80 HIDEXY UPDATE)
    debug(`bench LAYER 1 't0h_bg.bmp')
    debug(`bench LAYER 2 't0h_state.bmp')
    debug(`bench LAYER 3 't0h_digits.bmp')
    debug(`bench crop 1)
    debug(`bench update)

PRI t0hDrawPanel(stateIdx, transitions, illegalCount) | divisor, digitVal, destX, colIdx
' Compose one panel frame -- state word, transitions readout, illegal readout -- then one
' UPDATE (DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS2, "batch all crops, then one update"). Called
' only at each state change and every T0_12_PRINT_POLLS polls (~500 ms) from testT0_12()'s
' counting loop -- far below the 1 ms hall-poll rate, so it cannot starve pinread() polling.
'
' @param stateIdx - T0H_STATE_WAITING / T0H_STATE_COUNTING / T0H_STATE_DONE
' @param transitions - hall-code-change count to render (T0H_TRANS_COUNT digits, leading-zero suppressed)
' @param illegalCount - illegal-code-entry count to render (T0H_ILL_COUNT digits, leading-zero suppressed)
' @local divisor - selects the digit column currently being extracted (1000, 100, 10, 1, ...)
' @local digitVal - the digit value 0..9 for the current column
' @local destX - destination X for the current column's blit
' @local colIdx - loop index (digit column, most-significant first)

    debug(`bench crop 2 `(0, stateIdx * T0H_STATE_H, T0H_STATE_W, T0H_STATE_H, T0H_STATE_X, T0H_STATE_Y))

    divisor := 1000
    repeat colIdx from 0 to T0H_TRANS_COUNT - 1
        destX := T0H_TRANS_X + (colIdx * T0H_TRANS_PITCH)
        if (divisor == 1) or (transitions >= divisor)
            digitVal := (transitions / divisor) // 10
            debug(`bench crop 3 `(digitVal * T0H_DGT_W, 0, T0H_DGT_W, T0H_DGT_H, destX, T0H_TRANS_Y))
        else
            debug(`bench crop 3 `(T0H_DGT_BLANK * T0H_DGT_W, 0, T0H_DGT_W, T0H_DGT_H, destX, T0H_TRANS_Y))
        divisor /= 10

    divisor := 100
    repeat colIdx from 0 to T0H_ILL_COUNT - 1
        destX := T0H_ILL_X + (colIdx * T0H_ILL_PITCH)
        if (divisor == 1) or (illegalCount >= divisor)
            digitVal := (illegalCount / divisor) // 10
            debug(`bench crop 3 `(digitVal * T0H_DGT_W, 0, T0H_DGT_W, T0H_DGT_H, destX, T0H_ILL_Y))
        else
            debug(`bench crop 3 `(T0H_DGT_BLANK * T0H_DGT_W, 0, T0H_DGT_W, T0H_DGT_H, destX, T0H_ILL_Y))
        divisor /= 10

    debug(`bench update)
#endif

#ifdef T0_STOPMODE
PRI testT0_24() | seqPos, startResult, bReady, workerCog
' T0-24, stop-state hand test -- SEPARABLE, compiled only under -D T0_STOPMODE (its own
' bench-run.sh tier, t0-stopmode), so the unattended T0 run never waits on a person and never
' drives a motor. It is the run-time proof owed by task 3568 (DOCs/plans/STOP-STATE-DESIGN.md
' SS5, PL-89): the driver now names one bridge state per stop path, and only a hand on the wheel
' can say which state the hardware actually reached. REBUILT task 3607 (PL-115/PL-116) with the hold
' rows of task 3608 (DRIVER_REV 8), its instrument rebuilt by task 3617 (PL-123), and its
' interaction rebuilt by task 3619 (PL-127, DOCs/plans/T0-24-INTERACTION-DESIGN.md).
'
' EIGHT ROWS, each on the RIGHT wheel (T0_MOTOR_BASE). Semantic ids (T0_24_ROW_*) never move;
' t0sRowOrder (a DAT table, picked by -D T0_24_FLT_FIRST) is the only thing that reorders them:
'   HOLDRISE    pushed and held displaced            predicted the hold's duty rises to its ceiling
'   HOLDSLIP    pushed past a low ceiling             predicted HS_SLIPPED, a hand-off to the short
'   HOLDLIMIT   a sustained push at the ceiling       predicted HS_LIMITED after the time limit
'   COAST       holdAtStop(FALSE) + stopMotor()      predicted BR_COAST, a freewheel
'   ESTOP       spun free; the program applies       predicted BR_SHORT, a dynamic brake
'               emergencyCutoff() at the band entry  (task 3617: a hand cannot spin a short into the band)
'   FLTCOAST    a forced fault under SM_FLOAT         predicted BR_COAST
'   FLTHOLD     a forced fault under SM_BRAKE         predicted BR_SHORT
'   COGSTOP     stop()                                the pins released: the free yardstick, ALWAYS LAST
' Each hold row re-arms the hold first and runs only from HS_HOLDING at displacement 0 (PL-123 item 1).
' Every stop row is read as band_ticks, the ticks from T0_24_BAND_RATE to rest (PL-123 item 2).
' COGSTOP is always last because stop() ends the driver cog; FLTCOAST/FLTHOLD are the only rows
' that drive under power. -D T0_24_FLT_FIRST (PL-116's discriminator) runs FLTCOAST/FLTHOLD ahead
' of ESTOP.
'
' WHY ESTOP ALSO ANSWERS "DID THE OLD BUILD BRAKE IN FLOAT?" (STOP-STATE-DESIGN.md SS7's open
' question, settled BY CONSTRUCTION). BR_SHORT is written as `wypin #0, drive_pins` on all six
' pins -- the identical instruction the old `driveoff = 1` path ran for FLOAT at rest. So this row
' measures, on the fixed binary, the very state the old build put a floated wheel into.
'
' WHY THE OPERATOR NEVER JUDGES A ROW (overlay P7). Every action is a TITLED BUTTON, and a click only
' sequences the row or ends a measurement; it is an input, not an opinion, and no cell reads it.
' Every verdict comes from the hall counter, the driver's own state, or getHoldStatus()/testGetHold().
'
' THE COGS. Cog 0 runs the panel and the row sequence (t0sRunRow()); the measure cog (t0sWorker())
' does every job that touches the wheel. Cog 0 starts and stops every cog itself -- start(), the
' measure cog, and COGSTOP's stop() -- each in its own quiet window (PLOT-DISPLAY-RULES.md rule 9).
'
' FREEREF IS READ FIRST (INS-14): t0sEmitCells() prints the free-yardstick cell before any other,
' so the log shows the instrument proved it can report a coast before any other cell is trusted.
'
' @local seqPos - position in THIS run's execution order, 0-based
' @local startResult - start()'s return
' @local bReady - TRUE when the driver came up ready, so the rows can run at all
' @local workerCog - the measure cog's id, or -1 when none could start

    t0sSetupPanel()
    emitCellDecl(@sCellHoldRise, @sTaskHoldRows)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellHoldSlip, @sTaskHoldRows)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellHoldLimit, @sTaskHoldRows)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellRestCoast, @sTaskStopMode)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellRestShort, @sTaskStopMode)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellStopGap, @sTaskStopMode)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellFltCoast, @sTaskStopMode)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellFltShort, @sTaskStopMode)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellFltGap, @sTaskStopMode)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellFreeRef, @sTaskStopMode)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellEvHold, @sTaskReporting)                 ' task 3621: the hold's hand-offs as events (rows 1-3)
    debug("T0-24,begin,wheel,RIGHT_P16,rows,", udec_(T0_24_ROW_COUNT), ",fault_power,", udec_(T0_24_FLT_POWER), ",prompt,each_row_is_previewed_and_waits_for_the_operator")

    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    bReady := bWaitReady(startResult)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    workerCog := cogspin(NEWCOG, t0sWorker(), @t0wStack)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    debug("T0-24,cogs,start_result,", sdec_(startResult), ",ready,", zstr_(bReady ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",measure_cog,", sdec_(workerCog))
    if bReady and (workerCog >= 0)
        repeat seqPos from 0 to T0_24_ROW_COUNT - 1
            t0sRunRow(t0sRowOrder[seqPos], seqPos + 1)
    else
        debug("T0-24,not_ready,start_result,", sdec_(startResult), ",measure_cog,", sdec_(workerCog), ",note,every_cell_is_NOMEAS")
    t0sEmitCells()
    if bReady and (workerCog >= 0)
        t0sDrawSpecial(T0S_NAME_ALLDONE, T0S_B_ALLDONE, T0S_CARD_ALLDONE, T0S_ST_CELLS_LOGGED)
    else
        t0sDrawSpecial(T0S_NAME_NOTREADY, T0S_B_NOTREADY, T0S_CARD_NOTREADY, T0S_ST_NOT_READY)
    waitms(T0_24_ALLDONE_MS)                                    ' the last screen stays up before the session ends
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    if workerCog >= 0
        cogstop(workerCog)
    motor.stop()                                                ' COGSTOP already stopped it on a full run; harmless twice,
    motor.getError()                                            '  and it is the only release on the not-ready path
    debug("T0-24,end")

PRI t0sRunRow(rowIdx, seqNum) | runNum, btn, bRan, whyShown, res1, res2, bFirst, introSt
' One row, as a lesson (DOCs/plans/T0-24-INTERACTION-DESIGN.md SS4): the INTRO screen previews the
' whole row and waits for START ROW. Then SETUP, ACT and RESULT run, as often as he chooses REDO ROW.
' The RESULT screen waits for NEXT ROW (FINISH on the last row) or REDO ROW. Nothing here judges:
' t0sEmitCells() does that once, at the end, from each row's last run, because three of the cells
' compare one row with another.
'
' THE PANEL TESTS (PL-135). On a row's first run, a (row, phase) with an entry in t0sTestTab shows
' that screen instead, which draws only the control that performs one deliberate act. Asked for in
' card text alone, none of the three was made (PL-131). Row 1's intro first shows the grey box and no
' button, and moves on only when a click lands on it, which the log reads hit,MISS. Row 4's first
' RESULT and row 6's draw REDO ROW only, so each row runs twice. Row 6's first ACT draws ABORT only,
' as every powered ACT does, under a card that asks for it. Later runs are the normal screens.
'
' @param rowIdx - which row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @param seqNum - this run's 1-based position -- what the panel, the log AND the runner banner
'                 all call this row (PLOT-DISPLAY-RULES.md rule 10: one numbering)
'
' @local runNum - this row's run, 1-based: a REDO ROW is the next run
' @local btn - the RESULT screen's answer, T0S_BT_*
' @local bRan - TRUE when SETUP reached the row's state and ACT ran
' @local whyShown - the RESULT phrase, T0S_ST_*
' @local res1 - the RESULT readings, -1 when there is none
' @local res2
' @local bFirst - TRUE on the row's first run, when its panel-test screens are shown
' @local introSt - the normal INTRO screen's phrase: the grey box's click acknowledged, or the plain wait

    introSt := T0S_ST_WAIT_START
    if bT0sHasTest(rowIdx, T0S_PH_INTRO)
        t0sUiWait(rowIdx, seqNum, T0S_PH_INTRO, T0S_ST_WAIT_MISS, -1, -1, FALSE, TRUE) ' no button: only the grey box's click ends it
        introSt := T0S_ST_MISS_GOT
    t0sUiWait(rowIdx, seqNum, T0S_PH_INTRO, introSt, -1, -1, FALSE, FALSE) ' START ROW is its only live button
    runNum := 0
    repeat
        runNum += 1
        bFirst := (runNum == 1)
        debug("T0-24,row,", udec_(seqNum), ",id,", udec_(rowIdx), ",run,", udec_(runNum), ",prediction,", zstr_(t0sRowPrediction(rowIdx)), ",asking_for,", zstr_(t0sRowAction(rowIdx)))
        t0wStopReq := FALSE                                     ' cog 0 is these two flags' only writer, and the
        t0wAbortReq := FALSE                                    '  measure cog is idle between jobs
        bRan := bT0sSetUp(rowIdx, seqNum)
        if bRan
            if bT0sHoldRow(rowIdx)
                t0sEvRead(rowIdx, seqNum, runNum, FALSE)            ' task 3621: what SETUP left is not this ACT's
            t0sRunJob(rowIdx, seqNum, T0S_PH_ACT, T0_24_JOB_ACT, bFirst)
            whyShown := t0wWhy
            res1 := t0wRes1
            res2 := t0wRes2
            t0sPrintRow(rowIdx, seqNum, runNum)
            if bT0sHoldRow(rowIdx)
                t0sEvRead(rowIdx, seqNum, runNum, TRUE)             ' task 3621: this ACT's hand-offs, as the log reports them
        else
            if t0wAbortReq
                whyShown := T0S_ST_NM_ABORTED
            else
                whyShown := T0S_ST_NM_SETUP
            res1 := -1
            res2 := -1
        t0sJob(rowIdx, T0_24_JOB_TEARDOWN)                      ' the wheel is left safe before he reads the result
        debug("T0-24,row,", udec_(seqNum), ",run,", udec_(runNum), ",result,ran,", zstr_(bRan ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",why,", zstr_(t0sWhyToken(whyShown)), ",res1,", sdec_(res1), ",res2,", sdec_(res2))
        btn := t0sUiWait(rowIdx, seqNum, T0S_PH_RESULT, whyShown, res1, res2, FALSE, bFirst)
        if btn <> T0S_BT_REDO
            quit

PRI bT0sSetUp(rowIdx, seqNum) : bSetUp | pScreen
' SETUP, on the measure cog for every row but COGSTOP. COGSTOP's setup is stop(), which ends two cogs,
' so cog 0 runs it in its own quiet window (PLOT-DISPLAY-RULES.md rule 9); its SETUP screen shows no
' ABORT, because nothing polls one during it. A setup that ABORT interrupted is not set up.
'
' @param rowIdx - which row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @param seqNum - this run's 1-based row position
' @returns bSetUp - TRUE when the row's state was reached and ABORT was not clicked
'
' @local pScreen - COGSTOP's SETUP entry in t0sScreenTab

    if rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP
        pScreen := t0sScreenPtr(rowIdx, T0S_PH_SETUP, FALSE)
        t0sDrawRow(pScreen, rowIdx, seqNum, byte[pScreen][T0S_SCR_STATUS], -1, -1, T0S_BT_NONE, TRUE)
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        motor.stop()
        waitms(T0_24_SETTLE_MS)
        motor.getError()
        bSetUp := TRUE
    else
        t0sRunJob(rowIdx, seqNum, T0S_PH_SETUP, T0_24_JOB_SETUP, FALSE)
        bSetUp := bT0wSetUp and (t0wAbortReq == FALSE)
        if (rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE) or (rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP) or (rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT)
            debug("T0-24,row,", udec_(seqNum), ",rearm,off_hs,", udec_(t0wOffHs), ",hs,", udec_(t0wHoldHs), ",disp,", sdec_(t0wHoldDisp), ",fault_sig,", zstr_(bT0wFaultSig ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",held,", zstr_(bT0wHeld ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

PRI t0sPost(rowIdx, job)
' Post one job to the measure cog. t0wJobSeq is written last, so the job's other longs are in place
' when the measure cog sees it.
'
' @param rowIdx - the row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @param job - T0_24_JOB_*

    t0wJob := job
    t0wRow := rowIdx
    t0wJobSeq += 1

PRI t0sRunJob(rowIdx, seqNum, phase, job, bFirst)
' Post a job and keep the panel live until the measure cog answers: DONE and ABORT are read on every
' pass, and the live phrase and readings are redrawn as they change.
'
' @param rowIdx - the row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @param seqNum - this run's 1-based row position
' @param phase - the screen shown meanwhile, T0S_PH_SETUP or T0S_PH_ACT
' @param job - T0_24_JOB_SETUP or T0_24_JOB_ACT
' @param bFirst - TRUE on the row's first run: the (row, phase)'s panel-test screen, if it has one

    t0sPost(rowIdx, job)
    repeat while t0wTakenSeq <> t0wJobSeq                     ' its first phrase is in place before the first frame
        waitus(T0_24_JOB_POLL_US)
    t0sUiWait(rowIdx, seqNum, phase, T0S_ST_BLANK, -1, -1, TRUE, bFirst)

PRI t0sJob(rowIdx, job)
' Post a job and wait for it with no panel: the teardown, which has nothing to show and nothing to stop.
'
' @param rowIdx - the row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @param job - T0_24_JOB_TEARDOWN

    t0sPost(rowIdx, job)
    repeat while t0wDoneSeq <> t0wJobSeq
        waitms(1)

PRI t0sUiWait(rowIdx, seqNum, phase, statusIdx, r1, r2, bJob, bFirst) : btn | pScreen, btnL, btnR, bBox, bBoxHit, bTestShown, litBtn, shownSt, shownR1, shownR2, lastDrawMs, bEnded, bDraw, bLitNow
' THE PANEL LOOP: one screen, from its first draw until it is left. On every pass it reads the mouse
' (and the keyboard every T0_24_UI_KEY_PASSES), so no click falls between reads. Without a job it
' returns the button he chose; the only buttons drawn are the ones that can be chosen. With a job it
' runs until the measure cog answers: DONE and ABORT are passed to the measure cog as requests and the
' clicked button stays lit, the live phrase is redrawn as soon as it changes, and the readings at most
' every T0_24_UI_REDRAW_MS. A screen showing the grey box (row 1's panel test, PL-135) has no button:
' it ends when a click lands on the box, and returns T0S_BT_NONE. A key cannot end it.
'
' @param rowIdx - the row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @param seqNum - this run's 1-based row position
' @param phase - T0S_PH_*: with rowIdx, picks the t0sScreenTab entry
' @param statusIdx - the phrase to show, T0S_ST_* (ignored with a job: the measure cog's is shown)
' @param r1 - the readings to show, -1 for none (ignored with a job)
' @param r2
' @param bJob - TRUE while a posted job runs
' @param bFirst - TRUE on the row's first run: the (row, phase)'s panel-test screen, if it has one
' @returns btn - the button chosen, T0S_BT_*; T0S_BT_NONE when a job or the grey box ended the screen
'
' @local pScreen - this screen's t0sScreenTab or t0sTestTab entry
' @local btnL - the live left button, T0S_BT_*
' @local btnR - the live right button, T0S_BT_*
' @local bBox - TRUE when this screen shows the grey box
' @local bBoxHit - TRUE when this pass took a click on the grey box
' @local bTestShown - TRUE when this screen is a panel test's, for the screen record
' @local litBtn - the button drawn lit (clicked), T0S_BT_NONE when none
' @local shownSt - the phrase last drawn
' @local shownR1 - the readings last drawn
' @local shownR2
' @local lastDrawMs - getms() at the last draw
' @local bEnded - TRUE once the screen is left
' @local bDraw - TRUE when this pass must redraw
' @local bLitNow - TRUE when a button lit this pass, so the redraw includes the buttons

    pScreen := t0sScreenPtr(rowIdx, phase, bFirst)
    bTestShown := (pScreen <> t0sScreenPtr(rowIdx, phase, FALSE))
    btnL := byte[pScreen][T0S_SCR_BTN_L]
    btnR := byte[pScreen][T0S_SCR_BTN_R]
    bBox := (byte[pScreen][T0S_SCR_LBL1] == T0S_L_MISS_BOX)   ' the grey box sits in reading label 1's slot
    litBtn := T0S_BT_NONE
    btn := T0S_BT_NONE
    if bJob
        statusIdx := t0wStatus
        r1 := t0wRead1
        r2 := t0wRead2
    t0sDrawRow(pScreen, rowIdx, seqNum, statusIdx, r1, r2, litBtn, TRUE)
    debug("T0-24,screen,row,", udec_(seqNum), ",id,", udec_(rowIdx), ",phase,", udec_(phase), ",status,", udec_(statusIdx), ",panel_test,", zstr_(bTestShown ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))
    shownSt := statusIdx
    shownR1 := r1
    shownR2 := r2
    lastDrawMs := getms()
    t0sIgnoreUntilMs := lastDrawMs + T0_24_UI_DEBOUNCE_MS      ' a press this soon belongs to the last screen
    bEnded := FALSE
    repeat while bEnded == FALSE
        bDraw := FALSE
        bLitNow := FALSE
        if bJob
            bEnded := (t0wDoneSeq == t0wJobSeq)
            statusIdx := t0wStatus
            r1 := t0wRead1
            r2 := t0wRead2
        if bEnded == FALSE
            btn, bBoxHit := t0sReadInput(seqNum, btnL, btnR, bBox)
            if btn <> T0S_BT_NONE
                litBtn := btn
                bLitNow := TRUE                                 ' the buttons are redrawn only when one lights
                bDraw := TRUE
                if bJob                                         ' a request to the measure cog; the screen stays
                    if btn == T0S_BT_DONE
                        t0wStopReq := TRUE
                    elseif btn == T0S_BT_ABORT
                        t0wAbortReq := TRUE
                    btn := T0S_BT_NONE
                else
                    bEnded := TRUE
            elseif bBoxHit and (bJob == FALSE)                  ' the grey box's click, logged hit,MISS (PL-135)
                bEnded := TRUE
            if statusIdx <> shownSt
                bDraw := TRUE
                debug("T0-24,status,row,", udec_(seqNum), ",phase,", udec_(phase), ",status,", udec_(statusIdx), ",read1,", sdec_(r1), ",read2,", sdec_(r2))
            elseif ((r1 <> shownR1) or (r2 <> shownR2)) and ((getms() - lastDrawMs) >= T0_24_UI_REDRAW_MS)
                bDraw := TRUE
            if bDraw
                t0sDrawRow(pScreen, rowIdx, seqNum, statusIdx, r1, r2, litBtn, bLitNow)
                shownSt := statusIdx
                shownR1 := r1
                shownR2 := r2
                lastDrawMs := getms()
            if bEnded == FALSE
                waitms(T0_24_UI_WAIT_MS)

PRI t0sReadInput(seqNum, btnL, btnR, bBox) : btn, bBoxHit | viaCode, candBtn, xPos, yPos, keyCode, pHit
' Read the mouse every pass and the keyboard every T0_24_UI_KEY_PASSES -- the panel's ONLY input read,
' so each backtick statement exists once in this binary (DBG-2). A click is a left-button press edge
' (0 -> -1, builder's guide SS7: the button is a live state), taken on the button slot it lands on.
' Enter duplicates the right button and Esc the left; on an empty slot a key chooses nothing. Every
' press is logged -- the button it chose, MISS for none, or IGNORED inside the debounce after a screen
' change -- so a click that did nothing can be told from one that never arrived (PLOT-DISPLAY-RULES.md
' rule 10). A click on the grey box hits no button, so it too logs MISS; only a click reports bBoxHit.
'
' @param seqNum - this run's 1-based row position, for the log
' @param btnL - the live left button, T0S_BT_* (T0S_BT_NONE when the slot is empty)
' @param btnR - the live right button, T0S_BT_*
' @param bBox - TRUE when the screen shows the grey box (T0S_BOX_*)
' @returns btn - the button chosen, T0S_BT_NONE when none
' @returns bBoxHit - TRUE when a click, outside the debounce, landed on the grey box
'
' @local viaCode - 0 none, 1 a mouse press, 2 a key
' @local candBtn - the button the press lands on, T0S_BT_NONE for none
' @local xPos - the press's position, window pixels (the key's log reads -1)
' @local yPos
' @local keyCode - the key read, 0 for none
' @local pHit - the log's token for the press: a button's name, MISS, or IGNORED

    btn := T0S_BT_NONE
    bBoxHit := FALSE
    viaCode := 0
    candBtn := T0S_BT_NONE
    xPos := -1
    yPos := -1
    keyCode := 0
    t0sUiPass += 1
    debug(`t0stop `pc_mouse(@t0sMouse))
    if (t0sMouse[T0_24_MOUSE_LBTN] <> 0) and (t0sPrevLbtn == 0)
        viaCode := 1
        xPos := t0sMouse[T0_24_MOUSE_XPOS]
        yPos := t0sMouse[T0_24_MOUSE_YPOS]
        if (yPos >= T0S_BTN_Y) and (yPos < T0S_BTN_Y + T0S_BTN_H)
            if (xPos >= T0S_BTN_L_X) and (xPos < T0S_BTN_L_X + T0S_BTN_W)
                candBtn := btnL
            elseif (xPos >= T0S_BTN_R_X) and (xPos < T0S_BTN_R_X + T0S_BTN_W)
                candBtn := btnR
    t0sPrevLbtn := t0sMouse[T0_24_MOUSE_LBTN]
    if (viaCode == 0) and ((t0sUiPass +// T0_24_UI_KEY_PASSES) == 0)
        debug(`t0stop `pc_key(@t0sKey))
        keyCode := t0sKey
        if keyCode <> 0
            viaCode := 2
            if keyCode == T0_24_KEY_ENTER
                candBtn := btnR
            elseif keyCode == T0_24_KEY_ESC
                candBtn := btnL
    if viaCode <> 0
        if getms() < t0sIgnoreUntilMs                           ' if/else, never `? :` with a call -- PL-29
            pHit := @"IGNORED"
        else
            btn := candBtn
            pHit := t0sBtnName(candBtn)
            if bBox and (viaCode == 1) and (candBtn == T0S_BT_NONE)
                bBoxHit := (xPos >= T0S_BOX_X) and (xPos < T0S_BOX_X + T0S_BOX_W) and (yPos >= T0S_BOX_Y) and (yPos < T0S_BOX_Y + T0S_BOX_H)
        debug("T0-24,input,row,", udec_(seqNum), ",via,", udec_(viaCode), ",x,", sdec_(xPos), ",y,", sdec_(yPos), ",key,", udec_(keyCode), ",hit,", zstr_(pHit), ",left,", zstr_(t0sBtnName(btnL)), ",right,", zstr_(t0sBtnName(btnR)))

PRI t0sBtnName(btn) : pName
' The log's name for a button; MISS for no button.
'
' @param btn - T0S_BT_*
' @returns pName - pointer to the name

    case btn
        T0S_BT_START:  pName := @"START_ROW"
        T0S_BT_DONE:   pName := @"DONE"
        T0S_BT_NEXT:   pName := @"NEXT_ROW"
        T0S_BT_FINISH: pName := @"FINISH"
        T0S_BT_ABORT:  pName := @"ABORT"
        T0S_BT_REDO:   pName := @"REDO_ROW"
        other:         pName := @"MISS"

PRI t0sWhyToken(statusIdx) : pText
' The log's token for a RESULT phrase.
'
' @param statusIdx - T0S_ST_* shown on the RESULT screen
' @returns pText - pointer to the token

    case statusIdx
        T0S_ST_MEASURED:     pText := @"MEASURED"
        T0S_ST_NM_NO_PUSH:   pText := @"NO_PUSH_SEEN"
        T0S_ST_NM_NOT_FRESH: pText := @"HOLD_NOT_FRESH"
        T0S_ST_NM_NO_SPIN:   pText := @"NO_SPIN_IN_BAND"
        T0S_ST_NM_NO_ESTOP:  pText := @"ESTOP_NOT_APPLIED"
        T0S_ST_NM_ABORTED:   pText := @"ABORTED"
        T0S_ST_NM_NO_SPEED:  pText := @"NEVER_REACHED_SPEED"
        T0S_ST_NM_NO_FAULT:  pText := @"NO_FAULT"
        T0S_ST_NM_10A:       pText := @"ABS_CURRENT_10A"
        T0S_ST_NM_SETUP:     pText := @"SETUP_FAILED"
        other:               pText := @"UNKNOWN_STATUS"      ' a new phrase this list lacks, never a wrong one

PRI t0sPrintRow(rowIdx, seqNum, runNum) | tryIdx, pTry, sampleIdx, firstIdx, pSample, keptCount
' Print what the measure cog buffered during ACT, now that the step is over -- outside the measured
' interval (doctrine D6). Nothing is silently capped: a ring or buffer that overflowed says how many
' it dropped.
'
' @param rowIdx - the row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @param seqNum - this run's 1-based row position
' @param runNum - this row's run
'
' @local tryIdx - a spin row's try, 0-based
' @local pTry - that try's record in t0wTries
' @local sampleIdx - a hold sample's index, counting every sample this run
' @local firstIdx - the oldest sample the ring still holds
' @local pSample - that sample's record in t0wHold
' @local keptCount - samples or tries kept

    case rowIdx
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE, T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP, T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT:
            keptCount := t0wHoldCount <# T0_24_HOLD_RING
            firstIdx := t0wHoldCount - keptCount
            repeat sampleIdx from firstIdx to t0wHoldCount - 1
                pSample := @t0wHold[(sampleIdx +// T0_24_HOLD_RING) * T0_24_HOLD_LONGS]
                debug("T0-24,hold_log,row,", udec_(seqNum), ",run,", udec_(runNum), ",ms,", udec_(long[pSample][T0_24_HS_MS]), ",pos,", sdec_(long[pSample][T0_24_HS_POS]), ",disp,", sdec_(long[pSample][T0_24_HS_DISP]), ",duty,", udec_(long[pSample][T0_24_HS_DUTY]), ",drv_state,", udec_(long[pSample][T0_24_HS_DRV_STATE]), ",sense_i,", sdec_(long[pSample][T0_24_HS_SENSE_I]))
            debug("T0-24,row,", udec_(seqNum), ",run,", udec_(runNum), ",hold_result,displaced,", zstr_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_DISPLACED] ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",disp_first_ms,", sdec_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_DISP_MS]), ",ceil_first_ms,", sdec_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_CEIL_MS]), ",ceil_sense_i,", sdec_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_CEIL_I]), ",slip_first_ms,", sdec_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_SLIP_MS]), ",limit_first_ms,", sdec_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_LIMIT_MS]), ",fault_first_ms,", sdec_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_FAULT_MS]), ",fault_first,", zstr_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_FLT_FIRST] ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",aborted,", zstr_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_ABORTED] ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",pass,", zstr_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_PASS] ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
            debug("T0-24,row,", udec_(seqNum), ",run,", udec_(runNum), ",hold_start,start_hs,", udec_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_START_HS]), ",start_disp,", sdec_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_START_DISP]), ",start_held,", zstr_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_START_HELD] ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",max_disp,", udec_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_MAX_DISP]), ",rise_ms,", sdec_(t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_RISE_MS]), ",samples,", udec_(t0wHoldCount), ",dropped,", udec_(firstIdx), ",protective,", sdec_(t0wProtCode))
        other:
            if (rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST) or (rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD)
                debug("T0-24,provoke,row,", udec_(seqNum), ",run,", udec_(runNum), ",stop_mode,", zstr_((rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD) ? @"BRAKE" : @"FLOAT"), ",fr_err,", sdec_(t0wFrErr), ",force_err,", sdec_(t0wForceErr), ",at_speed,", zstr_(bT0wAtSpeed ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",release_span_ms,", udec_(t0sReleaseSpan[rowIdx]), ",faulted,", zstr_(bT0wFaulted ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",band_entered,", zstr_(bT0wEntered ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",driver_state,", udec_(t0wDrvState), ",abort_amps_x10k,", sdec_(t0wAbortAmps))
            else
                keptCount := t0wTryCount <# T0_24_TRY_MAX
                repeat tryIdx from 0 to keptCount - 1
                    pTry := @t0wTries[tryIdx * T0_24_TRY_LONGS]
                    debug("T0-24,row,", udec_(seqNum), ",run,", udec_(runNum), ",try,", udec_(tryIdx + 1), ",hand_ticks,", udec_(long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_HAND]), ",release_span_ms,", udec_(long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_SPAN]), ",after_ticks,", udec_(long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_AFTER]), ",after_ms,", udec_(long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_AFTER_MS]), ",band_ticks,", udec_(long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_BAND]), ",band_ms,", udec_(long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_BAND_MS]), ",in_band,", udec_(long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_IN_BAND]), ",band_entered,", udec_(long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_ENTERED]), ",shorted,", udec_(long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_SHORTED]), ",estop_latched,", udec_(long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_LATCHED]), ",measured,", udec_(long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_MEASURED]))
                debug("T0-24,row,", udec_(seqNum), ",run,", udec_(runNum), ",tries,", udec_(t0wTryCount), ",printed,", udec_(keptCount))
            debug("T0-24,row,", udec_(seqNum), ",run,", udec_(runNum), ",set_up,TRUE,hand_ticks,", udec_(t0sHandTicks[rowIdx]), ",after_ticks,", udec_(t0sAfterTicks[rowIdx]), ",after_ms,", udec_(t0sAfterMs[rowIdx]), ",band_ticks,", udec_(t0sBandTicks[rowIdx]), ",band_ms,", udec_(t0sBandMs[rowIdx]), ",in_band,", zstr_(bT0sInBand[rowIdx] ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",release_span_ms,", udec_(t0sReleaseSpan[rowIdx]), ",still_faulted,", zstr_(bT0sStillFaulted[rowIdx] ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",protective,", sdec_(t0wProtCode), ",measured,", zstr_(bT0sRowMeasured[rowIdx] ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

PRI t0sWorker() | jobSeq, job, rowIdx
' THE MEASURE COG (task 3619). It waits for a job, does it, and answers by setting t0wDoneSeq. It owns
' every act that touches the wheel and every timed reading -- the hall poll, the hold samples, the
' e-stop at the band, the forced fault and the 10 A abort -- and it PRINTS NOTHING: a debug() here
' could wait on the panel's input read (LOCK[15], DBG-10) and stall the 1 ms hall poll. What it
' measures is buffered in hub, and cog 0 prints it after the step. It starts and stops no cog.
'
' @local jobSeq - the job's sequence number, answered in t0wDoneSeq
' @local job - T0_24_JOB_*
' @local rowIdx - the job's row, T0_24_ROW_*

    repeat
        repeat while t0wDoneSeq == t0wJobSeq
            waitus(T0_24_JOB_POLL_US)
        jobSeq := t0wJobSeq
        job := t0wJob
        rowIdx := t0wRow
        if job <> T0_24_JOB_TEARDOWN                            ' teardown keeps the readings the cells judge
            t0sClearRow(rowIdx)                                 ' this run's readings replace the last run's
        t0wRead1 := -1
        t0wRead2 := -1
        if job == T0_24_JOB_SETUP                               ' the screen's opening phrase, from the generated table
            t0wStatus := byte[t0sScreenPtr(rowIdx, T0S_PH_SETUP, FALSE)][T0S_SCR_STATUS]
        elseif job == T0_24_JOB_ACT                             ' a panel test opens with the same phrase (the generator checks)
            t0wStatus := byte[t0sScreenPtr(rowIdx, T0S_PH_ACT, FALSE)][T0S_SCR_STATUS]
        t0wTakenSeq := jobSeq                                   ' the panel draws its first frame only now: never a stale phrase
        case job
            T0_24_JOB_SETUP:
                bT0wSetUp := bT0sSetUpRow(rowIdx)
            T0_24_JOB_ACT:
                case rowIdx
                    T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE, T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP, T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT:
                        t0sHoldAct(rowIdx)
                    T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST, T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD:
                        t0sPowerAct(rowIdx)
                    other:                                      ' COAST, ESTOP, COGSTOP: he spins it
                        t0sSpinAct(rowIdx)
                t0wProtCode := motor.getProtectiveStop()
            T0_24_JOB_TEARDOWN:
                t0sTearDownRow(rowIdx)
        motor.getError()                                        ' this cog's own error slot, drained after every job
        t0wDoneSeq := jobSeq                                    ' written last: every result long is in place

PRI t0sClearRow(rowIdx)
' Forget a row's readings before it runs, so a redo, or a run that stops short, cannot be judged from
' an earlier run's values. The measure cog is their only writer.
'
' @param rowIdx - the row, T0_24_ROW_*

    t0sHandTicks[rowIdx] := 0
    t0sAfterTicks[rowIdx] := 0
    t0sAfterMs[rowIdx] := 0
    t0sBandTicks[rowIdx] := 0
    t0sBandMs[rowIdx] := 0
    t0sReleaseSpan[rowIdx] := 0
    bT0sInBand[rowIdx] := FALSE
    bT0sRowMeasured[rowIdx] := FALSE
    bT0sStillFaulted[rowIdx] := FALSE
    case rowIdx
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE:  bT0sHoldRiseMeasured := FALSE
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP:  bT0sHoldSlipMeasured := FALSE
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT: bT0sHoldLimitMeasured := FALSE
    t0wWhy := T0S_ST_NM_SETUP
    t0wRes1 := -1
    t0wRes2 := -1

PRI t0sScreenPtr(rowIdx, phase, bFirst) : pScreen | testIdx, pTest
' The screen entry for one (row, phase): the one place the two tables are indexed. On a row's first
' run it is the (row, phase)'s panel test in t0sTestTab when it has one (PL-135), else t0sScreenTab's.
'
' @param rowIdx - the row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @param phase - T0S_PH_*
' @param bFirst - TRUE on the row's first run
' @returns pScreen - the entry's first byte; read it with T0S_SCR_* offsets
'
' @local testIdx - a t0sTestTab entry, 0-based
' @local pTest - that entry's first byte

    pScreen := @t0sScreenTab + (((rowIdx * T0S_PHASE_COUNT) + phase) * T0S_SCREEN_BYTES)
    if bFirst
        repeat testIdx from 0 to T0S_TEST_COUNT - 1
            pTest := @t0sTestTab + (testIdx * T0S_TEST_BYTES)
            if (byte[pTest][T0S_TEST_ROW] == rowIdx) and (byte[pTest][T0S_TEST_PHASE] == phase)
                pScreen := pTest + T0S_TEST_SCREEN

PRI bT0sHasTest(rowIdx, phase) : bHas
' Report whether one (row, phase) has a panel-test screen for its first run (t0sTestTab, PL-135).
'
' @param rowIdx - the row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @param phase - T0S_PH_*
' @returns bHas - TRUE when t0sTestTab has an entry for it

    bHas := (t0sScreenPtr(rowIdx, phase, TRUE) <> t0sScreenPtr(rowIdx, phase, FALSE))

PRI bT0sSetUpRow(rowIdx) : bSetUp
' Put the driver into this row's stop or hold state, and report whether it got there (measure cog).
'
' A stop state is only what the DRIVER is in, so each row checks the driver rather than assuming
' the call took: the e-stop row must read NOT emergency-stopped (it is spun free, and shorted at the
' band by t0sSpinAct()), and every hold row requires a NEW hold (bT0sRearmHold(): HS_HOLDING at
' displacement 0, and isFaultSignal() still FALSE -- a fault recorded from here, not carried over from
' an earlier row). The two fault rows need nothing here: their whole provocation is their ACT, so
' ABORT is live for all of it.
'
' @param rowIdx - which row, T0_24_ROW_* (never COGSTOP: cog 0 sets that one up)
' @returns bSetUp - TRUE when the row's state was reached

    bSetUp := FALSE
    case rowIdx
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE:
            bSetUp := bT0sRearmHold(T0_24_HOLD_DEFAULT_CEIL_PCT, T0_24_HOLD_DEFAULT_LIMIT_MS)
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP:
            bSetUp := bT0sRearmHold(T0_24_HOLD_SLIP_CEIL_PCT, T0_24_HOLD_DEFAULT_LIMIT_MS)
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT:
            bSetUp := bT0sRearmHold(T0_24_HOLD_DEFAULT_CEIL_PCT, T0_24_HOLD_LIMIT_TEST_MS)
        T0_24_ROW_COAST, T0_24_ROW_ESTOP:
            ' task 3617: the e-stop row is set up COASTING too, so he can spin it into the band.
            ' t0sSpinAct() applies the e-stop itself at the band entry, and counts a try only when it latched.
            motor.holdAtStop(FALSE)
            motor.stopMotor()
            waitms(T0_24_SETTLE_MS)
            bSetUp := (rowIdx <> T0_24_ROW_ESTOP) or (motor.isEmergency() == FALSE) ' free to spin: no e-stop left from before
        T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST, T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD:
            bSetUp := TRUE

PRI t0sTearDownRow(rowIdx)
' Leave the driver ready for the next row (measure cog). Nothing here runs before the row's reading is
' taken: every one of these calls would itself change the bridge state the row just measured. The
' rows with nothing to undo (COAST, COGSTOP) fall through; the measure cog drains its error slot
' after every job.
'
' @param rowIdx - the row just finished, T0_24_ROW_*

    case rowIdx
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE:
            motor.clearFaultSignal()
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP, T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT:
            motor.clearFaultSignal()
            motor.clearProtectiveStop()
            motor.setHoldLimits(T0_24_HOLD_DEFAULT_CEIL_PCT, T0_24_HOLD_DEFAULT_RISE_MS, T0_24_HOLD_DEFAULT_LIMIT_MS)
        T0_24_ROW_ESTOP:
            if motor.isEmergency()                              ' latched only when a try applied the short
                motor.clearEmergency()
        T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST, T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD:
            ' DCS_FAULTED is a latch (DRIVER_REV 14+): only a commanded stop or drive clears it, and the
            ' fault's bridge holds until then. testResetFault() commands the stop, clears the fault
            ' signal and waits for DCS_STOPPED. It acts only on a recorded fault; a row that did not
            ' fault already stopped the wheel in t0sPowerAct().
            motor.testResetFault()
            motor.clearProtectiveStop()

PRI bT0sRearmHold(ceilingPct, limitMs) : bHeld | offState
' PL-123 item 1: start a hold row from a NEW hold, never from the last row's. The front cog arms a hold
' only after a pass that finds the stop mode off SM_BRAKE or the motor off rest (frontHold()), so
' SM_FLOAT is selected for T0_24_REARM_MS (the old hold reads HS_OFF), then SM_BRAKE again (a new
' hold is armed where the wheel now is). The row is set up only when the new hold reads HS_HOLDING
' at displacement 0 with no fault signal; otherwise its cell is NOMEAS, never judged from an
' inherited slip. Measure cog: the readings go to hub, and cog 0 prints them as the rearm record.
'
' @param ceilingPct - the row's hold ceiling, % (setHoldLimits())
' @param limitMs - the row's time limit at the ceiling, ms (setHoldLimits())
' @returns bHeld - TRUE when the old hold ended and a new one holds at displacement 0
'
' @local offState - getHoldStatus()'s state with SM_FLOAT selected, HS_* (HS_OFF when the old hold ended)

    motor.setHoldLimits(ceilingPct, T0_24_HOLD_DEFAULT_RISE_MS, limitMs)
    motor.clearFaultSignal()
    motor.holdAtStop(FALSE)
    motor.stopMotor()
    waitms(T0_24_REARM_MS)
    offState, _ := motor.getHoldStatus()
    motor.holdAtStop(TRUE)
    motor.stopMotor()
    waitms(T0_24_SETTLE_MS)
    t0wHoldHs, t0wHoldDisp := motor.getHoldStatus()
    bT0wFaultSig := motor.isFaultSignal()
    t0wOffHs := offState
    bHeld := (offState == motor.HS_OFF) and (t0wHoldHs == motor.HS_HOLDING) and (t0wHoldDisp == 0) and (bT0wFaultSig == FALSE)
    bT0wHeld := bHeld

PRI t0sPowerAct(rowIdx) | bHold, releaseSpan, afterTicks, afterMs, bandTicks, bandMs, bInBand, bAborted
' The two fault rows' ACT (measure cog): drive the wheel to speed, fault the driver under the stop mode
' the row selects, and let the wheel come to rest with the fault still in force. ABORT and the 10 A
' abort are live from the first command to rest (bT0sPoweredAbort()), and either stops the wheel.
'
' THE FAULT IS FORCED, NOT PROVOKED (task 3617, PL-123 item 3; PL-119). testForceFault() faults the
' driver on its next DRIVEN frame, at its own fault test, so the response is the real one: under
' FR_SHIPPED the bridge takes the stop mode's fault state at once, SM_FLOAT a coast and SM_BRAKE a
' short. No offset is touched, so the field is never left off the rotor to plug the motor, as the
' offset shift did at Visit 10 pass 2 (10.4 A aborts, debug_260923-193439.log:2194, :2250).
' FR_SHIPPED is set explicitly, so the row does not rest on the start-up default.
'
' NOTHING IS COMMANDED AFTER THE FAULT. DCS_FAULTED is a latch (DRIVER_REV 14+): the fault's bridge
' holds until a stop or a drive is commanded, and either would replace it with another state and
' measure the wrong thing. So the coast to rest here is only a measurement; t0sTearDownRow() ends
' the fault afterwards.
'
' @param rowIdx - T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST (SM_FLOAT, predicted BR_COAST) or T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD (SM_BRAKE, BR_SHORT)
'
' @local bHold - TRUE for the brake-mode row
' @local releaseSpan - the steady AT_SPEED six-interval span, measured just before the fault: the
'                       fault's own "release rate", parallel to a spin row's hand rate
' @local afterTicks - t0sCoastDecay()'s tick count
' @local afterMs - t0sCoastDecay()'s elapsed-ms reading
' @local bandTicks - t0sCoastDecay()'s band reading
' @local bandMs - the ms that took
' @local bInBand - TRUE when the steady rate was above T0_24_BAND_RATE
' @local bAborted - TRUE when ABORT or the 10 A abort ended the row

    bHold := (rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD)
    releaseSpan := 0
    bInBand := FALSE
    bT0wAtSpeed := FALSE
    bT0wFaulted := FALSE
    bT0wEntered := FALSE
    t0wForceErr := 0
    t0wAbortAmps := 0
    t0wFrErr := motor.setFaultResponse(motor.FR_SHIPPED, motor.BRAKE_PCT_DEFAULT)
    motor.clearFaultSignal()                                    ' the fault signal then records this row's fault only
    motor.holdAtStop(bHold)
    motor.driveAtPower(T0_24_FLT_POWER)
    bT0wAtSpeed := bT0sWaitDriver(T0_24_UNTIL_SPEED, T0_24_SPEED_MS)
    if bT0wAtSpeed
        t0wStatus := T0S_ST_AT_SPEED
        if bT0sSettle(T0_24_SETTLE_MS)
            releaseSpan := t0sMeasureSteadyRate(T0_24_SPEED_MS)
            if releaseSpan > 0
                t0wRead1 := T0_24_SPAN_TO_RATE / releaseSpan
            if bT0sPoweredAbort() == FALSE
                t0wForceErr := motor.testForceFault()
                bT0wFaulted := bT0sWaitDriver(T0_24_UNTIL_FAULT, T0_24_FORCE_WAIT_MS)
                if bT0wFaulted
                    t0wStatus := T0S_ST_FAULTED
                    afterTicks, afterMs, bandTicks, bandMs, bInBand := t0sCoastDecay(releaseSpan, getms(), T0_24_REST_QUIET_MS, T0_24_REST_WAIT_MS)
                    bT0wEntered := bT0sBandEntered
    bAborted := t0wAbortReq or (t0wAbortAmps <> 0)
    t0sReleaseSpan[rowIdx] := releaseSpan
    if bT0wFaulted and (bAborted == FALSE)
        t0sAfterTicks[rowIdx] := afterTicks
        t0sAfterMs[rowIdx] := afterMs
        t0sBandTicks[rowIdx] := bandTicks
        t0sBandMs[rowIdx] := bandMs
        bT0sInBand[rowIdx] := bInBand
        bT0sStillFaulted[rowIdx] := (motor.getDriverState() == motor.DCS_FAULTED)
        bT0sRowMeasured[rowIdx] := bInBand                      ' the wheel was driven above the band before the fault
    elseif bT0wFaulted == FALSE
        motor.stopMotor()                                       ' no fault to preserve, so the wheel is stopped at once
    t0wDrvState := motor.getDriverState()
    if t0wAbortAmps <> 0                                        ' if/else, never `? :` -- PL-29, PL-76
        t0wWhy := T0S_ST_NM_10A
    elseif bAborted
        t0wWhy := T0S_ST_NM_ABORTED
    elseif bT0wAtSpeed == FALSE
        t0wWhy := T0S_ST_NM_NO_SPEED
    elseif bT0wFaulted == FALSE
        t0wWhy := T0S_ST_NM_NO_FAULT
    elseif bInBand == FALSE
        t0wWhy := T0S_ST_NM_NO_SPEED
    else
        t0wWhy := T0S_ST_MEASURED
        t0wRes1 := bandTicks
        t0wRes2 := bandMs

PRI bT0sSettle(boundMs) : bOk | waitedMs
' The powered wait at speed before the fault, with both aborts live on every sample.
'
' @param boundMs - how long to hold at speed
' @returns bOk - TRUE when the whole wait passed with nothing aborting
'
' @local waitedMs - wait accumulator

    bOk := TRUE
    waitedMs := 0
    repeat while bOk and (waitedMs < boundMs)
        if bT0sPoweredAbort()
            bOk := FALSE
        else
            waitms(T0_24_SAMPLE_MS)
            waitedMs += T0_24_SAMPLE_MS

PRI bT0sWaitDriver(untilKind, boundMs) : bReached | waitedMs, bEnded
' The one bounded wait a powered window uses, for either state it ever waits on. The absolute
' current abort and the operator's ABORT are live on every sample, and either stops the motor,
' so the caller's next act is never to drive further. ABORT is a hub flag cog 0 sets, so reading it
' costs nothing, and the fault rows' coast measurement starts within one T0_24_SAMPLE_MS of the fault.
'
' @param untilKind - T0_24_UNTIL_SPEED or T0_24_UNTIL_FAULT: the driver state being waited on
' @param boundMs - the wait's bound; reaching it is not an abort, it is the state not arriving
' @returns bReached - TRUE when the state arrived inside the bound with nothing aborting
'
' @local waitedMs - wait accumulator
' @local bEnded - TRUE once the wait is over, however it ended

    bReached := FALSE
    bEnded := FALSE
    waitedMs := 0
    repeat while bEnded == FALSE
        if bT0sDriverAt(untilKind)
            bReached := TRUE
            bEnded := TRUE
        elseif bT0sPoweredAbort()
            bEnded := TRUE
        elseif waitedMs >= boundMs
            bEnded := TRUE
        else
            waitms(T0_24_SAMPLE_MS)
            waitedMs += T0_24_SAMPLE_MS

PRI bT0sDriverAt(untilKind) : bThere
' Report whether the driver is in the state a wait is waiting on.
'
' @param untilKind - T0_24_UNTIL_SPEED or T0_24_UNTIL_FAULT
' @returns bThere - TRUE when the driver is in that state now

    if untilKind == T0_24_UNTIL_FAULT                           ' if/else, never `? :` -- PL-29, PL-76
        bThere := motor.isFaulted()
    else
        bThere := (motor.getDriverState() == motor.DCS_AT_SPEED)

PRI bT0sPoweredAbort() : bAbort | amps
' The two live aborts of a powered window, both read on every sample: the absolute current ceiling,
' and ABORT, which cog 0 passes as the hub flag t0wAbortReq. Either stops the motor here, so the
' caller's next act is never to drive further. The 10 A reading is kept for cog 0's provoke record.
'
' @returns bAbort - TRUE when the powered window must end now
'
' @local amps - getCurrent()'s reading, 0.1 mA units

    bAbort := FALSE
    amps, _ := motor.getCurrent()
    if abs(amps) >= T0_24_ABORT_AMPS
        bAbort := TRUE
        t0wAbortAmps := amps
    elseif t0wAbortReq
        bAbort := TRUE
    if bAbort
        motor.stopMotor()

PRI t0sMeasureSteadyRate(boundMs) : releaseSpan | hallCode, priorCode, tickMs[T0_24_TICK_RING], ringIdx, tickN, startMs, nowMs
' The AT_SPEED six-interval span, measured just before the fault is forced -- the fault rows' own
' "release rate", read the same way t0sSpinAct() reads a hand's (PL-115: a rate from the hall
' signal, never from a keypress or a guess). Six intervals, one electrical cycle: the span is read
' from the slot the new tick is about to overwrite, which holds the tick six before it (task 3617;
' SRC_REV 12 read after writing, and so spanned five). ABORT ends it at once (it returns 0).
'
' @param boundMs - give up and return 0 if seven ticks never arrive inside this bound
' @returns releaseSpan - the six-interval span, ms; 0 when it was never read
'
' @local hallCode - the 3-bit hall code just read
' @local priorCode - the previous poll's code
' @local tickMs - the last T0_24_TICK_RING tick timestamps
' @local ringIdx - where the next tick's timestamp goes, and so the oldest kept
' @local tickN - ticks counted so far
' @local startMs - getms() at the start, for the bound
' @local nowMs - getms() at the tick just counted

    priorCode := t0sHallCode()
    ringIdx := 0
    tickN := 0
    releaseSpan := 0
    startMs := getms()
    repeat while (tickN <= T0_24_TICK_RING) and ((getms() - startMs) < boundMs) and (t0wAbortReq == FALSE)
        hallCode := t0sHallCode()
        if hallCode <> priorCode
            nowMs := getms()
            tickN += 1
            if tickN > T0_24_TICK_RING                          ' every slot holds a tick: this one is six ticks back
                releaseSpan := nowMs - tickMs[ringIdx]
            tickMs[ringIdx] := nowMs
            ringIdx := (ringIdx + 1) +// T0_24_TICK_RING
            priorCode := hallCode
        waitms(T0_24_POLL_MS)

PRI t0sCoastDecay(releaseSpan, releaseMs, restQuietMs, boundMs) : afterTicks, afterMs, bandTicks, bandMs, bInBand | hallCode, priorCode, tickMs[T0_24_TICK_RING], ringIdx, lastTickMs, nowMs, spanNow, bEnded
' The fault rows' coast measurement: what the wheel does with nobody driving it, counted from the
' fault (releaseMs) to rest, and read as band_ticks exactly as t0sSpinAct() reads a hand's release --
' the same three helpers compute it (t0sBandReset(), t0sBandTick(), t0sBandResult()). It runs on the
' measure cog, which prints nothing, so the 1 ms hall poll never stalls. The live readings go to
' t0wRead1/t0wRead2 for the panel. ABORT ends it: the wheel is stopped, and the row is not measured.
'
' @param releaseSpan - the six-interval span at release (the steady driven rate), ms
' @param releaseMs - getms() at the moment of release
' @param restQuietMs - no transition for this long ends the coast (the wheel is at rest)
' @param boundMs - hard bound on the whole coast
' @returns afterTicks - hall ticks counted after releaseMs
' @returns afterMs - ms from releaseMs to the last tick
' @returns bandTicks - ticks from T0_24_BAND_RATE to rest (0 when the release was not above the band)
' @returns bandMs - ms those took
' @returns bInBand - TRUE when the release was above T0_24_BAND_RATE
'
' @local hallCode - the 3-bit hall code just read
' @local priorCode - the previous poll's code
' @local tickMs - the last T0_24_TICK_RING tick timestamps, THIS call's own ring (starts empty)
' @local ringIdx - where the next tick's timestamp goes, and so the oldest kept
' @local lastTickMs - getms() at the last transition
' @local nowMs - this poll's getms()
' @local spanNow - the six-interval span ending at the tick just counted
' @local bEnded - TRUE once the coast is over

    priorCode := t0sHallCode()
    afterTicks := 0
    ringIdx := 0
    lastTickMs := releaseMs
    t0sBandReset()
    bEnded := FALSE
    repeat while bEnded == FALSE
        hallCode := t0sHallCode()
        nowMs := getms()
        if hallCode <> priorCode
            afterTicks += 1
            if afterTicks > T0_24_TICK_RING                     ' every slot holds a tick of this coast: six intervals back
                spanNow := nowMs - tickMs[ringIdx]
                t0sBandTick(afterTicks, nowMs, spanNow, releaseSpan)
                t0wRead1 := T0_24_SPAN_TO_RATE / (spanNow #> 1)
            tickMs[ringIdx] := nowMs
            ringIdx := (ringIdx + 1) +// T0_24_TICK_RING
            priorCode := hallCode
            lastTickMs := nowMs
            t0wRead2 := afterTicks
        if t0wAbortReq
            motor.stopMotor()
            bEnded := TRUE
        else
            bEnded := ((nowMs - lastTickMs) >= restQuietMs) or ((nowMs - releaseMs) >= boundMs)
        waitms(T0_24_POLL_MS)
    afterMs := (lastTickMs - releaseMs) #> 0
    bandTicks, bandMs, bInBand := t0sBandResult(releaseSpan, 0, releaseMs, afterTicks, lastTickMs)

PRI t0sBandReset()
' Forget any band entry: a new coast begins (t0sCoastDecay()), or a faster release was found and the
' band is now entered after it (t0sSpinAct()).

    bT0sBandEntered := FALSE
    t0sBandEntryTick := 0
    t0sBandEntryMs := 0

PRI t0sBandTick(tickIdx, nowMs, spanNow, releaseSpan)
' At each tick after the release whose six-interval span is valid: the first span of
' T0_24_BAND_SPAN_MS or more enters the band (the wheel's rate has fallen to T0_24_BAND_RATE) --
' but only after a release ABOVE the band. A slow spin's windows are all that long, and entering on
' one would fire the e-stop row's short with nothing to measure (task 3617).
'
' @param tickIdx - this tick's count, in the caller's own numbering
' @param nowMs - getms() at this tick
' @param spanNow - the six-interval span ending at this tick, ms
' @param releaseSpan - the release's six-interval span so far, ms (0 or -1: none yet)

    if (bT0sBandEntered == FALSE) and (releaseSpan > 0) and (releaseSpan < T0_24_BAND_SPAN_MS) and (spanNow >= T0_24_BAND_SPAN_MS)
        bT0sBandEntered := TRUE
        t0sBandEntryTick := tickIdx
        t0sBandEntryMs := nowMs

PRI t0sBandResult(releaseSpan, releaseTick, releaseMs, lastTick, lastMs) : bandTicks, bandMs, bInBand
' The row's stop reading (PL-123 item 2): the ticks, and the ms, from the band entry to the last tick.
' A wheel released above the band that stopped before any span reached it -- only a braked wheel does
' this, since a coast carries 9 or more ticks past the band -- reads every tick after the release,
' which bounds its ticks from the band from above. A release not above the band is no reading at all.
'
' @param releaseSpan - the six-interval span at the release, ms
' @param releaseTick - the tick count at the release, in the caller's numbering
' @param releaseMs - getms() at the release
' @param lastTick - the tick count at the last tick
' @param lastMs - getms() at the last tick
' @returns bandTicks - ticks from the band to rest; 0 when not in band
' @returns bandMs - ms from the band to the last tick; 0 when not in band
' @returns bInBand - TRUE when the release was faster than T0_24_BAND_RATE

    bInBand := (releaseSpan > 0) and (releaseSpan < T0_24_BAND_SPAN_MS)
    bandTicks := 0
    bandMs := 0
    if bInBand
        if bT0sBandEntered
            bandTicks := lastTick - t0sBandEntryTick
            bandMs := (lastMs - t0sBandEntryMs) #> 0
        else
            bandTicks := lastTick - releaseTick
            bandMs := (lastMs - releaseMs) #> 0

PRI t0sSpinAct(rowIdx) | bShortRow, hallCode, priorCode, nowMs, lastAnyMs, tickMs[T0_24_TICK_RING], ringIdx, totalTicks, bestSpan, bestEndMs, bestTickIdx, curSpan, bShorted, bAtRest, bKept, bAnyInBand
' The spin rows' ACT (measure cog) -- COAST, ESTOP, COGSTOP: he spins the wheel hard and lets go, as
' often as he likes, until he clicks DONE (task 3619). Each spin is a TRY: it starts at the first hall
' tick and ends when the wheel has been still for T0_24_REST_QUIET_MS. The live phrase says what the
' program sees (not fast enough yet, fast enough, slowing, stopped and got it, too slow). The row's
' reading is the LAST try that was measured; a later try that was not does not erase it, and the
' phrase says so. Every try is buffered, and cog 0 prints each one after the step. Nothing is timed
' out: without DONE or ABORT the row waits.
'
' The hall poll is this harness's own (T0-12's proven loop), so rows with a driver cog running and
' COGSTOP, which has none, are measured by the identical instrument. It runs on the measure cog,
' which prints nothing, so no input read or redraw ever stalls it (up to SRC_REV 13 the one cog did
' both, and suspended the panel while the wheel turned).
'
' PL-115, REBUILT A SECOND TIME (arbiter review): the release is the RATE PEAK, not a fixed gap
' threshold. "Spin briskly, then let go" means the hand ACCELERATES the wheel and lets go at its
' highest rate; after release the rate only falls. A fixed gap threshold is wrong for exactly the
' row this instrument exists to certify: a FREE coast keeps its tick gaps under a 100 ms threshold
' until the wheel is nearly stopped, so "release" landed near the END of the coast, and RESTCOAST and
' FREEREF would FAIL on a healthy free wheel (PL-115's own class of defect).
'
' ONE CONTINUOUS PASS PER TRY, single 6-tick ring, O(1) extra state. At every tick past the first
' T0_24_TICK_RING, the CURRENT six-interval span (read from the slot the new tick is about to
' overwrite: the tick six back) is compared against the RUNNING MINIMUM span of this try. A new
' minimum is a faster peak: record its end time and tick count, and forget any band entry taken after
' the previous (slower) peak (t0sBandReset()). Once no smaller span follows, the running minimum IS
' the release. The band entry is looked for live, after whichever span is currently the minimum.
'
' WHY TICKS FROM A FIXED RATE, NOT THE HALF-RATE TIME (task 3617, PL-123 item 2). A free wheel slows
' at a nearly constant rate, so the time to half its speed grows with the speed he gave it. Counting
' only from T0_24_BAND_RATE down makes the reading the same whatever the spin, provided the release
' was above the band (in_band); t0sBandResult() and CON { T0-24 sign-off limits }.
'
' THE E-STOP ROW'S SHORT IS APPLIED HERE (task 3617). At the band-entry tick emergencyCutoff() is
' called at once, so band_ticks counts the short from the same rate as every coast. The call waits on
' the front cog's answer (one front pass, about 1 ms), well inside the 8 ms tick interval at the band.
' After it the release is frozen: a later, faster window cannot move the band entry. A try counts only
' when the short was applied there AND latched (isEmergency()). At rest the e-stop is released, so
' the next spin starts free.
'
' @param rowIdx - T0_24_ROW_COAST, T0_24_ROW_ESTOP or T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP
'
' @local bShortRow - TRUE for the e-stop row
' @local hallCode - the 3-bit hall code just read
' @local priorCode - the previous poll's code
' @local nowMs - this poll's getms()
' @local lastAnyMs - the last tick, for the rest test
' @local tickMs - the last T0_24_TICK_RING tick timestamps
' @local ringIdx - where the next tick's timestamp goes, and so the oldest kept
' @local totalTicks - every hall tick of this try
' @local bestSpan - this try's running minimum six-interval span; -1 until T0_24_TICK_RING + 1 ticks
' @local bestEndMs - getms() at the tick ending the fastest window: the release, so far
' @local bestTickIdx - totalTicks when bestSpan was last set
' @local curSpan - the six-interval span ending at the tick just counted
' @local bShorted - TRUE once this try applied the e-stop at the band entry
' @local bAtRest - TRUE once the wheel has been still T0_24_REST_QUIET_MS after this try's first tick
' @local bKept - TRUE when a try was measured: the row has a reading
' @local bAnyInBand - TRUE once any try's release was above the band

    bShortRow := (rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_ESTOP)
    bAnyInBand := FALSE
    t0wTryCount := 0
    t0wRead1 := 0
    t0wRead2 := 0
    repeat while (t0wStopReq == FALSE) and (t0wAbortReq == FALSE) ' one pass per try
        totalTicks := 0
        ringIdx := 0
        bestSpan := -1
        bestEndMs := 0
        bestTickIdx := 0
        curSpan := 0
        bShorted := FALSE
        bAtRest := FALSE
        t0sBandReset()
        priorCode := t0sHallCode()
        lastAnyMs := getms()
        repeat while (bAtRest == FALSE) and (t0wStopReq == FALSE) and (t0wAbortReq == FALSE)
            hallCode := t0sHallCode()
            nowMs := getms()
            if hallCode <> priorCode
                priorCode := hallCode
                lastAnyMs := nowMs
                totalTicks += 1
                if totalTicks > T0_24_TICK_RING
                    curSpan := nowMs - tickMs[ringIdx]       ' ringIdx holds the tick six back, about to be overwritten
                    if ((bestSpan < 0) or (curSpan < bestSpan)) and (bShorted == FALSE)
                        bestSpan := curSpan
                        bestEndMs := nowMs
                        bestTickIdx := totalTicks
                        t0sBandReset()                        ' a faster peak: the band is entered after IT
                    else
                        t0sBandTick(totalTicks, nowMs, curSpan, bestSpan)
                        if bShortRow and bT0sBandEntered and (bShorted == FALSE)
                            motor.emergencyCutoff()           ' the e-stop row: BR_SHORT from the band-entry tick on
                            bShorted := TRUE
                    t0wRead1 := T0_24_SPAN_TO_RATE / (curSpan #> 1)
                tickMs[ringIdx] := nowMs
                ringIdx := (ringIdx + 1) +// T0_24_TICK_RING
                t0wRead2 := totalTicks
                t0wStatus := t0sSpinPhrase(t0wStatus, bShorted, bestSpan, curSpan)
            else
                bAtRest := (totalTicks > 0) and ((nowMs - lastAnyMs) >= T0_24_REST_QUIET_MS)
            waitms(T0_24_POLL_MS)
        if totalTicks > 0                                     ' at rest, or cut short by DONE / ABORT: logged either way
            bAnyInBand := bT0sEndTry(rowIdx, bShortRow, totalTicks, bestSpan, bestEndMs, bestTickIdx, lastAnyMs, bShorted, bAnyInBand, bAtRest)
    bKept := bT0sInBand[rowIdx]                               ' set only when a try was measured (bT0sEndTry())
    bT0sRowMeasured[rowIdx] := bKept and (t0wAbortReq == FALSE)
    if t0wAbortReq                                            ' if/else, never `? :` -- PL-29, PL-76
        t0wWhy := T0S_ST_NM_ABORTED
    elseif bKept
        t0wWhy := T0S_ST_MEASURED
        t0wRes1 := t0sBandTicks[rowIdx]
        t0wRes2 := t0sBandMs[rowIdx]
    elseif bShortRow and bAnyInBand
        t0wWhy := T0S_ST_NM_NO_ESTOP
    else
        t0wWhy := T0S_ST_NM_NO_SPIN

PRI bT0sEndTry(rowIdx, bShortRow, totalTicks, bestSpan, bestEndMs, bestTickIdx, lastAnyMs, bShorted, bAnyIn, bComplete) : bAnyInBand | releaseSpan, handTicks, afterTicks, afterMs, bandTicks, bandMs, bInBand, bLatched, bMeasured, pTry
' Close one try of a spin row (measure cog): compute its reading, buffer it for cog 0's log, keep it as
' the row's reading when it was measured, set the phrase he sees, and release a latched e-stop so the
' next spin starts free.
'
' @param rowIdx - the row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @param bShortRow - TRUE for the e-stop row
' @param totalTicks - the try's ticks
' @param bestSpan - the try's fastest six-interval span, -1 when it never had one
' @param bestEndMs - getms() at the end of that span: the release
' @param bestTickIdx - the tick count there
' @param lastAnyMs - getms() at the try's last tick
' @param bShorted - TRUE when the try applied the e-stop at the band entry
' @param bAnyIn - TRUE when an earlier try's release was above the band
' @param bComplete - TRUE when the wheel came to rest, FALSE when DONE / ABORT cut the try
' @returns bAnyInBand - TRUE when any try so far was released above the band
'
' The row's reading is kept in t0s*[rowIdx]; bT0sInBand[rowIdx] is TRUE exactly when one is kept.
'
' @local releaseSpan - the try's release span, ms; 0 when it never had one
' @local handTicks - ticks up to and including the release
' @local afterTicks - ticks after the release
' @local afterMs - ms from the release to the last tick
' @local bandTicks - ticks from T0_24_BAND_RATE to rest
' @local bandMs - ms those took
' @local bInBand - TRUE when the release was above the band
' @local bLatched - isEmergency() now
' @local bMeasured - TRUE when this try is a reading
' @local pTry - this try's record in t0wTries

    if bestSpan < 0
        releaseSpan := 0                                      ' too few ticks for one span: no release rate
        handTicks := totalTicks
        afterTicks := 0
        afterMs := 0
    else
        releaseSpan := bestSpan
        handTicks := bestTickIdx
        afterTicks := totalTicks - bestTickIdx
        afterMs := (lastAnyMs - bestEndMs) #> 0
    bandTicks, bandMs, bInBand := t0sBandResult(releaseSpan, bestTickIdx, bestEndMs, totalTicks, lastAnyMs)
    bLatched := motor.isEmergency()
    bMeasured := bComplete and (handTicks >= SF_HAND_MIN_TICKS) and bInBand
    if bShortRow
        bMeasured := bMeasured and bShorted and bLatched
    if t0wTryCount < T0_24_TRY_MAX
        pTry := @t0wTries[t0wTryCount * T0_24_TRY_LONGS]
        long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_HAND] := handTicks
        long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_SPAN] := releaseSpan
        long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_AFTER] := afterTicks
        long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_AFTER_MS] := afterMs
        long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_BAND] := bandTicks
        long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_BAND_MS] := bandMs
        long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_IN_BAND] := bInBand & 1
        long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_ENTERED] := bT0sBandEntered & 1
        long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_SHORTED] := bShorted & 1
        long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_LATCHED] := bLatched & 1
        if bComplete == FALSE
            long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_MEASURED] := T0_24_TRY_CUT
        else
            long[pTry][T0_24_TRY_MEASURED] := bMeasured & 1
    t0wTryCount += 1                                          ' counted even past T0_24_TRY_MAX: the log says how many it kept
    bAnyInBand := bAnyIn or bInBand
    if bMeasured
        t0sHandTicks[rowIdx] := handTicks
        t0sAfterTicks[rowIdx] := afterTicks
        t0sAfterMs[rowIdx] := afterMs
        t0sBandTicks[rowIdx] := bandTicks
        t0sBandMs[rowIdx] := bandMs
        t0sReleaseSpan[rowIdx] := releaseSpan
        bT0sInBand[rowIdx] := TRUE
        t0wStatus := T0S_ST_STOP_GOT
    elseif bComplete
        if bT0sInBand[rowIdx]                                 ' an earlier try's reading stands; if/else, never `? :` (PL-29)
            t0wStatus := T0S_ST_STOP_KEPT
        elseif bInBand == FALSE
            t0wStatus := T0S_ST_STOP_SLOW
        else
            t0wStatus := T0S_ST_STOP_AGAIN
    t0wRead1 := 0
    if bShortRow and bLatched                                 ' the next spin must start free
        motor.clearEmergency()
        motor.holdAtStop(FALSE)
        motor.stopMotor()
        waitms(T0_24_REARM_MS)

PRI t0sSpinPhrase(priorIdx, bShorted, bestSpan, curSpan) : statusIdx
' What a spin row's live phrase says while the wheel turns. SLOWING is entered only once a span runs
' an eighth longer than the fastest, and left only for a new fastest, so tick-to-tick jitter while a
' hand is still accelerating the wheel does not flip the phrase (each flip is a redraw and a log line).
'
' @param priorIdx - the phrase shown now, T0S_ST_*
' @param bShorted - TRUE once the e-stop was applied this try
' @param bestSpan - the try's fastest six-interval span so far, -1 when none yet
' @param curSpan - the span ending at the tick just counted
' @returns statusIdx - T0S_ST_*

    if bShorted
        statusIdx := T0S_ST_ESTOP_ON
    elseif (bestSpan > 0) and (bestSpan < T0_24_BAND_SPAN_MS)
        if curSpan == bestSpan                                ' a new fastest: still speeding up, or at its peak
            statusIdx := T0S_ST_SPIN_FAST
        elseif (priorIdx == T0S_ST_SLOWING) or (curSpan > bestSpan + (bestSpan >> 3))
            statusIdx := T0S_ST_SLOWING
        else
            statusIdx := T0S_ST_SPIN_FAST
    else
        statusIdx := T0S_ST_SPIN_SLOW

PRI t0sHoldAct(rowIdx) | hallCode, priorHall, posAccum, startMs, elapsedMs, eState, disp, duty, ceilDuty, drvState, senseI, bDisplaced, dispFirstMs, ceilFirstMs, ceilSenseI, slipFirstMs, limitFirstMs, faultFirstMs, maxDisp, startHs, startDisp, bStartHeld, bMeasured, bPass, bFaultedFirst, bAborted, eventMs, pSample, startDuty, priorMs, priorDuty, bPriorRising, riseSpanMs, riseGain, riseMs
' The three hold-mechanism rows' ACT (task 3608, DRIVER_REV 8; measure cog): watch the driver's own
' hold state change under a hand, sample it every 10 ms (pos, holdDisp, hold duty, drv_state,
' sense_i) into the t0wHold ring for cog 0 to print after the step, and judge each row from those
' transitions, never from how hard or how long he pushed. There is no watch bound (task 3619): the
' row runs until he clicks DONE or ABORT, and the live phrase (t0sHoldPhrase()) says when the program
' has seen what it needs.
'
' @param rowIdx - T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE, T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP or T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT
'
' @local hallCode - the 3-bit hall code just read
' @local priorHall - the previous poll's code
' @local posAccum - signed hall-tick position since this row began, t0hHallDeltas65's table (PL-39)
' @local startMs - getms() at the row's start
' @local elapsedMs - ms since the row began
' @local eState - this sample's getHoldStatus() state, HS_*
' @local disp - this sample's getHoldStatus() displacement, hall ticks
' @local duty - this sample's testGetHold() hold duty
' @local ceilDuty - this sample's testGetHold() ceiling duty
' @local drvState - this sample's getDriverState() reading, DCS_*
' @local senseI - this sample's testGetTelemetry() nSenseI
' @local bDisplaced - TRUE once he actually pushed the wheel off the hold position
' @local dispFirstMs - ms into the row at first displacement, -1 if never
' @local ceilFirstMs - ms into the row when duty first reached the ceiling, -1 if never
' @local ceilSenseI - sense_i at the moment the ceiling was first reached (sizes the ceiling in amps)
' @local slipFirstMs - ms into the row of the first HS_SLIPPED reading, -1 if never
' @local limitFirstMs - ms into the row of the first HS_LIMITED reading, -1 if never
' @local faultFirstMs - ms into the row of the first DCS_FAULTED reading, -1 if never
' @local maxDisp - the largest |displacement| seen, hall ticks
' @local startHs - getHoldStatus()'s state at the first sample, HS_* (PL-123 item 1)
' @local startDisp - its displacement then, hall ticks
' @local bStartHeld - TRUE when the row began on a fresh hold: HS_HOLDING at displacement 0
' @local bMeasured - TRUE when the row's cell is a measurement: a fresh hold, pushed, not aborted
' @local bPass - this row's pre-registered criterion
' @local bFaultedFirst - TRUE when the driver's own fault test beat the front cog's slip test
' @local bAborted - TRUE when ABORT ended the row
' @local eventMs - the row's own event (ceiling, slip or limit), ms into the row; -1 if never
' @local pSample - this sample's record in the t0wHold ring
' @local startDuty - the hold duty at the first sample: duty_min on a fresh hold
' @local priorMs - the previous sample's elapsedMs
' @local priorDuty - the previous sample's hold duty
' @local bPriorRising - TRUE when the previous sample was displaced and under the ceiling
' @local riseSpanMs - ms between sample pairs displaced and under the ceiling at both ends (PL-130)
' @local riseGain - the hold duty those pairs gained
' @local riseMs - the rise the rate implies, duty_min to the ceiling, ms; -1 if no pair was seen

    priorHall := t0sHallCode()
    posAccum := 0
    bDisplaced := FALSE
    dispFirstMs := -1
    ceilFirstMs := -1
    ceilSenseI := 0
    slipFirstMs := -1
    limitFirstMs := -1
    faultFirstMs := -1
    maxDisp := 0
    t0wHoldCount := 0
    bPriorRising := FALSE
    riseSpanMs := 0
    riseGain := 0
    startHs, startDisp := motor.getHoldStatus()                ' the state the row begins from, before any push
    startDuty, _, _, _, _ := motor.testGetHold()
    startMs := getms()
    repeat while (t0wStopReq == FALSE) and (t0wAbortReq == FALSE)
        hallCode := t0sHallCode()
        if hallCode <> priorHall
            posAccum += t0hHallDeltas65[(priorHall << 3) | hallCode] SIGNX 7
            priorHall := hallCode
        elapsedMs := getms() - startMs
        eState, disp := motor.getHoldStatus()
        duty, ceilDuty, _, _, _ := motor.testGetHold()
        drvState := motor.getDriverState()                      ' the latched state (DCS_FAULTED), not the raw drv_state
        _, _, senseI, _, _, _, _, _ := motor.testGetTelemetry()
        if disp <> 0
            if bDisplaced == FALSE
                bDisplaced := TRUE
                dispFirstMs := elapsedMs
            if (ceilFirstMs < 0) and (duty >= ceilDuty)
                ceilFirstMs := elapsedMs
                ceilSenseI := senseI
        if (slipFirstMs < 0) and (eState == motor.HS_SLIPPED)
            slipFirstMs := elapsedMs
        if (limitFirstMs < 0) and (eState == motor.HS_LIMITED)
            limitFirstMs := elapsedMs
        if (faultFirstMs < 0) and (drvState == motor.DCS_FAULTED)
            faultFirstMs := elapsedMs
        maxDisp := maxDisp #> abs(disp)
        if bPriorRising and (disp <> 0) and (duty < ceilDuty) and (eState == motor.HS_HOLDING) ' PL-130: rising at both ends
            riseSpanMs += elapsedMs - priorMs
            riseGain += duty - priorDuty
        bPriorRising := (disp <> 0) and (duty < ceilDuty) and (eState == motor.HS_HOLDING)  ' a slipped hold stops rising (PL-134)
        priorMs := elapsedMs
        priorDuty := duty
        pSample := @t0wHold[(t0wHoldCount +// T0_24_HOLD_RING) * T0_24_HOLD_LONGS]
        long[pSample][T0_24_HS_MS] := elapsedMs
        long[pSample][T0_24_HS_POS] := posAccum
        long[pSample][T0_24_HS_DISP] := disp
        long[pSample][T0_24_HS_DUTY] := duty
        long[pSample][T0_24_HS_DRV_STATE] := drvState
        long[pSample][T0_24_HS_SENSE_I] := senseI
        t0wHoldCount += 1
        if ceilDuty > 0
            t0wRead1 := (duty * 100) / ceilDuty
        else
            t0wRead1 := 0
        t0wRead2 := abs(disp)
        t0wStatus := t0sHoldPhrase(rowIdx, bDisplaced, ceilFirstMs, slipFirstMs, limitFirstMs, faultFirstMs)
        waitms(T0_24_HOLD_LOG_MS)
    bAborted := t0wAbortReq
    if bAborted
        motor.stopMotor()

    ' PL-123 item 1: a row whose first sample is not a fresh hold (HS_HOLDING at displacement 0) is
    ' judged from whatever the last row left, so its cell is NOMEAS whatever it reads
    bStartHeld := (startHs == motor.HS_HOLDING) and (startDisp == 0)
    bMeasured := bDisplaced and bStartHeld and (bAborted == FALSE)
    bFaultedFirst := bDisplaced and (faultFirstMs >= 0) and ((slipFirstMs < 0) or (faultFirstMs <= slipFirstMs))
    riseMs := -1
    if riseGain > 0                                             ' if/else, never `? :` -- PL-29, PL-76
        riseMs := muldiv64(ceilDuty - startDuty, riseSpanMs, riseGain)
    case rowIdx
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE:
            ' PL-130: the rise's rate, and the hold still holding when it reached the ceiling; what a push past the
            '  ceiling does afterwards (a slip, the time limit) is rows 2 and 3's, not this one's
            bPass := bDisplaced and (ceilFirstMs >= 0) and (riseMs >= T0_24_HOLD_RISE_LO_MS) and (riseMs <= T0_24_HOLD_RISE_HI_MS)
            bPass &= ((slipFirstMs < 0) or (slipFirstMs >= ceilFirstMs)) and ((limitFirstMs < 0) or (limitFirstMs >= ceilFirstMs))
            bPass &= (faultFirstMs < 0) or (faultFirstMs >= ceilFirstMs)
            bT0sHoldRiseMeasured := bMeasured
            bT0sHoldRisePass := bPass
            eventMs := ceilFirstMs
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP:
            bPass := bDisplaced and (slipFirstMs >= 0) and (bFaultedFirst == FALSE)
            bT0sHoldSlipMeasured := bMeasured
            bT0sHoldSlipPass := bPass
            eventMs := slipFirstMs
        other:
            bPass := bDisplaced and (limitFirstMs >= 0)
            bT0sHoldLimitMeasured := bMeasured
            bT0sHoldLimitPass := bPass
            eventMs := limitFirstMs
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_DISPLACED] := bDisplaced
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_DISP_MS] := dispFirstMs
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_CEIL_MS] := ceilFirstMs
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_CEIL_I] := ceilSenseI
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_SLIP_MS] := slipFirstMs
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_LIMIT_MS] := limitFirstMs
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_FAULT_MS] := faultFirstMs
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_FLT_FIRST] := bFaultedFirst
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_ABORTED] := bAborted
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_PASS] := bPass
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_START_HS] := startHs
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_START_DISP] := startDisp
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_START_HELD] := bStartHeld
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_MAX_DISP] := maxDisp
    t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_RISE_MS] := riseMs
    if bAborted                                                 ' if/else, never `? :` -- PL-29, PL-76
        t0wWhy := T0S_ST_NM_ABORTED
    elseif bStartHeld == FALSE
        t0wWhy := T0S_ST_NM_NOT_FRESH
    elseif bDisplaced == FALSE
        t0wWhy := T0S_ST_NM_NO_PUSH
    else
        t0wWhy := T0S_ST_MEASURED
    if rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE
        t0wRes1 := riseMs                                       ' PL-130: the rise its rate implies, ms displaced
    elseif bDisplaced and (eventMs >= 0)
        t0wRes1 := eventMs - dispFirstMs                        ' from his first push to the row's own event
    t0wRes2 := maxDisp

PRI t0sHoldPhrase(rowIdx, bDisplaced, ceilMs, slipMs, limitMs, faultMs) : statusIdx
' What a hold row's live phrase says. The first of slip, limit and fault ends what the row can show,
' so it wins; each row says GOT IT for its own event and NOT EXPECTED for another's.
'
' @param rowIdx - T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE, T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP or T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT
' @param bDisplaced - TRUE once he pushed the wheel off the hold position
' @param ceilMs - ms of the first ceiling reading, -1 if never
' @param slipMs - ms of the first HS_SLIPPED, -1 if never
' @param limitMs - ms of the first HS_LIMITED, -1 if never
' @param faultMs - ms of the first DCS_FAULTED, -1 if never
' @returns statusIdx - T0S_ST_*

    if (faultMs >= 0) and ((slipMs < 0) or (faultMs <= slipMs)) and ((limitMs < 0) or (faultMs <= limitMs))
        statusIdx := T0S_ST_HOLD_FAULT
    elseif (slipMs >= 0) and ((limitMs < 0) or (slipMs <= limitMs))
        if rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP
            statusIdx := T0S_ST_SLIP_GOT
        else
            statusIdx := T0S_ST_SLIP_BAD
    elseif limitMs >= 0
        if rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT
            statusIdx := T0S_ST_LIMIT_GOT
        else
            statusIdx := T0S_ST_LIMIT_BAD
    elseif ceilMs >= 0
        case rowIdx
            T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE:  statusIdx := T0S_ST_CEIL_GOT
            T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT: statusIdx := T0S_ST_CEIL_KEEP
            other:               statusIdx := T0S_ST_PUSH_SEEN
    elseif bDisplaced
        if rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP
            statusIdx := T0S_ST_PUSH_SEEN
        else
            statusIdx := T0S_ST_PUSH_RISING
    else
        statusIdx := T0S_ST_WAIT_PUSH

PRI t0sHallCode() : hallCode
' The three hall inputs as one 3-bit code. They are plain inputs -- nothing ever raises their DIR
' (task 3524) -- not smart pins, so pinread() is safe whether or not a driver cog is running.
'
' @returns hallCode - the 3-bit hall code

    hallCode := pinread((T0_MOTOR_BASE + T0_12_HALL_OFFSET) addpins T0_12_HALL_SPAN)

PRI t0sRowPrediction(rowIdx) : pText
' STOP-STATE-DESIGN.md SS5's prediction for a stop-path row, or DRIVER_REV 8's hold design for a
' hold-mechanism row, printed beside the row's own reading so the log carries what was expected
' before anyone reads what happened.
'
' @param rowIdx - which row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @returns pText - pointer to the prediction text

    case rowIdx
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE:  pText := @"WHILE_DISPLACED_THE_DUTY_RISES_TO_THE_CEILING_IN_ABOUT_250_MS"
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP:  pText := @"HS_SLIPPED_WITHIN_2_TICKS_THEN_A_SPEED_DEPENDENT_DRAG_NO_HOLD"
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT: pText := @"HS_LIMITED_AFTER_ABOUT_2_S_AT_THE_CEILING"
        T0_24_ROW_COAST:     pText := @"SPINS_FREELY_AND_COASTS"
        T0_24_ROW_ESTOP:     pText := @"THE_PROGRAM_SHORTS_IT_AS_IT_SLOWS_AND_IT_STOPS_ABRUPTLY"
        T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST:  pText := @"THE_FORCED_FAULT_LETS_IT_COAST_TO_A_STOP"
        T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD:   pText := @"THE_FORCED_FAULT_SHORTS_IT_AND_IT_STOPS_ALMOST_AT_ONCE"
        other:               pText := @"SPINS_FREELY_THE_PINS_ARE_RELEASED"

PRI t0sRowAction(rowIdx) : pText
' What the operator is asked to do in this row, named in the log BEFORE the row runs and shown on
' the panel at the same moment (overlay P1: an observation nothing asked for is never requested
' afterwards).
'
' @param rowIdx - which row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @returns pText - pointer to the action text

    case rowIdx
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE:  pText := @"PUSH_IT_BY_HAND_AND_HOLD_IT_DISPLACED_THEN_CLICK_DONE"
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP:  pText := @"PUSH_IT_PAST_THE_LOW_CEILING_THEN_CLICK_DONE"
        T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT: pText := @"PUSH_IT_TO_THE_CEILING_AND_HOLD_STEADILY_FOR_ABOUT_2_S"
        T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST, T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD:
                             pText := @"HANDS_OFF_IT_DRIVES_ITSELF_AND_IS_FAULTED_ON_PURPOSE_ABORT_STOPS_IT"
        other:               pText := @"SPIN_IT_HARD_AND_LET_GO_IT_MUST_PASS_THE_MEASURING_SPEED"

PRI t0sEmitCells() | coastGap, fltGap
' Every cell this tier judges, emitted once, after the last row. FREEREF is emitted FIRST
' (register INS-14): it is the instrument's own proof that it can report a coast at all, so it is
' read before any other cell is trusted. Three others compare two rows with each other and so
' cannot be judged where either row runs.
'
' Every stop cell judges band_ticks (task 3617, PL-123 item 2) against the limits derived in
' CON { T0-24 sign-off limits }: a coast carries SF_COAST_MIN_TICKS or more from T0_24_BAND_RATE,
' a brake SF_BRAKE_MAX_TICKS or fewer. A row released below the band is NOMEAS, never judged.
' FREEREF can FAIL: a wheel that stops like a brake reads at most SF_BRAKE_MAX_TICKS, under its limit.
'
' @local coastGap - COAST's band_ticks less ESTOP's
' @local fltGap - FLTCOAST's band_ticks less FLTHOLD's

    t0sEmitNum(@sCellFreeRef, @sCritFreeRef, t0sBandTicks[T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP], SF_COAST_MIN_TICKS, SF_BAND_TICKS_HI, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP], t0sBandTicks[T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP] >= SF_COAST_MIN_TICKS)
    emitCellBool(@sCellHoldRise, @sTaskHoldRows, @"RIGHT", @sCritHoldRise, bT0sHoldRiseMeasured, bT0sHoldRisePass, 1)
    emitCellBool(@sCellHoldSlip, @sTaskHoldRows, @"RIGHT", @sCritHoldSlip, bT0sHoldSlipMeasured, bT0sHoldSlipPass, 1)
    emitCellBool(@sCellHoldLimit, @sTaskHoldRows, @"RIGHT", @sCritHoldLimit, bT0sHoldLimitMeasured, bT0sHoldLimitPass, 1)
    t0sEmitNum(@sCellRestCoast, @sCritRestCoast, t0sBandTicks[T0_24_ROW_COAST], SF_COAST_MIN_TICKS, SF_BAND_TICKS_HI, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_COAST], t0sBandTicks[T0_24_ROW_COAST] >= SF_COAST_MIN_TICKS)
    t0sEmitNum(@sCellRestShort, @sCritRestShort, t0sBandTicks[T0_24_ROW_ESTOP], 0, SF_BRAKE_MAX_TICKS, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_ESTOP], t0sBandTicks[T0_24_ROW_ESTOP] <= SF_BRAKE_MAX_TICKS)
    coastGap := t0sBandTicks[T0_24_ROW_COAST] - t0sBandTicks[T0_24_ROW_ESTOP]
    t0sEmitNum(@sCellStopGap, @sCritStopGap, coastGap, SF_MODE_GAP_TICKS, SF_BAND_TICKS_HI, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_COAST] and bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_ESTOP], coastGap >= SF_MODE_GAP_TICKS)
    emitCellBool(@sCellFltCoast, @sTaskStopMode, @"RIGHT", @sCritFltCoast, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST], (t0sBandTicks[T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST] >= SF_COAST_MIN_TICKS) and bT0sStillFaulted[T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST], 1)
    emitCellBool(@sCellFltShort, @sTaskStopMode, @"RIGHT", @sCritFltShort, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD], (t0sBandTicks[T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD] <= SF_BRAKE_MAX_TICKS) and bT0sStillFaulted[T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD], 1)
    fltGap := t0sBandTicks[T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST] - t0sBandTicks[T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD]
    t0sEmitNum(@sCellFltGap, @sCritFltGap, fltGap, SF_MODE_GAP_TICKS, SF_BAND_TICKS_HI, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST] and bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD], fltGap >= SF_MODE_GAP_TICKS)
    t0sEmitEvHold()

PRI t0sEmitEvHold() | rowIdx, nJudged, bPos1, bPos2, bNeg, bPass, bRowOk
' R20-T0-EV-HOLD (task 3621, DRIVER-REPORTING-DESIGN.md SS6): the hold's hand-offs to the phase short are logged as
' events. Two sources of one fact are compared per hold row's last run whose own cell was a measurement: the event log
' cog 0 read after the ACT (t0sEvRead()), and the hold states the measure cog saw during it. A row passes when it holds
' one EV_HOLD_SLIP, of |value| at least HOLD_SLIP_TICKS, exactly when HS_SLIPPED was seen, and one EV_HOLD_LIMIT exactly
' when HS_LIMITED was seen, with nothing lost. Measured only when the positives arose -- HOLDSLIP slipped and HOLDLIMIT
' limited -- AND a measured row did not slip, which is the negative: a hold that did not hand off must log none (SS6:
' "the hold row that must not slip: none"). An event logged for a hand-off that did not happen fails, as does one
' missing.
'
' @local rowIdx - T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE .. T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT
' @local nJudged - hold rows judged
' @local bPos1 - HOLDSLIP was measured and slipped
' @local bPos2 - HOLDLIMIT was measured and limited
' @local bNeg - a measured hold row did not slip
' @local bPass - every judged row matched
' @local bRowOk - this row matched

    nJudged := 0
    bPass := TRUE
    bNeg := FALSE
    repeat rowIdx from T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE to T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT
        if bT0sEvRan[rowIdx] and bT0sEvMeasured[rowIdx]
            nJudged += 1
            bRowOk := bT0sEvClean[rowIdx]
            if bT0sEvSlipSeen[rowIdx]
                bRowOk &= (t0sEvSlips[rowIdx] == 1) and (t0sEvSlipMin[rowIdx] >= motor.HOLD_SLIP_TICKS)
            else
                bRowOk &= (t0sEvSlips[rowIdx] == 0)
                bNeg := TRUE
            if bT0sEvLimitSeen[rowIdx]
                bRowOk &= (t0sEvLimits[rowIdx] == 1)
            else
                bRowOk &= (t0sEvLimits[rowIdx] == 0)
            bPass &= bRowOk
    bPos1 := bT0sEvRan[T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP] and bT0sEvMeasured[T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP] and bT0sEvSlipSeen[T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP]
    bPos2 := bT0sEvRan[T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT] and bT0sEvMeasured[T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT] and bT0sEvLimitSeen[T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT]
    emitCellBool(@sCellEvHold, @sTaskReporting, @"RIGHT", @sCritEvHold, bPos1 and bPos2 and bNeg, bPass, nJudged)

PRI bT0sHoldRow(rowIdx) : bHold
' Whether a row is one of the three hold rows (task 3608), whose ACT the event log is read around (task 3621).
'
' @param rowIdx - T0_24_ROW_*
' @returns bHold - TRUE for HOLDRISE, HOLDSLIP and HOLDLIMIT

    bHold := (rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE) or (rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP) or (rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_HOLDLIMIT)

PRI t0sEvRead(rowIdx, seqNum, runNum, bKeep) | eKind, nValue, nSlips, nSlipMin, nLimits, nOther, bLost, bEnded
' Read cog 0's event log to EV_NONE (task 3621, R20-T0-EV-HOLD; at most T0_24_EV_READ_MAX reads). Before a hold row's
' ACT the read only discards what SETUP's re-arm left. After it, the hand-offs it held are kept for the row beside the
' hold states the measure cog saw in that same ACT (t0wHoldRes, still this run's) and printed as
' T0-24,row,N,run,K,events. The measure cog is idle between jobs, and only cog 0 reads the log.
'
' @param rowIdx - the hold row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @param seqNum - this run's 1-based row position
' @param runNum - the row's run, 1-based
' @param bKeep - TRUE after the ACT: keep and print; FALSE before it: discard
'
' @local eKind - a read's kind
' @local nValue - its value
' @local nSlips - EV_HOLD_SLIP events read
' @local nSlipMin - the least |value| among them, hall ticks; 0 when none
' @local nLimits - EV_HOLD_LIMIT events read
' @local nOther - events of any other kind read
' @local bLost - the read was told it lost events
' @local bEnded - the read ended on EV_NONE inside the bound

    nSlips := 0
    nSlipMin := POSX
    nLimits := 0
    nOther := 0
    bLost := FALSE
    bEnded := FALSE
    repeat T0_24_EV_READ_MAX
        eKind, _, nValue := motor.getEvent()
        if eKind == motor.EV_NONE
            bEnded := TRUE
            quit
        if eKind == motor.EV_LOST
            bLost := TRUE
        elseif eKind == motor.EV_HOLD_SLIP
            nSlips += 1
            nSlipMin <#= abs(nValue)
        elseif eKind == motor.EV_HOLD_LIMIT
            nLimits += 1
        else
            nOther += 1
    if nSlips == 0
        nSlipMin := 0
    if bKeep
        bT0sEvRan[rowIdx] := TRUE
        t0sEvSlips[rowIdx] := nSlips
        t0sEvSlipMin[rowIdx] := nSlipMin
        t0sEvLimits[rowIdx] := nLimits
        bT0sEvClean[rowIdx] := bEnded and (bLost == FALSE)
        bT0sEvSlipSeen[rowIdx] := (t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_SLIP_MS] >= 0)
        bT0sEvLimitSeen[rowIdx] := (t0wHoldRes[T0_24_HR_LIMIT_MS] >= 0)
        case rowIdx                                             ' the row's own cell's measured flag, this run's
            T0_24_ROW_HOLDRISE:
                bT0sEvMeasured[rowIdx] := bT0sHoldRiseMeasured
            T0_24_ROW_HOLDSLIP:
                bT0sEvMeasured[rowIdx] := bT0sHoldSlipMeasured
            other:
                bT0sEvMeasured[rowIdx] := bT0sHoldLimitMeasured
        debug("T0-24,row,", udec_(seqNum), ",run,", udec_(runNum), ",events,slip,", udec_(nSlips), ",slip_min,", udec_(nSlipMin), ",limit,", udec_(nLimits), ",other,", udec_(nOther), ",lost,", zstr_(bLost ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",ended,", zstr_(bEnded ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",hs_slip,", zstr_(bT0sEvSlipSeen[rowIdx] ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",hs_limit,", zstr_(bT0sEvLimitSeen[rowIdx] ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

PRI t0sEmitNum(pCell, pCrit, measuredTicks, loTicks, hiTicks, bMeasured, bPass)
' One numeric SIGNOFF for a T0-24 cell, in hall ticks (task 3617: band_ticks), through the shared
' emitCellNum() -- one record format for every numeric cell in this file, from hub strings (DBG-2).
'
' @param pCell - pointer to the cell id
' @param pCrit - pointer to the criterion token
' @param measuredTicks - the reading
' @param loTicks - the criterion's low limit
' @param hiTicks - its high limit
' @param bMeasured - TRUE when the row was set up AND its release was above the band
' @param bPass - the criterion held

    emitCellNum(pCell, @sTaskStopMode, @"RIGHT", pCrit, bMeasured, measuredTicks, loTicks, hiTicks, @"TICKS", bMeasured ? 1 : 0, bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL")

PRI t0sSetupPanel()
' Create the T0-24 panel window and load its eight layers -- crop-and-overlay technique,
' DOCs/REF-NO-COMMIT/dbg-display-theory/DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS2 and SS6 step 4, as
' T0-12's own panel draws it on this rig. Geometry and ids are the T0S_* CON block and t0sScreenTab,
' both printed by `python3 tools/gen_t0stop_assets.py`, which also writes the t0s_*.bmp assets
' committed beside this file.
'
' CARTESIAN 1 is declared right after the window opens (PLOT-DISPLAY-RULES.md rule 7) so
' PC_MOUSE reports y DOWN from the top-left, the basis every CROP destination here uses and
' t0sReadInput() hit-tests in -- test_bench_dual.spin2 panelSetup()'s own form.
'
' THE TITLE NAMES THE WHEEL (task 3617, PL-123 item 4), as does the header art. It is single-quoted,
' and has no apostrophe and NO PARENTHESIS (PLOT-DISPLAY-RULES.md rule 6). A ')' in the text closes the
' debug() call: at SRC_REV 13-14 the title read '... RIGHT WHEEL (P16 BOARD)', the rest of the line
' (SIZE 560 470 POS 60 60 HIDEXY UPDATE) became a comment, it compiled clean, and the window opened at
' the host's default size showing a quarter of the panel (debug_260924-162831.log:23, PL-128).

    debug(`PLOT t0stop TITLE 'T0-24 stop-state hand test -- RIGHT WHEEL, P16 BOARD' SIZE 560 470 POS 60 60 HIDEXY UPDATE)
    debug(`t0stop cartesian 1)
    debug(`t0stop LAYER 1 't0s_bg.bmp')
    debug(`t0stop LAYER 2 't0s_names.bmp')
    debug(`t0stop LAYER 3 't0s_banners.bmp')
    debug(`t0stop LAYER 4 't0s_cards.bmp')
    debug(`t0stop LAYER 5 't0s_digits.bmp')
    debug(`t0stop LAYER 6 't0s_status.bmp')
    debug(`t0stop LAYER 7 't0s_labels.bmp')
    debug(`t0stop LAYER 8 't0s_buttons.bmp')
    debug(`t0stop crop 1)
    debug(`t0stop update)

PRI t0sDrawRow(pScreen, rowIdx, seqNum, statusIdx, r1, r2, litBtn, bFull)
' Draw one row's screen from its t0sScreenTab entry: the banner, card, reading labels and buttons the
' generator chose for this (row, phase), with this phrase and these readings.
'
' @param pScreen - the t0sScreenTab entry (t0sScreenPtr())
' @param rowIdx - the row, T0_24_ROW_*: its name cell
' @param seqNum - this run's 1-based row position
' @param statusIdx - the phrase under SEEN NOW, T0S_ST_*
' @param r1 - the readings, -1 for none
' @param r2
' @param litBtn - the button to draw lit (clicked), T0S_BT_NONE for none
' @param bFull - TRUE for a screen's first frame or a lit button; FALSE redraws only the phrase and readings

    t0sDraw(rowIdx, seqNum, byte[pScreen][T0S_SCR_BANNER], byte[pScreen][T0S_SCR_CARD], statusIdx, byte[pScreen][T0S_SCR_LBL1], byte[pScreen][T0S_SCR_LBL2], r1, r2, byte[pScreen][T0S_SCR_BTN_L], byte[pScreen][T0S_SCR_BTN_R], litBtn, bFull)

PRI t0sDrawSpecial(nameIdx, bannerIdx, cardIdx, statusIdx)
' Draw a whole-test screen (all rows done, or the driver not ready): no row number, no readings,
' no buttons.
'
' @param nameIdx - the row-name cell, T0S_NAME_*
' @param bannerIdx - T0S_B_*
' @param cardIdx - T0S_CARD_*
' @param statusIdx - T0S_ST_*

    t0sDraw(nameIdx, 0, bannerIdx, cardIdx, statusIdx, T0S_L_BLANK, T0S_L_BLANK, -1, -1, T0S_BT_NONE, T0S_BT_NONE, T0S_BT_NONE, TRUE)

PRI t0sDraw(nameIdx, seqNum, bannerIdx, cardIdx, statusIdx, lbl1, lbl2, r1, r2, btnL, btnR, litBtn, bFull) | digitIdx
' Compose one frame, then one UPDATE (DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS2, "batch all crops,
' then one update"). Runs on cog 0 only, which never measures. Within one screen only the phrase and
' the reading digits change, so a partial frame (bFull FALSE) sends just those: about half the bytes of
' a full one over the 2 Mbaud link. The buttons are sent in a partial frame only when litBtn is set.
'
' @param nameIdx - the row-name cell (layer 2)
' @param seqNum - the row number to show, 0 to blank it
' @param bannerIdx - the phase banner (layer 3)
' @param cardIdx - the text card (layer 4)
' @param statusIdx - the phrase under SEEN NOW (layer 6)
' @param lbl1 - the two reading labels (layer 7)
' @param lbl2
' @param r1 - the two readings, -1 for none (layer 5)
' @param r2
' @param btnL - the left and right buttons, T0S_BT_NONE for an empty slot (layer 8)
' @param btnR
' @param litBtn - the button drawn lit, T0S_BT_NONE for none
' @param bFull - TRUE sends every element; FALSE only the phrase and the reading digits
'
' @local digitIdx - the row-number digit cell

    if bFull
        if seqNum > 0                                           ' if/else, never `? :` -- PL-29, PL-76
            digitIdx := seqNum
        else
            digitIdx := T0S_DGT_BLANK
        debug(`t0stop crop 5 `(digitIdx * T0S_DGT_W, 0, T0S_DGT_W, T0S_DGT_H, T0S_RNUM_X, T0S_ROW_LINE_Y))
        debug(`t0stop crop 2 `(0, nameIdx * T0S_NAME_H, T0S_NAME_W, T0S_NAME_H, T0S_NAME_X, T0S_ROW_LINE_Y))
        debug(`t0stop crop 3 `(0, bannerIdx * T0S_BAN_H, T0S_BAN_W, T0S_BAN_H, T0S_BAN_X, T0S_BAN_Y))
        debug(`t0stop crop 4 `(0, cardIdx * T0S_CARD_H, T0S_CARD_W, T0S_CARD_H, T0S_CARD_X, T0S_CARD_Y))
        debug(`t0stop crop 7 `(0, lbl1 * T0S_LBL_H, T0S_LBL_W, T0S_LBL_H, T0S_LBL_X, T0S_READ1_Y))
        debug(`t0stop crop 7 `(0, lbl2 * T0S_LBL_H, T0S_LBL_W, T0S_LBL_H, T0S_LBL_X, T0S_READ2_Y))
        t0sBlitButton(T0S_BTN_L_X, btnL, litBtn)
        t0sBlitButton(T0S_BTN_R_X, btnR, litBtn)
    debug(`t0stop crop 6 `(0, statusIdx * T0S_STAT_H, T0S_STAT_W, T0S_STAT_H, T0S_STAT_X, T0S_STAT_Y))
    t0sBlitReading(T0S_READ1_Y, r1)
    t0sBlitReading(T0S_READ2_Y, r2)
    debug(`t0stop update)

PRI t0sBlitReading(destY, numValue) | divisor, digitVal, colIdx
' Blit one reading's digits, most significant first, leading zeros suppressed. A negative value
' blanks every digit: there is no reading.
'
' @param destY - the reading's row on the canvas
' @param numValue - the value, 0..99_999 shown, -1 for none
'
' @local divisor - selects the digit column being extracted
' @local digitVal - that column's digit cell, or the blank cell
' @local colIdx - the digit column, most significant first

    numValue <#= 99_999
    divisor := 10_000                                           ' T0S_READ_COUNT (5) digits
    repeat colIdx from 0 to T0S_READ_COUNT - 1
        if (numValue >= 0) and ((divisor == 1) or (numValue >= divisor))
            digitVal := (numValue / divisor) +// 10
        else
            digitVal := T0S_DGT_BLANK
        debug(`t0stop crop 5 `(digitVal * T0S_DGT_W, 0, T0S_DGT_W, T0S_DGT_H, T0S_READ_X + (colIdx * T0S_READ_PITCH), destY))
        divisor /= 10

PRI t0sBlitButton(destX, btnIdx, litBtn) | colX
' Blit one button slot: the button's cell, lit when it was just clicked, or the bare panel for an
' empty slot (T0S_BT_NONE's cell), so a slot never shows a button that cannot be chosen.
'
' @param destX - the slot's left edge
' @param btnIdx - T0S_BT_*
' @param litBtn - the button drawn lit, T0S_BT_NONE for none
'
' @local colX - the cell's column in layer 8: 0 normal, T0S_BTN_W lit

    colX := 0
    if (btnIdx == litBtn) and (btnIdx <> T0S_BT_NONE)
        colX := T0S_BTN_W
    debug(`t0stop crop 8 `(colX, btnIdx * T0S_BTN_H, T0S_BTN_W, T0S_BTN_H, destX, T0S_BTN_Y))
#endif

